E["item:bag-of-empty-ooze-containers"] = {t="item",n="Bag of Empty Ooze Containers",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Laris Geardawdle supplies empty jars for his study of Azeroth’s oozes. He means them to hold clean slime gathered in the wild.",h="In Ironforge, Laris Geardawdle supplies empty jars for his study of Azeroth’s oozes.",sec={{t="Field Research Equipment",b="Laris Geardawdle studies the strange biology of Azeroth’s oozes. He found that they quickly take on the corruption around them, including Felwood’s tainted residues. So he commissioned sturdy jars that can hold acidic specimens without harming them. The bag carries enough jars to gather clean slime in wild regions, especially Un’Goro Crater, where ancient glutinous oozes live free of demonic taint.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Bag of Empty Ooze Containers?",a="The bag holds ten Empty Pure Sample Jars. Their glass can hold caustic ooze without damaging or contaminating a sample.",al={"what's in the bag","bag contents","ooze container contents"},it="item"},{q="Who provided these containers?",a="Laris Geardawdle, a gnome researcher in Ironforge’s Hall of Explorers, supplied the containers. He studies how slimes adapt to their surroundings.",al={"who gives the ooze bag","laris geardawdle bag","who gives bag of empty ooze containers"},it="origin"},{q="What kind of oozes are these jars meant to collect?",a="The jars are meant for pure, uncorrupted ooze. You can gather pristine slime from Un’Goro Crater’s glutinous oozes, unlike the blighted specimens in Felwood.",al={"what slime goes in the jars","pure sample jar target","where to fill jars"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Laris need pure ooze samples?",a="Laris needs pure ooze to study how oozes absorb qualities from their surroundings. He can compare an uncorrupted specimen with polluted slimes from blighted regions.",al={"why collect pure slime","geardawdle research goal","why pure oozes"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Bag of Empty Ooze Containers?",a="This sack is a kit of specialized field gear given to you by Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge. Inside are ten empty sample jars designed to hold and safely transport volatile slime specimens back to his workshop without leaking or contaminating the contents.",al={"bag of empty ooze containers","what are ooze containers","laris ooze bag"},it="identity",add="9a2213f5"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see the ingenuity in these durable, chemical-resistant jars. They let researchers carry dangerous, corrosive wildlife samples safely.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can help Laris Geardawdle with his ecological research in Ironforge. Bring him field samples from untamed places like Un’Goro Crater."},kw={"bag of empty ooze containers","empty pure sample jar","ironforge","laris geardawdle","ooze containers","pure sample jar","slime"},rel={"quest:4512","item:filled-pure-sample-jar","npc:laris-geardawdle","zone:ironforge","zone:ungoro","zone:felwood"},src={"Bag of Empty Ooze Containers","A Little Slime Goes a Long Way (2)"}}
E["item:crocolisk-skin-classic"] = {t="item",n="Crocolisk Skin (Classic)",z="ironforge",s="At Farstrider Lodge in Loch Modan, hunters brave the Loch’s crocolisks for hides sought by merchants and leatherworkers.",h="At Farstrider Lodge in Loch Modan, hunters brave the Loch’s crocolisks for hides sought by merchants and...",sec={{t="A Dangerous Trade",b="Crocolisks make dens along the islands and shores of the Loch’s cold waters. Their sharp teeth and thick scales make them dangerous quarry. Still, hunters based at Farstrider Lodge pursue them for their tough skins. Tailors and distant merchants seek the hides for sturdy garments and armor, so an undamaged skin brings a good price nearby.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do crocolisk skins come from?",a="Loch Crocolisks and Large Loch Crocolisks provide the skins. They live in Loch Modan’s waters and on its islands.",al={"where to get croc skins","loch croc skin source","who drops crocolisk skin"},it="origin"},{q="Who buys or trades these hides in Loch Modan?",a="Marek Ironheart, a dwarven hunter at Farstrider Lodge, gathers crocolisk skins and meat to sell to visiting merchants and craftsmen.",al={"who wants croc skins","farstrider lodge croc skins","marek ironheart skins"}},{q="Why are these skins in demand?",a="Merchants seek the tough, scaly hides for sturdy clothing and armor. Crocolisks are fierce and hard to kill, so good skins bring steady pay.",al={"what are croc skins used for","crocolisk leather use","why hunt crocs"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is hunting crocolisks in the Loch considered dangerous?",a="Yes. Loch crocolisks are aggressive, with powerful jaws and serrated teeth that can sever limbs. Local hunters such as Marek Ironheart trade tales of near-fatal encounters while trying to pin down their quarry.",al={"are loch crocs dangerous","crocolisk hunting danger"},it="danger"},{q="What is a Crocolisk Skin?",a="A Crocolisk Skin is the tough, scaled hide harvested from the crocolisks inhabiting the waters and islands of Loch Modan. Prized for its durability and distinctive texture, it serves as a valuable raw material for leatherworkers and tailors looking to craft sturdy clothing, protective gear, or specialized armor.",al={"what is crocolisk skin","crocolisk hide","what are croc skins"},it="identity",add="c6e655b9"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you earn Farstrider Lodge’s respect by wading to the islands and subduing a thrashing crocolisk for its hide.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Loch Modan’s crocolisks test the grit of mountaineers and lodge woodsmen."},kw={"crocolisk hunting","crocolisk skin","farstrider lodge","loch crocolisk","loch modan","marek ironheart","the loch"},rel={"quest:385","npc:marek-ironheart","subzone:farstrider-lodge","subzone:the-loch","zone:lochmodan","topic:hunter"},src={"Crocolisk Skin (Classic)","Crocolisk Hunting"}}
E["item:filled-cursed-ooze-jar"] = {t="item",n="Filled Cursed Ooze Jar",z="ironforge",s="In Felwood, a Filled Cursed Ooze Jar carries a sample for Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge. The gnome scholar seeks the ancient origins of slimes across Azeroth.",h="In Felwood, a Filled Cursed Ooze Jar carries a sample for Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Curious Specimen",b="Laris Geardawdle, a gnome researcher, sees mystery in the vile puddles and caustic slimes others pass by. Slimes thrive across Azeroth, and Forsaken apothecaries gather them with care. These sights led Geardawdle to a bold theory: oozes may be primordial secretions bound to Azeroth's creation. To gather a sample, brave Felwood's blighted woods and defeat a cursed ooze. Scoop its acidic remains into an empty jar before they dissolve.",sp=0},{t="Academic Ambition",b="Laris Geardawdle hopes his ooze samples will bring knowledge and a lasting name. A major discovery could secure his reputation in the dwarven-led Explorers' League. Since Gnomeregan fell, many gnome refugees in Ironforge have felt pressed to prove their worth to their dwarven hosts. Geardawdle believes that uncovering ooze's ancient secrets will show them that welcoming gnomes was no mistake.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this jar come from?",a="Use an Empty Cursed Ooze Jar on the remains of a defeated Cursed Ooze in Felwood's corrupted lands to fill it.",al={"where do i get cursed ooze jar","how to get filled cursed ooze jar","ooze jar location"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants these ooze samples?",a="Laris Geardawdle, a gnome researcher in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, wants the samples for his natural history research.",al={"who needs ooze jars","laris geardawdle quest","who turns in ooze jar"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Laris Geardawdle studying oozes?",a="Laris Geardawdle studies oozes because he sees nature and the Royal Apothecary Society taking an interest in them. He suspects slimes may be ancient secretions tied to life's creation and development on Azeroth, and needs samples to test his theory.",al={"why study slimes","geardawdle ooze theory","why ooze"},it="motive"},{q="Why does a gnome care about the Explorers' League?",a="After Gnomeregan fell, gnome refugees found shelter among the dwarves in Ironforge. Laris Geardawdle hopes a major discovery through the Explorers' League will prove sheltering them was the right choice.",al={"why explorers league","gnomes in ironforge"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Filled Cursed Ooze Jar?",a="It is a specially prepared specimen container packed with a fresh sample taken from a slain cursed ooze in Felwood. These foul, corrupted slimes thrive amidst the demonic decay of the tainted forest, making even small remnants volatile and dangerous to handle without proper glasswork.",al={"what is filled cursed ooze jar","filled cursed ooze jar purpose","cursed ooze jar"},it="identity",add="b5982a20"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see why Laris Geardawdle cares so deeply about slime research. He hopes to honor displaced gnomes and prove their intellectual worth to their dwarven hosts in Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see natural philosophers in Ironforge watching Forsaken movements. The Royal Apothecary Society has also shown a dark interest in gathering ooze samples across Azeroth."},kw={"cursed ooze","explorers' league","felwood","filled cursed ooze jar","ironforge","laris geardawdle","slime"},rel={"quest:4512","item:filled-tainted-ooze-jar","npc:laris-geardawdle","zone:felwood","zone:ironforge","topic:explorers-league","topic:royal-apothecary-society","item:package-of-empty-ooze-containers"},src={"Filled Cursed Ooze Jar","A Little Slime Goes a Long Way"}}
E["item:filled-pure-sample-jar"] = {t="item",n="Filled Pure Sample Jar",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Laris Geardawdle studies how corruption changes living matter. A Filled Pure Sample Jar holds primordial ooze from the remote wilds, giving him a clean specimen for comparison.",h="In Ironforge, Laris Geardawdle studies how corruption changes living matter.",sec={{t="A Search for Uncorrupted Slime",b="Laris Geardawdle studies oozes across Azeroth and how corruption changes living matter. He found that these shapeless creatures absorb the magic and conditions of their homes, then reflect them. After cataloging tainted slimes in Felwood, he sought a clean sample for comparison. A Filled Pure Sample Jar holds primordial ooze gathered from the wilds of Un'Goro Crater, away from corrupted strains.",sp=0},{t="Primordial Ecology",b="Oozes change readily, so Laris cannot find pure samples near civilization, demonic blights, or necromantic fallout. The glutinous oozes of Un'Goro Crater's untamed basin remain relatively isolated from outside corruption. That makes them a useful standard for scholars in Ironforge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants these pure samples?",a="Laris Geardawdle, a gnomish researcher in Ironforge, seeks pure samples to study Azeroth's ooze populations.",al={"laris geardawdle quest","who needs filled pure sample jar","who wants the jars"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Laris need pure ooze instead of tainted ooze?",a="Laris found that slimes quickly absorb properties of their surroundings, including Felwood's demonic rot. He needs uncorrupted samples to compare with tainted ooze and understand how far corruption reaches and how it works.",al={"why pure ooze","why pure sample","slime study purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where can pure ooze samples be collected?",a="Pure samples come from the glutinous oozes in Un'Goro Crater's primordial wilderness, where they remain isolated from outside blights.",al={"where do i find pure ooze","pure sample jar location","where to fill pure jars"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens once the samples are delivered to Ironforge?",a="Laris uses the samples to test how oozes adapt to and withstand their environment. He rewards adventurers who brave hazardous wilds to bring them to Ironforge.",al={"quest reward laris","what does laris do with them"},it="next_step"},{q="What is a Filled Pure Sample Jar?",a="It is an airtight glass container packed with an untainted ooze specimen. Unlike slimes corrupted by demonic energies or blight, the substance inside represents an unpolluted baseline of ooze life, preserved carefully for academic study.",al={"what is filled pure sample jar","pure sample jar meaning","filled pure sample jar"},it="identity",add="630b5cc1"},{q="Where does a Filled Pure Sample Jar come from?",a="The empty containers are crafted and provided by Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge. You fill them yourself in the field by harvesting viscous remnants from wild, uncorrupted oozes found flourishing in pristine natural environments like Un'Goro Crater.",al={"filled pure sample jar origin","where do pure samples come from","who made pure sample jar"},it="origin",add="e9b3a5fa"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can help scholars study living matter by comparing Felwood's tainted slimes with pure Un'Goro specimens.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance explorer, you can bring knowledge of remote places like Un'Goro Crater to scholars in Ironforge."},kw={"filled pure sample jar","glutinous ooze","ironforge","laris geardawdle","ooze","slime","un'goro crater"},rel={"npc:laris-geardawdle","quest:4512","zone:ironforge","zone:ungoro","zone:felwood","item:bag-of-empty-ooze-containers"},src={"Filled Pure Sample Jar","A Little Slime Goes a Long Way (2)"}}
E["item:filled-tainted-ooze-jar"] = {t="item",n="Filled Tainted Ooze Jar",z="ironforge",s="In Felwood, a Filled Tainted Ooze Jar carries samples of corruption to Ironforge. The samples may help explain how life began on Azeroth.",h="In Felwood, a Filled Tainted Ooze Jar carries samples of corruption to Ironforge.",sec={{t="Slime of the Corrupted Wood",b="Across northern Kalimdor, tainted oozes bear Felwood’s lingering corruption. Gnomish researchers provide jars to hold them safely. Most travelers keep clear of these noxious creatures, yet their remains yield samples for natural philosophy and biological study far from the blighted woods.",sp=0},{t="Geardawdle's Grand Theory",b="Laris Geardawdle, a gnome scholar with the Explorers' League in Ironforge, gathers the samples. The commonness of slimes fascinates him, and he has seen the Forsaken's Royal Apothecary Society take an interest in them too.\n\nMany scholars dismiss Geardawdle's theory. He believes slimes and oozes may be primal secretions tied to Azeroth's creation. He seeks proof, and a place among dwarven scholars after Gnomeregan's tragic fall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside a Filled Tainted Ooze Jar?",a="A Filled Tainted Ooze Jar holds a fresh sample from the remains of a Tainted Ooze native to Felwood, sealed in a gnomish collection jar.",al={"what is in the jar","tainted ooze jar contents","what is tainted ooze"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants these ooze samples?",a="Laris Geardawdle, a gnome researcher with the Explorers' League in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, wants the samples for his natural history studies.",al={"who takes the ooze","laris geardawdle quest","who wants tainted ooze"},it="motive"},{q="Why is Laris Geardawdle studying oozes?",a="Geardawdle saw the Royal Apothecary Society gathering slime samples and set out to understand their nature. He believes oozes are primordial secretions tied to Azeroth's creation, and hopes to earn a name as a scientist in Ironforge.",al={"why study slime","geardawdle slime theory","why does the gnome want ooze"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these samples collected?",a="You gather the samples in Felwood by defeating Tainted Oozes, then using an empty containment jar on their remains.",al={"where to find tainted ooze","tainted ooze jar location","where do i fill the jar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does a Filled Tainted Ooze Jar come from, and who made it?",a="The jar itself is provided by the gnome researcher Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge, who crafts specialized empty glass containers to safely collect volatile specimens. It becomes filled only after an adventurer slays a tainted ooze in the corrupted forests of Felwood and uses the jar to scrape up remnants of the creature's gelatinous remains.",al={"tainted ooze jar origin","who made tainted ooze jar","where do tainted ooze jars come from"},it="origin",add="297c9c04"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome refugee in Ironforge, your scientific work with the Explorers' League can prove your worth and repay dwarven hospitality after Gnomeregan's tragedy.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout, you watch the Forsaken's Royal Apothecary Society closely. Learning why the Undercity gathers slime across the continents is a key intelligence priority."},kw={"explorers' league","felwood","ironforge","laris geardawdle","royal apothecary society","slime","tainted ooze"},rel={"quest:4512","item:filled-cursed-ooze-jar","npc:laris-geardawdle","item:package-of-empty-ooze-containers","zone:felwood","zone:ironforge","topic:explorers-league","topic:royal-apothecary-society"},src={"Filled Tainted Ooze Jar","A Little Slime Goes a Long Way"}}
E["item:honorary-picks"] = {t="item",n="Honorary Picks",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Honorary Picks are bound for Brock Stoneseeker’s mining apprentices in Thelsamar. Gryphons carry the ceremonial tools to Loch Modan, where they mark students ready to work its ore veins.",h="In Ironforge, Honorary Picks are bound for Brock Stoneseeker’s mining apprentices in Thelsamar.",sec={{t="Tools for the Next Generation",b="Mining keeps the great forges burning and brings dwarves the iron and stone they need. In Thelsamar, Brock Stoneseeker teaches young apprentices to mine. Honorary Picks from Ironforge mark the students ready to work the open ore deposits across Loch Modan.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Gryphon Lines",b="The picks travel through the Alliance gryphon network, linking Ironforge with its outlying settlements. At Ironforge’s Great Forge, Gryth Thurden receives the shipment. He sends it over the mountains to Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Honorary Picks used for?",a="Brock Stoneseeker’s mining students in Loch Modan receive the Honorary Picks. The ceremonial tools are ready for apprentices to use on ore veins across the region.",al={"what are honorary picks","use of honorary picks","honorary picks purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the picks, and who receives them?",a="The picks are prepared in Ironforge and brought to Gryth Thurden at the city’s gryphon roost. From there, they fly east to Thelsamar, where mining instructor Brock Stoneseeker receives them.",al={"who gets honorary picks","honorary picks delivery","honorary picks recipient"},it="people"},{q="Why do the picks need to be delivered by gryphon?",a="Gryphons carry the picks quickly between Ironforge and Loch Modan, along the Alliance’s established flight paths. The route also teaches travelers to use those paths. The picks could also be carried on foot through the North Gate Pass.",al={"why fly picks","why take gryphon","honorary picks flight"}},{q="Are the Honorary Picks actual weapons or tools you can equip?",a="No. The courier carries the picks as cargo for Brock Stoneseeker’s mining students. They are eager to use them on Loch Modan’s ore deposits.",al={"can i equip honorary picks","are honorary picks an item","honorary picks usable"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What are the Honorary Picks?",a="The Honorary Picks are a bundle of ceremonial or commemorative mining tools crafted in Ironforge. They are designated as a special presentation for novitiate miners learning the craft under the guidance of seasoned prospectors in the hills of Loch Modan.",al={"what are honorary picks","honorary picks item","honorary picks lore"},it="identity",add="a7b14bb4"},{q="Where do the Honorary Picks come from, and who made them?",a="The picks are procured in the dwarven capital of Ironforge. Crafted by skilled mountain smiths in the city's Great Forge, they are packaged together specifically for transport out to instructors training apprentices beyond Dun Morogh's borders.",al={"who made honorary picks","honorary picks origin","where did the picks come from"},it="origin",add="0ecadd79"},{q="Why does anyone want the Honorary Picks?",a="Mining instructor Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar requested the picks to present to his novice students. As aspiring prospectors working in Loch Modan, the students eagerly await these honors and tools to begin working the rich mineral veins of the region.",al={"why deliver honorary picks","who wants the honorary picks","why does brock want the picks"},it="why_wanted",add="1a632b74"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know the worth of a solid pick. An honorary tool marks a novice’s passage into the profession.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the kinship and craft in presenting tools forged in Ironforge to apprentices working in the provinces."},kw={"brock stoneseeker","gryth thurden","honorary picks","ironforge","loch modan","mining picks","thelsamar","thorgrum borrelson"},rel={"npc:brock-stoneseeker","subzone:thelsamar","zone:ironforge","zone:lochmodan","quest:6388","quest:6392","npc:thorgrum-borrelson"},src={"Honorary Picks","Gryth Thurden (Classic)","Return to Brock"}}
E["item:moldy-tome"] = {t="item",n="Moldy Tome",z="ironforge",s="Along the Hillsbrad coast, the Moldy Tome lies ruined after a shipwreck. Once part of the Tome of the Cabal, it still draws warlocks seeking its lore on demonic summoning.",h="Along the Hillsbrad coast, the Moldy Tome lies ruined after a shipwreck.",sec={{t="Lost to the Waves",b="The Tome of the Cabal was a rare work of dark arts held in Lordaeron. Someone vandalized it and tore it in two. One half, now called the Moldy Tome, sailed south toward Menethil Harbor and Ironforge. The ship never arrived. It sank in the dangerous waters west of Southshore, and the half that survived washed ashore south of Azurelode Mine. Damp and surf ruined its pages as murlocs scavenged along the Hillsbrad coast.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Dark Work",b="Though its vellum is mildewed and rotting, the Moldy Tome still holds powerful lore about demons. Warlocks seeking it brave the coastal camps. Krom Stoutarm guides some of them in Ironforge, while Jorah Annison guides others in the Undercity. Joined with its counterpart, the Tattered Manuscript from the caves of Thousand Needles, the restored book gives the precise words needed to summon and bind a felhunter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Moldy Tome?",a="The Moldy Tome is half of the rare Tome of the Cabal, a dark book of rituals for summoning demons. Waterlogged and decayed, it is the half lost in a shipwreck.",al={"moldy book","what is this item","moldy tome lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where did the Moldy Tome end up?",a="The Moldy Tome washed ashore in Hillsbrad Foothills, west of Southshore and south of Azurelode Mine. Coastal murlocs keep it in their encampment.",al={"moldy tome location","where is moldy tome","where to find moldy tome"}},{q="Why was the tome on a ship?",a="A ship carried the Moldy Tome from Lordaeron toward Menethil Harbor, bound for Ironforge scholars. The ship sank off the Hillsbrad coast before completing its voyage.",al={"why was it lost at sea","shipwreck tome","tome transit"}},{q="What is needed to complete the Tome of the Cabal?",a="The Tome of the Cabal is completed by joining the Moldy Tome with the Tattered Manuscript, its other half. The manuscript ended up at Splithoof Hold in Thousand Needles.",al={"other half of the tome","missing pages","tome of the cabal parts"}},{q="Where does the Moldy Tome come from?",a="The Moldy Tome was originally part of a single, unique volume known as the Tome of the Cabal, once preserved within the great halls of Lordaeron. Long ago, the singular grimoire was vandalized, and a substantial portion of its parchment was torn away from the binding. The surviving portion of the book was slated to be shipped south from Hillsbrad across the sea to Menethil Harbor and Ironforge, but the vessel carrying it wrecked along the shore west of Southshore, leaving the damp pages to rot in the shallows.",al={"moldy tome origin","who made moldy tome","where was moldy tome kept","history of moldy tome"},it="origin",add="f96f31c9"},{q="Why does anyone want the Moldy Tome?",a="Scholars and practitioners of the dark arts seek it because only a single copy of the Tome of the Cabal was ever written. Its arcane passages contain rare and closely guarded warlock lore, including secrets essential for mastering the summoning and binding of felhunters. Scholars like Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge and Jorah Annison in the Undercity covet even a brief glimpse at its forbidden text, making the recovery of this waterlogged remnant vital to reuniting the full work.",al={"why find moldy tome","who wants moldy tome","why is moldy tome important","why do warlocks want moldy tome"},it="why_wanted",add="53a1a6b9"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you seek the Moldy Tome to help recover the rituals needed to command a felhunter."},kw={"azurelode","felhunter","hillsbrad","moldy tome","southshore","tattered manuscript","tome of the cabal","warlock"},rel={"item:tattered-manuscript","quest:1758","quest:1471","topic:warlock","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","npc:krom-stoutarm","npc:jorah-annison"},src={"Moldy Tome","Tome of the Cabal (Alliance, 2)","Tome of the Cabal (Horde, 2)"}}
E["item:package-of-empty-ooze-containers"] = {t="item",n="Package of Empty Ooze Containers",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, a package of empty ooze containers is bound for dangerous sampling in Felwood. Laris Geardawdle supplies jars that can hold tainted and cursed ooze without dissolving.",h="In Ironforge, a package of empty ooze containers is bound for dangerous sampling in Felwood.",sec={{t="Field Research Equipment",b="Laris Geardawdle sends a dozen empty jars with travelers bound for Felwood. Six are for cursed ooze and six for tainted ooze. Raw specimens are caustic, and ordinary luggage can be eaten away by them. Sturdy, sealed glass keeps the acidic residue contained on the journey across continents to Laris's workbench in Ironforge.",sp=0},{t="The Mystery of the Ooze",b="Laris Geardawdle's interest in ooze reaches beyond an eccentric hobby. He has seen Forsaken researchers from the Royal Apothecary Society harvesting these strange organisms across Azeroth, and wonders what they know. He suspects slimes may be primordial secretions tied to the world's creation. Field agents gather evidence in his jars, which he hopes will win him acclaim within the Explorers' League.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the package of empty ooze containers?",a="The package holds twelve empty specimen jars: six for cursed ooze and six for tainted ooze.",al={"package contents","what does package contain","ooze jars inside"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who provides this package?",a="Laris Geardawdle, a gnomish scholar and researcher in Ironforge, provides the package to Alliance adventurers.",al={"who gives the jars","laris geardawdle quest item","where do i get the ooze package"},it="origin"},{q="Where are these containers meant to be used?",a="The containers are meant for Felwood. There, adventurers defeat tainted and cursed oozes, then harvest residue from the fallen creatures.",al={"where do i use ooze jars","which zone for oozes","ooze jar location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Laris Geardawdle want these ooze samples?",a="Laris has seen the Forsaken Royal Apothecary Society gathering ooze across the world and wants to uncover its secrets. He suspects slimes may be primordial secretions tied to Azeroth's creation, and hopes evidence will earn him status in the Explorers' League.",al={"why collect slime","geardawdle research","why does laris want ooze"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Package of Empty Ooze Containers?",a="It is a field kit assembled by the gnome researcher Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge. The parcel contains a set of specially prepared jars designed to collect and safely store samples harvested from the corrupted oozes and slimes found throughout Felwood.",al={"what is package of empty ooze containers","ooze containers package","empty ooze container bundle"},it="identity",add="d8bf9111"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Laris Geardawdle's ooze research gives him a chance to show Ironforge's Dwarves that hosting refugee gnomes was worth the trouble.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, gathering these samples helps you keep pace with the unsettling research of the Forsaken Royal Apothecary Society."},kw={"containers","cursed","felwood","ironforge","jars","laris geardawdle","ooze","package","slime","tainted"},rel={"quest:4512","npc:laris-geardawdle","zone:felwood","zone:ironforge","item:filled-cursed-ooze-jar","item:filled-tainted-ooze-jar","topic:explorers-league","topic:royal-apothecary-society"},src={"Package of Empty Ooze Containers","A Little Slime Goes a Long Way"}}
E["item:searing-coral"] = {t="item",n="Searing Coral",z="ironforge",s="Along the Wetlands coast, Searing Coral is gathered from living iron coral beneath the sea. Tinkerers and smiths prize its heat-resistant mineral for strengthening armor.",h="Along the Wetlands coast, Searing Coral is gathered from living iron coral beneath the sea.",sec={{t="A Rare coastal Resource",b="Searing Coral grows in the cold sea south of Menethil Harbor. Living iron coral thrives in saltwater and yields mineral-rich material that withstands extreme heat. Harvesters must pry the hardened growths loose while wild murlocs and other aquatic beasts roam nearby.",sp=0},{t="Application in Smithing",b="Dwarven smiths do not traditionally work Searing Coral. In Ironforge, curious gnome craftsmen such as Klockmort Spannerspan follow methods from veteran armorsmith Furen Longbeard. They smelt the coral and hammer it into metal alloys, making lightweight, durable armor for aspiring warriors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Searing Coral grow?",a="Searing Coral grows in iron coral beds beneath the shallow coastal waters south of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"searing coral location","where to find searing coral","iron coral location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Searing Coral in Ironforge?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan, a gnomish artificer in Ironforge's Tinkertown, seeks Searing Coral. He experiments with smithing methods learned from the legendary dwarven armorer Furen Longbeard.",al={"who uses searing coral","klockmort spannerspan coral","furen longbeard coral"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How can coral be forged into armor?",a="Searing Coral has an unusually dense, heat-resistant structure. Smelted in a forge and hammered into metal alloys, it strengthens the composite plating and makes exceptionally tough protective gear.",al={"coral forging","can you smelt coral","searing coral metallurgy"}},{q="Is Searing Coral dangerous to harvest?",a="The coral itself is safe to gather once found. Reaching it means swimming in open waters off the Wetlands coast, where wild murlocs and aggressive aquatic beasts roam.",al={"is searing coral hot","harvesting iron coral"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is Searing Coral?",a="Searing Coral is a rare, mineral-rich marine growth harvested from Iron Coral formations beneath the waves along the coast of the Wetlands, south of Menethil Harbor. Despite being an oceanic specimen, its dense and peculiar properties allow it to be smelted, hammered, and worked like metal by skilled smiths.",al={"what is searing coral","searing coral info","searing coral lore"},it="identity",add="3e3d13aa"},{q="Where does Searing Coral come from?",a="Searing Coral is a natural aquatic growth rather than a manufactured artifact. It grows exclusively in one known place in the world: amidst the iron coral beds submerged along the coastal waters south of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"origin of searing coral","where does searing coral come from","who made searing coral"},it="origin",add="1c0d8f00"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, gathering Searing Coral proves your dedication to Ironforge's master armorers. They forge you a custom breastplate for heavy frontline combat.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how gnomish ingenuity joins classic dwarven metalworking to turn oceanic minerals into tempered plate."},kw={"furen longbeard","iron coral","ironforge","klockmort spannerspan","menethil harbor","searing coral","warrior armor","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1708","quest:1704","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge","npc:furen-longbeard"},src={"Searing Coral","Iron Coral (quest)"}}
E["item:senir-s-report"] = {t="item",n="Senir's Report",z="ironforge",s="In Dun Morogh’s cold foothills, Senir Whitebeard sends his findings on the Frostmane trolls to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge.",h="In Dun Morogh’s cold foothills, Senir Whitebeard sends his findings on the Frostmane trolls to Senator Barin...",sec={{t="A Royal Directive",b="Senir’s report gathers what mountaineers saw while scouting the Frostmane trolls in Dun Morogh’s crags. He also includes his brother Grelin’s account of Coldridge Valley. Grelin acted there with King Magni Bronzebeard’s sanction.\n\nSenir sends the findings to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge’s High Seat. He advises couriers to leave out how much outside help he needed to compile them.",sp=0},{t="Friction in the High Seat",b="Senir Whitebeard’s account reaches the royal court and stirs an uproar. Senator Barin Redstone is angered by the troll threat and by the authority stamped on the report. Magni bypassed legislative oversight, while Whitebeard acted on unchecked royal orders.\n\nThe move deepens resentment among senators who demand control over procedure. The strain sharpens between Magni’s decisive rule and the Senate’s claims to authority.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Senir's Report?",a="Senir Whitebeard’s report records his investigations into the Frostmane trolls in Dun Morogh. He sends it to the dwarven Senate in Ironforge.",al={"senirs report","what is this report","the report"},it="identity"},{q="Who is supposed to receive the report?",a="Senir Whitebeard addresses the report to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge’s High Seat, near King Magni Bronzebeard’s throne.",al={"who gets the report","who do i give the report to","report recipient"},it="target"},{q="Why does Senator Redstone get so angry when he reads it?",a="Senator Redstone is furious because Grelin Whitebeard’s enclosed report says Grelin acted under King Magni’s authority without consulting the Senate. Redstone resents the crown taking unilateral action on defense matters without senatorial approval.",al={"why is barin mad","why is the senator angry","redstone reaction"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Why does Senir ask you not to mention helping him?",a="Senir Whitebeard asks you to keep your help quiet so his superiors will believe he handled the hazardous scouting in the snowy hills alone. He wants to protect his reputation as a diligent, capable mountaineer.",al={"why keep quiet","senir secret","senir credit"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Senir's Report come from, and who made it?",a="Senir Whitebeard drafted this dispatch himself in Dun Morogh after scouting out the local Frostmane troll threats and securing aid in dealing with Frostmane Hold. Along with his own findings, it encloses his brother Grelin's report on Coldridge Valley, which Grelin wrote under a sanction from King Magni Bronzebeard, and carries both from the snowy frontiers into the great halls of the capital.",al={"who wrote senirs report","where did senirs report come from","author of senirs report"},it="origin",add="078e838e"},{q="Why does anyone want Senir's Report?",a="Senator Barin Redstone and the Ironforge Senate require official field assessments to track regional developments and military actions in Dun Morogh. However, because this specific dispatch asserts King Magni's unilateral authority over local maneuvers, it carries sharp political weight, informing the Senate of crown actions they feel bypass their oversight.",al={"why deliver senirs report","why does redstone need senirs report","purpose of senirs report"},it="why_wanted",add="e0c0da53"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, carrying Senir’s Report brings you into Ironforge’s divide between King Magni Bronzebeard’s decrees and the authority the Senate demands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, carrying Senir’s Report helps defend Dun Morogh while you navigate the prickly politics of Ironforge’s rulers."},kw={"barin redstone","frostmane","ironforge","magni bronzebeard","senate","senir whitebeard","senir's report","the reports"},rel={"quest:291","quest:287","zone:ironforge","subzone:kharanos"},src={"Senir's Report","The Reports"}}
E["item:tattered-manuscript"] = {t="item",n="Tattered Manuscript",z="ironforge",s="In Thousand Needles, Tattered Manuscript lies hidden in Splithoof Hold. Its torn pages came from the Tome of the Cabal, and warlocks seek them to learn how to summon a felhunter.",h="In Thousand Needles, Tattered Manuscript lies hidden in Splithoof Hold.",sec={{t="A Vandalized Grimoire",b="Once, the Tome of the Cabal was a unique, whole volume kept in the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron. An unknown defiler tore almost half its pages from the binding. The spine and pages left behind became known as the Moldy Tome. They were sent south toward Khaz Modan, then lost at sea. The torn leaves crossed the Great Sea to Kalimdor and came into the hands of the Galak centaur inside Splithoof Hold.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Words",b="A battered chest deep in the caverns of Splithoof Hold holds the manuscript. There it endured the dry winds of Thousand Needles. Alliance warlocks work with Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge, while Horde practitioners aid Jorah Annison in the Undercity. Both groups brave the aggressive centaur to reunite the leaves with the Moldy Tome. Together, the books hold dark rituals for summoning and binding a demonic felhunter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tattered Manuscript?",a="Tattered Manuscript gathers torn pages that make up roughly half of the unique Tome of the Cabal, a grimoire about demonology.",al={"tattered manuscript lore","what is manuscript","pages tome cabal"},it="identity"},{q="How did these pages end up in Thousand Needles?",a="After an unknown defiler tore the Tome of the Cabal in Lordaeron, its pages crossed the sea. The Galak centaur took them and hid them in a chest inside Splithoof Hold.",al={"why in splithoof","centaur tome","thousand needles manuscript"},it="place"},{q="What is the manuscript used for?",a="Warlocks reunite Tattered Manuscript with the waterlogged Moldy Tome to restore the Tome of the Cabal. The restored book teaches the ritual for summoning a felhunter.",al={"why do i need manuscript","felhunter quest pages"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was responsible for tearing the original book apart?",a="No one knows who tore the original book apart. Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge and Jorah Annison in the Undercity both lament the damage to the one-of-a-kind scholarly work.",al={"who ripped the tome","who vandalized tome cabal"},it="origin"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you seek the manuscript for the knowledge to command felhunters."},kw={"felhunter","jorah annison","krom stoutarm","moldy tome","splithoof hold","tattered manuscript","thousand needles","tome of the cabal"},rel={"item:moldy-tome","quest:1758","quest:1471","subzone:splithoof-hold","zone:thousandneedles","npc:krom-stoutarm","npc:jorah-annison","topic:warlock"},src={"Tattered Manuscript","Tome of the Cabal (Alliance, 2)","Tome of the Cabal (Horde, 2)"}}
E["npc:braenna-flintcrag"] = {t="npc",n="Braenna Flintcrag",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's Mystic Ward, Braenna Flintcrag teaches the ways of the Holy Light. She trains priests in healing and spiritual discipline, and tells visiting night elf priests when they are called home to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",h="In Ironforge's Mystic Ward, Braenna Flintcrag teaches the ways of the Holy Light.",sec={{t="A Guide in the Hall of Mysteries",b="Braenna Flintcrag trains priests in the Hall of Mysteries. There, in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, she teaches dwarven acolytes to heal and raise defensive wards with the Holy Light. Her lessons prepare them for a dangerous world. Through this work, she tends the spiritual needs of Khaz Modan, in a city renowned for its forges and warriors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Braenna Flintcrag?",a="Braenna Flintcrag trains priests in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. She teaches holy prayers, spells, and spiritual discipline.",al={"braenna flintcrag","who is braenna","priest trainer braenna"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Braenna Flintcrag?",a="Braenna Flintcrag is in the Hall of Mysteries, within Ironforge's Mystic Ward.",al={"where is braenna","braenna flintcrag location","find braenna flintcrag"},gp=true},{q="What services does she provide to travelers?",a="Braenna Flintcrag trains Alliance priests and advances their ranks. She also tells visiting night elf priests when they are called home to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"braenna services","what does braenna do","can braenna train me"},gp=true},{q="Is she related to anyone else in Khaz Modan?",a="Braenna Flintcrag shares her surname with Thulman Flintcrag. The name suggests a connection to a notable dwarven lineage in Khaz Modan.",al={"flintcrag family","thulman flintcrag relative","braenna flintcrag relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Braenna Flintcrag on?",a="Braenna is devoted to the Alliance and the dwarven kingdom of Ironforge. Operating from the Hall of Mysteries alongside fellow scholars, mystics, and holy practitioners, she serves her people and the broader Alliance through the teachings and spiritual discipline of the Holy Light.",al={"braenna flintcrag faction","who does braenna serve","braenna flintcrag alliance"},it="side",add="d5abdbfc"},{q="What does Braenna Flintcrag want?",a="Braenna is dedicated to guiding and preparing faithful disciples in the mysteries of the Holy Light. She devotes her time to training aspiring dwarven priests in Ironforge, ensuring they have the spiritual fortitude and sacred skills needed to aid their community and safeguard the Alliance.",al={"what does braenna want","braenna flintcrag goal","braenna flintcrag purpose"},it="wants",add="787cf3cf"},{q="Why is Braenna Flintcrag here?",a="Braenna resides in the Hall of Mysteries within Ironforge's Mystic Ward, which serves as the capital's sacred sanctuary for divine study and magical practice. Stationed among her fellow mentors, she remains readily available to assist and instruct priests traveling through or serving the mountain city.",al={"why is braenna here","why is braenna in ironforge","braenna flintcrag location reason"},it="why_here",add="19ad6f1b"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As an Alliance priest, you can learn essential spells and study the Light with Braenna Flintcrag in Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Ironforge's devotion to the Holy Light in Braenna Flintcrag's work alongside the city's martial traditions."},kw={"braenna flintcrag","hall of mysteries","holy light","ironforge","mystic ward","priest trainer","returning home"},rel={"subzone:hall-of-mysteries","subzone:mystic-ward","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf","quest:5628"},src={"Braenna Flintcrag"}}
E["npc:brandur-ironhammer"] = {t="npc",n="Brandur Ironhammer",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Brandur Ironhammer trains young paladins in the Holy Light and sends them across the Alliance.",h="In Ironforge, Brandur Ironhammer trains young paladins in the Holy Light and sends them across the Alliance.",sec={{t="A Guide in the Mystic Ward",b="In the Hall of Mysteries, Brandur Ironhammer teaches novice paladins the ways of the Holy Light. He and Tiza Battleforge guide young dwarven champions through the trials of the Tome of Divinity. Tiza has spoken plainly of Brandur’s flaws. He works to master his envy and keep the inner purity expected of a warrior of the Light.",sp=0},{t="Connecting the Silver Hand",b="Brandur links Ironforge to the wider Alliance brotherhood. Human initiates who come to the mountain are sent south to Duthorian Rall in the Cathedral of Light. Seasoned paladins go to battlegrounds such as Chillwind Camp in the Western Plaguelands. Veteran crusaders are directed to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker for the demanding trials of the war charger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Brandur Ironhammer located?",a="Brandur Ironhammer is in the Hall of Mysteries, in the Mystic Ward on Ironforge’s northern side.",al={"brandur ironhammer location","find brandur ironhammer","where is brandur"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Brandur Ironhammer play for paladins?",a="Brandur Ironhammer trains new paladins, guides initiates through the Tome of Divinity, and directs seasoned paladins to advanced trials across the Alliance.",al={"brandur paladin trainer","what does brandur do","brandur purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Brandur's peer in the Hall of Mysteries?",a="Brandur works alongside Tiza Battleforge, another dwarven paladin trainer in the Hall of Mysteries. Tiza has pointed out his jealousy, and Brandur works to overcome it.",al={"brandur partner","who works with brandur","tiza battleforge relation"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Brandur send paladins to Stormwind City?",a="Brandur sends human paladins training in Ironforge to Duthorian Rall or Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind’s Cathedral of Light for the formal rites of their own kingdom.",al={"brandur stormwind quest","why go to duthorian rall","brandur human paladins"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Brandur have connections to the fight against the Scourge?",a="Yes. Brandur passes along urgent calls from Commander Ashlam Valorfist and sends paladins proven in purity and valor to aid the Alliance crusade at Chillwind Camp on the border of the Western Plaguelands.",al={"brandur plaguelands","chillwind camp brandur","ashlam valorfist brandur"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Brandur Ironhammer?",a="Brandur Ironhammer is a dwarven paladin trainer stationed in the Hall of Mysteries within Ironforge's Mystic Ward. Dedicated to the Holy Light, he mentors ascending paladins in combat, faith, and virtue, guiding both dwarven initiates and human allies toward the trials and masters needed to hone their sacred calling.",al={"brandur ironhammer","who is brandur","brandur lore"},it="identity",add="ce9b1d9f"},{q="Whose side is Brandur Ironhammer on?",a="Brandur is firmly loyal to the Kingdom of Ironforge and the Grand Alliance. He serves the paladins of the Holy Light, cooperating closely with fellow defenders in Stormwind and relaying calls to support Alliance commanders on active fronts against the Scourge.",al={"brandur ironhammer faction","who does brandur serve","brandur alliance"},it="side",add="d07784b0"},{q="What does Brandur Ironhammer want?",a="Brandur seeks to foster a capable, righteous new generation of paladins to protect the Alliance and combat the darkness threatening Azeroth. On a personal level, he strives to overcome his own inner flaws, having sworn to his colleague Tiza Battleforge that he would work to conquer his lingering jealousy.",al={"brandur goal","what does brandur want","brandur purpose"},it="wants",add="cf78f4b8"},{q="Why is Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge?",a="He is stationed in the Hall of Mysteries to serve as a beacon and instructor for holy warriors within the dwarven capital. From here, he teaches martial and spiritual disciplines, tests novices, and coordinates with mentors across the Alliance to ensure that knights of the Light are ready for battle.",al={"why is brandur here","brandur in hall of mysteries","why brandur ironforge"},it="why_here",add="65b7f94c"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a dwarven or Alliance paladin, you can learn martial skills and sacred seals from Brandur in Ironforge, then follow his directions to advanced holy trials.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you share Khaz Modan’s tradition of paladins who join martial steel with reverence for the Holy Light in Ironforge."},kw={"brandur","hall of mysteries","ironforge","ironhammer","mystic ward","paladin","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity","trainer"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:hall-of-mysteries","subzone:mystic-ward","npc:tiza-battleforge","quest:2997","npc:duthorian-rall","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","subzone:chillwind-camp"},src={"Brandur Ironhammer"}}
E["npc:doctor-gustaf-vanhowzen"] = {t="npc",n="Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen",z="ironforge",s="At Foothold Citadel, Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen directs Theramore’s medical care. He trains healers and tests seasoned medics in field triage and bandage work.",h="At Foothold Citadel, Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen directs Theramore’s medical care.",sec={{t="Chief Physician of Theramore",b="On Foothold Citadel’s ground floor, Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen tends the forces of Lady Jaina Proudmoore and trains Theramore’s frontline healers. Dustwallow Marsh makes their work harsh, so VanHowzen demands skill under pressure. Experienced medics face his demanding triage test and must judge which wounds need care first.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen be found?",a="Doctor VanHowzen works on the ground floor of Foothold Citadel, the main fortress on Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"vanhowzen location","where is gustaf vanhowzen","gustaf vanhowzen spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does VanHowzen serve for the Alliance?",a="Doctor VanHowzen leads Alliance Trauma as its chief physician and Theramore’s leading trauma surgeon. He oversees the garrison’s medical ward and trains seasoned Alliance field medics in Artisan First Aid.",al={"what does vanhowzen do","vanhowzen role","who is doctor vanhowzen"},it="purpose"},{q="What does Doctor VanHowzen teach players?",a="Doctor VanHowzen gives the Artisan First Aid triage assessment, which lets skilled medics raise their skill cap. He also teaches qualified practitioners to make Heavy Mageweave and Runecloth bandages.",al={"what can i learn from vanhowzen","vanhowzen training","first aid from vanhowzen"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does the Horde have a counterpart to Doctor VanHowzen?",a="Yes. Doctor Gregory Victor is the Horde’s trauma specialist. He trains field medics and conducts triage examinations at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"horde triage trainer","horde vanhowzen counterpart","who is horde first aid master"},gp=true},{q="Who is Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen?",a="Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen is the chief physician of Alliance Trauma and a master trauma surgeon stationed in Theramore Isle. Renowned across the Alliance for his battlefield medical expertise, he is responsible for overseeing the training of Theramore's healers and teaching advanced triage techniques to field medics.",al={"who is vanhowzen","gustaf vanhowzen","who is doctor gustaf vanhowzen"},it="identity",add="5f514c39"},{q="Whose side is Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen on?",a="Doctor VanHowzen is thoroughly loyal to the Alliance. He directs the medical corps known as Alliance Trauma, serving under Lady Jaina Proudmoore's banner to ensure soldiers and frontline adventurers are kept alive through rigorous field medicine.",al={"vanhowzen faction","is vanhowzen alliance","doctor gustaf vanhowzen allegiance"},it="side",add="d768860b"},{q="What does Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen want?",a="Doctor VanHowzen wants to maintain the highest standards of trauma care across the Alliance's forces. In the field, hesitation costs lives, so he seeks to test and instruct competent field medics in triage methods to handle severe battle casualties under extreme pressure.",al={"what does vanhowzen want","vanhowzen motive","doctor vanhowzen goal"},it="wants",add="c346cbcd"},{q="Why is Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen here?",a="Stationed within Foothold Citadel on Theramore Isle, Doctor VanHowzen tends to the military bastion's injured and trains the local garrison's healers. From here, he tests prospective trauma medics venturing through Kalimdor who demonstrate mastery in first aid.",al={"why is vanhowzen in theramore","why is doctor vanhowzen here","where does vanhowzen work"},it="why_here",add="12e0bbc2"},{q="Who is Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen tied to?",a="Doctor VanHowzen serves the Alliance garrison at Theramore Isle, working under Lady Jaina Proudmoore's regional forces. He coordinates directly with Alliance military healers and commands the Alliance Trauma medical wing.",al={"vanhowzen affiliations","who does vanhowzen serve","doctor gustaf vanhowzen ties"},it="ties",add="9903e76f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance medic, travel to Theramore and prove your triage skills under Doctor VanHowzen’s watchful eye to master field surgery."},kw={"alliance trauma","artisan first aid","first aid","foothold citadel","gustaf vanhowzen","theramore","triage","vanhowzen"},rel={"subzone:foothold-citadel","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","quest:6625","npc:doctor-gregory-victor","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:alliance"},src={"Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen"}}
E["npc:elder-bronzebeard"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Bronzebeard",z="ironforge",s="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Bronzebeard appears in Ironforge's Mystic Ward. His name is the name of the clan that rules the city, and his earthen form recalls the dwarves' stone-born ancestors.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Bronzebeard appears in Ironforge's Mystic Ward.",sec={{t="A Progenitor in the Mystic Ward",b="Near the pool in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, Elder Bronzebeard appears in the shape of an earthen. The Titans forged the ancient earthen from living stone before they became creatures of flesh. Dwarven scholars and explorers are only beginning to uncover their origins through excavations across Khaz Modan and beyond.\n\nElder Bronzebeard bears the name of the ruling clan, and his form suggests he is a direct ancestor of the Bronzebeards. His spirit shows how far his stone-born descendants have changed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Elder Bronzebeard look like an earthen instead of a regular dwarf?",a="Dwarves descend from the earthen, ancient beings the Titans crafted from stone. Over time, the earthen became creatures of flesh. Elder Bronzebeard lived in the distant past, before that change took hold, and his spirit keeps the stony shape of his earthen days.",al={"why is elder bronzebeard stone","is elder bronzebeard earthen","elder bronzebeard race"},it="origin"},{q="Is he related to King Magni Bronzebeard?",a="His name and presence in Ironforge point to a revered ancestor of the Bronzebeard clan, the line that rules the city under King Magni. The exact branches of ancient family trees are lost to history.",al={"is he magni's ancestor","magni bronzebeard relative","bronzebeard family tree"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Elder Bronzebeard in Ironforge?",a="During the Lunar Festival, elder spirits appear throughout Azeroth to share wisdom and blessings with travelers. Elder Bronzebeard appears near the tranquil pool in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, where dwarven mages and scholars gather.",al={"what is elder bronzebeard doing here","where is elder bronzebeard","mystic ward ghost"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Elder Bronzebeard?",a="Elder Bronzebeard is an ancient earthen spirit lingering in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge. Appearing in the stony form of his Titan-forged forebears rather than flesh and bone, he represents the deep, ancestral roots of the dwarven people and their enduring lineage.",al={"who is elder bronzebeard","elder bronzebeard identity","what is elder bronzebeard"},it="identity",add="f31842b8"},{q="Whose side is Elder Bronzebeard on?",a="As an honored ancestor standing in the heart of Ironforge, Elder Bronzebeard watches peacefully over the dwarven capital. Like all the Lunar Festival elders he takes no side in mortal wars, offering greetings to travelers and pilgrims of any banner who approach him.",al={"elder bronzebeard faction","whose side is elder bronzebeard on","is elder bronzebeard alliance"},it="side",add="7b1c25c3"},{q="What does Elder Bronzebeard want?",a="Elder Bronzebeard seeks nothing beyond sharing communion with those who pay homage to the ancient ways. As a wandering spirit of the past, he greets pilgrims and bestows his presence upon respectful visitors.",al={"what does elder bronzebeard want","elder bronzebeard motive","why does elder bronzebeard want to talk"},it="wants",add="a81f3e52"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, meeting Elder Bronzebeard offers a rare glimpse of your earthen ancestry. The Explorers' League is uncovering more through its research.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance pilgrim in Ironforge during the Lunar Festival, you can meet an elder who represents the foundations of the dwarven kingdom."},kw={"ancestor","earthen","elder bronzebeard","ironforge","lunar festival","magni","mystic ward"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:mystic-ward","topic:bronzebeard-clan","quest:8866"},src={"Elder Bronzebeard"}}
E["npc:field-marshal-snowfall"] = {t="npc",n="Field Marshal Snowfall",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's Military Ward, Field Marshal Snowfall directs the Alliance's preparations against the silithid threat in Silithus. The dwarven officer oversees the supplies gathered for the coming war and rewards those who aid the realm.",h="In Ironforge's Military Ward, Field Marshal Snowfall directs the Alliance's preparations against the silithid...",sec={{t="Quartermaster of the Ahn'Qiraj Effort",b="From Ironforge's Military Ward, Field Marshal Snowfall directs the Alliance's war preparations. He sees the coming conflict as more than a border skirmish. It is a fight against an ancient enemy hostile to all creations of the Titans. Volunteers gather bandages, metal bars, leathers, herbs, and rations in great numbers. Snowfall oversees these stores so Alliance forces can be armed, armored, and fed when the march south to Silithus begins.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Silithus",b="Blacksmiths, gatherers, cooks, and soldiers across Alliance lands all have a part in preparing for war. Snowfall tracks their effort, accepts commendation signets, and offers supply requisitions to volunteers. Once both factions have gathered the required supplies, the stores are packed and hauled south to Cenarion Hold. From there, the grand assault will target the qiraji swarms and the Old God behind the Scarab Wall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Field Marshal Snowfall?",a="Field Marshal Snowfall is a high-ranking dwarven military officer in Ironforge's Military Ward. He oversees and tallies the Alliance's extensive supplies for the coming war against the qiraji in Silithus.",al={"snowfall role","who is snowfall","field marshal snowfall lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Alliance collecting so many supplies?",a="An ancient power threatens Kalimdor from beyond Ahn'Qiraj's gates. Before the armies can march across Silithus's harsh deserts, the Alliance must amass great reserves of armor, metal ingots, medical bandages, food, and herbs.",al={"why donate cloth","war effort purpose","why war supplies"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do the gathered materials go once finished?",a="When the Alliance and the Horde have both gathered the required supplies, caravans and supply ships carry the stockpiles to Cenarion Hold in Silithus. There, the combined forces establish their forward staging grounds.",al={"where do supplies go","what happens to the supplies"}},{q="What are the Signets for War Supplies used for?",a="Contributors receive Signets for War Supplies when they donate requested arms and materials. Snowfall accepts the signets in bundles and rewards dutiful Alliance citizens with supply crates and equipment for their service.",al={"signet turn ins","what are signets for"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Field Marshal Snowfall on?",a="Field Marshal Snowfall is a stalwart commander of the Alliance. Stationed in the Military Ward of Ironforge, he oversees the faction-wide logistics and resource gathering required to mount a joint offensive in Kalimdor. Though this campaign demands an uneasy parallel cooperation alongside the Horde to amass enough supplies, Snowfall's loyalties lie firmly with the kingdoms of the Grand Alliance.",al={"field marshal snowfall alliance or horde","snowfall faction","who does snowfall serve"},it="side",add="ec7ab6f1"},{q="What does Field Marshal Snowfall want?",a="Snowfall wants to stockpile staggering amounts of raw materials, bandages, metal bars, herbs, and food supplies from across the Alliance's lands. He aims to ensure that when the Gates of Ahn'Qiraj are breached, the standing army arriving in the harsh desert of Silithus has every weapon, potion, and ration needed to withstand C'Thun's legions without collapsing from attrition.",al={"field marshal snowfall goal","what is snowfall asking for","snowfall objective"},it="wants",add="e1b72348"},{q="Why is Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge?",a="Snowfall has set up command in Ironforge's Military Ward because the dwarven mountain city serves as a central hub of Alliance industry and trade. From here, he can track shipping manifests, coordinate incoming materials gathered by citizen-soldiers, and assemble the mountain of provisions before they are dispatched across the sea to the staging grounds in Silithus.",al={"why is snowfall in ironforge","snowfall military ward","why is field marshal snowfall here"},it="why_here",add="a597c3d5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Snowfall call on every race, from Stormwind to Darnassus, to empty its storehouses for the battle ahead. He represents the Alliance's unified industrial and military will.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you find Snowfall in the Great Forge's martial district. He speaks with pride of protecting the Titans' creations from an ancient, deep-seated depravity."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","field marshal snowfall","ironforge","military ward","signets","silithus","snowfall","war effort"},rel={"subzone:military-ward","zone:ironforge","zone:silithus","subzone:cenarion-hold","quest:8846","quest:8852","topic:old-god"},src={"Field Marshal Snowfall"}}
E["npc:gelbin-mekkatorque"] = {t="npc",n="Gelbin Mekkatorque",z="ironforge",s="In Tinker Town, Gelbin Mekkatorque leads the gnomes who live in exile in Ironforge. His inventions include the mechanostrider and the Deeprun Tram, and he guides the effort to reclaim Gnomeregan.",h="In Tinker Town, Gelbin Mekkatorque leads the gnomes who live in exile in Ironforge.",sec={{t="The High Tinker and Master Inventor",b="Gelbin Mekkatorque earned the title of High Tinker through inventive skill. Among the gnomes, leadership rests on intellect and merit, not bloodlines. He built the first working mechanostrider, changing how gnomes travel. He also helped the Bronzebeard dwarves develop siege engines and played a key part in building the Deeprun Tram between Ironforge and Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal and Exile in Ironforge",b="Troggs rose from deep below and invaded Gnomeregan. At the urging of his trusted friend and chief advisor, Mekgineer Thermaplugg, Gelbin Mekkatorque ordered radioactive waste released into the lower corridors to kill the attackers. Instead, the gas killed thousands of innocent gnomes and mutated the survivors. Thermaplugg took the ruined city.\n\nMekkatorque led the surviving refugees across Dun Morogh to Ironforge, burdened by guilt and determined to set things right. King Magni welcomed them in Tinker Town. There, Mekkatorque directs gnomekind’s military and scientific efforts toward reclaiming Gnomeregan.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelbin Mekkatorque?",a="Gelbin Mekkatorque leads the gnomes as their elected High Tinker. A master engineer, he designed important inventions, including the mechanostrider and the Deeprun Tram.",al={"high tinker","gnome leader","who is the gnome king"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Mekkatorque in Ironforge instead of Gnomeregan?",a="Troggs overran Gnomeregan, and radioactive fallout devastated the city. Mekkatorque led his people across Dun Morogh to Ironforge, where King Magni Bronzebeard gave them refuge in Tinker Town as they plan to reclaim their home.",al={"why is mekkatorque in ironforge","why are gnomes in ironforge","gnomeregan fall"},it="why_here"},{q="What caused the catastrophe in Gnomeregan?",a="Mekkatorque’s trusted advisor persuaded him to release toxic radioactive coolant into Gnomeregan’s lower chambers to stop the troggs. The gas failed to halt them and instead irradiated the city, killing thousands of gnomes.",al={"what happened to gnomeregan","why is gnomeregan irradiated","thermaplugg betrayal"}},{q="What did Mekkatorque invent before becoming High Tinker?",a="Before becoming High Tinker, Mekkatorque invented the mechanostrider. He also helped develop the dwarven siege engine and played a key part in creating the Deeprun Tram between Ironforge and Stormwind.",al={"mekkatorque inventions","what did gelbin build"}},{q="Is Mekkatorque an actual king?",a="Gnomes have no hereditary monarchy. They elect a High Tinker based on merit and intellect, and Mekkatorque’s authority comes from that election.",al={"is mekkatorque a king","king of gnomes"}},{q="Whose side is Gelbin Mekkatorque on?",a="Gelbin Mekkatorque stands firmly with the Alliance. As the leader of the gnomes, he maintains an unbreakable bond with King Magni Bronzebeard and the dwarves of Ironforge, who opened their gates to shelter his displaced people. Mekkatorque has pledged gnomish engineering, ingenuity, and military resources to aid their Alliance allies across Azeroth.",al={"mekkatorque faction","gelbin alliance","who does mekkatorque serve"},it="side",add="db25d752"},{q="What does Gelbin Mekkatorque want?",a="Mekkatorque's singular focus is reclaiming Gnomeregan. The loss of his home and the tragic deaths of countless gnomes weigh heavily upon him, driving him to find a way to purge the troggs and radiation poisoning their halls. From Tinker Town, he directs reconnaissance and organizes strike teams to prepare the groundwork for retaking the city.",al={"mekkatorque goal","what is gelbin trying to do","gelbin plan"},it="wants",add="0e3721be"},{q="Who is Gelbin Mekkatorque tied to?",a="Mekkatorque works closely with King Magni Bronzebeard, his gracious host in Ironforge, and coordinates with Alliance leadership in Stormwind. On a personal level, he is haunted by the loss of Gnomeregan and the thousands of gnomes who died after the radioactive venting he ordered on a trusted advisor's counsel.",al={"mekkatorque allies","gelbin relationships","who does mekkatorque work with"},it="ties",add="39ae11c6"},{q="Why is Gelbin Mekkatorque famous?",a="Mekkatorque is renowned across Azeroth as one of the greatest engineering geniuses in history. He invented the first functioning mechanostrider, helped design the dwarven siege engine, and was instrumental in creating the Deeprun Tram connecting Ironforge to Stormwind.",al={"why is mekkatorque famous","what is gelbin known for","mekkatorque inventions"},it="fame",add="5cf35b41"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you look to Mekkatorque as your people’s leader in exile. His guilt over Gnomeregan’s poisoning weighs on him, while his brilliance and devotion to reclaiming your ancestral home command loyalty in Tinker Town.",["profession:Engineering"]="Before you stands the High Tinker, inventor of the mechanostrider and a driving mind behind the Deeprun Tram. His Tinker Town workshop carries forward gnomish engineering."},kw={"deeprun tram","gelbin","gnome","gnomeregan","high tinker","ironforge","mechanostrider","mekkatorque","thermaplugg","tinker town"},rel={"zone:ironforge","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:deeprun-tram","npc:sicco-thermaplugg","npc:magni-bronzebeard","topic:gnome","topic:alliance","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Gelbin Mekkatorque"}}
E["npc:gerrig-bonegrip"] = {t="npc",n="Gerrig Bonegrip",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, Gerrig Bonegrip trades in strange texts and writings on dark rituals and ancient powers.",h="In Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, Gerrig Bonegrip trades in strange texts and writings on dark rituals and...",sec={{t="Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms",b="Gerrig Bonegrip runs Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms in the Forlorn Cavern. To most citizens, he seems an eccentric dealer in strange relics and forbidden lore. Beneath that trade, Gerrig serves the nihilistic Twilight's Hammer cult. He gathers dangerous manuscripts and obscure writings about the Old Gods, while the Ironforge Senate and the High Seat remain unaware.",sp=1},{t="Collecting Forbidden Knowledge",b="Gerrig enlists unwitting Alliance adventurers to recover ancient artifacts, including the Lorgalis Manuscript from deep within Blackfathom Deeps. He transcribes the knowledge in these relics and shares it with cult brethren across Azeroth. His connections include Skuerto and figures involved with ancient primordial entities such as Myzrael. Gerrig works to advance the cult's apocalyptic designs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gerrig Bonegrip?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip runs Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern. He trades in strange curiosities and obscure texts about ancient rituals.",al={"who is bonegrip","gerrig bonegrip lore","bonegrip ironforge"},sp=2,it="identity"},{q="What does he do with the Lorgalis Manuscript?",a="Gerrig seeks the Lorgalis Manuscript from Blackfathom Deeps for his collection of rare texts. Further investigation can reveal how he uses it.",al={"why does bonegrip want lorgalis manuscript","knowledge in the deeps turn in","lorgalis manuscript use"},sp=1,it="wants"},{q="How does Gerrig operate in Ironforge?",a="Gerrig keeps a low profile in the Forlorn Cavern as an eccentric scholar and merchant, buying and selling obscure texts.",al={"does ironforge know bonegrip is a cultist","why is bonegrip allowed in ironforge"},sp=2},{q="What is his connection to Myzrael?",a="Gerrig is an old associate of the dwarf Skuerto, who investigates the sealed earth elemental Myzrael in the Arathi Highlands. Through these ties, Gerrig helps arrange work connected to ancient binding rituals and primordial powers.",al={"gerrig bonegrip and myzrael","skuerto and gerrig"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Gerrig Bonegrip on?",a="Gerrig is a dwarf of Ironforge who runs Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms in the Forlorn Cavern. He trades in obscure lore about rituals and ancient powers, and he warns visitors that some of his knowledge is not meant for the uninitiated.",al={"gerrig bonegrip faction","who does gerrig work for","is gerrig bonegrip evil"},sp=1,it="side",add="ec528c98"},{q="Why is Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge?",a="Gerrig keeps his shop in Ironforge's shadowy Forlorn Cavern, where he collects, buys and sells rare manuscripts, runes and old lore about rituals. He pays adventurers to recover texts such as the Lorgalis Manuscript from Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"why is gerrig in ironforge","what is gerrig bonegrip doing here","why is gerrig bonegrip in the forlorn cavern"},sp=1,it="why_here",add="f2a99842"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may find Bonegrip's trade in forbidden lore casts an unsettling shadow over Ironforge's scholarly life.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock in the Forlorn Cavern, you can find dangerous knowledge in Bonegrip's collection of obscure rituals and dark tomes."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","bonegrip","forlorn cavern","gerrig","ironforge","lorgalis manuscript","runes and dooms"},rel={"subzone:forlorn-cavern","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:ironforge","quest:971","zone:blackfathom","npc:skuerto","topic:old-god","topic:dwarf"},src={"Gerrig Bonegrip"}}
E["npc:gnoarn"] = {t="npc",n="Gnoarn",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Gnoarn helps his scattered people find aid. After Gnomeregan fell, the exiled gnome made his home in Tinker Town and began directing travelers to fellow engineers and survivors.",h="In Ironforge, Gnoarn helps his scattered people find aid.",sec={{t="A Displaced Citizen of Gnomeregan",b="Troggs invaded Gnomeregan, and catastrophic radiation drove its people from the great underground city. The Bronzebeard dwarves gave Gnoarn refuge in Tinker Town. From there, he sends travelers to gnomes in need across Alliance lands, including the stranded pilot Bingles Blastenheimer in Loch Modan and the ambitious engineer Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gnoarn?",a="Gnoarn is a gnomish survivor living among the refugees in Tinker Town, Ironforge's gnomish quarter. He directs travelers to help exiled gnomes across Alliance lands.",al={"who is this gnome","gnoarn lore","gnoarn npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Gnoarn be found?",a="Gnoarn lives in Tinker Town, in northeastern Ironforge, among the machinery and workbenches of his exiled kin.",al={"gnoarn location","where is gnoarn","find gnoarn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Gnoarn give out?",a="Gnoarn directs travelers to help scattered gnomes. He sends them to Loch Modan to check on the missing pilot Bingles Blastenheimer, or to Stormwind to speak with the inventor Shoni the Shilent about her gyrodrillmatic excavationators.",al={"gnoarn quests","what does gnoarn want"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What happened to Gnoarn's hair?",a="Before Gnomeregan fell, Gnoarn was known for his eccentric 'gnomefro' hairstyle. Catastrophic fallout and radioactive venting devastated the city and took his hair with it.",al={"gnoarn gnomefro","gnoarn hair"}},{q="Whose side is Gnoarn on?",a="Gnoarn is loyal to his fellow gnomes of Gnomeregan and the Grand Alliance. Residing among the displaced gnomish population in Tinker Town, he works to keep his community organized and connected with their allies in Ironforge.",al={"gnoarn faction","is gnoarn alliance","who does gnoarn serve"},it="side",add="38923b37"},{q="Why is Gnoarn in Ironforge?",a="Like thousands of other gnomes, Gnoarn was driven from his home following the fall of Gnomeregan. When troggs overran the subterranean technological marvel and toxic radiation polluted its corridors, the survivors fled upward to seek sanctuary among their dwarven cousins in Ironforge, carving out a home in Tinker Town.",al={"why is gnoarn here","why did gnoarn come to ironforge","what brought gnoarn to ironforge"},it="why_here",add="ce7102b3"},{q="What does Gnoarn want?",a="Gnoarn is concerned with the safety and whereabouts of his displaced kin. In the disarray following Gnomeregan's evacuation, he looks for missing comrades like Bingles and directs capable adventurers to aid prominent inventors and specialists such as Shoni the Shilent.",al={"what is gnoarn trying to do","gnoarn goals","what does gnoarn need"},it="wants",add="82a3a1ba"},{q="Who is Gnoarn tied to?",a="Gnoarn maintains close ties with other Gnomeregan survivors in Ironforge, notably liaising with the renowned inventor Shoni the Shilent and coordinating efforts to locate fellow refugees like Bingles Blastenheimer.",al={"gnoarn allies","who does gnoarn know","gnoarn connections"},it="ties",add="efead32c"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Gnoarn's resolve in how he keeps displaced engineers in touch across the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero passing through Ironforge, you can speak with Gnoarn for leads on gnomish engineering efforts in Dun Morogh, Loch Modan, and Stormwind."},kw={"bingles","gnoarn","gnomefro","gnomeregan","ironforge","shoni the shilent","tinker town"},rel={"subzone:tinker-town","zone:ironforge","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome","quest:2039","quest:2041","quest:2927"},src={"Gnoarn"}}
E["npc:golnir-bouldertoe"] = {t="npc",n="Golnir Bouldertoe",z="ironforge",s="At Ironforge's Great Forge, Golnir Bouldertoe supplies miners and prospectors and receives dispatches from outposts.",h="At Ironforge's Great Forge, Golnir Bouldertoe supplies miners and prospectors and receives dispatches from...",sec={{t="Merchant of the Great Forge",b="Golnir Bouldertoe outfits prospectors and craftsmen at Ironforge's Great Forge. He sells mining picks, flux, and coal for the smelting fires and smithies of the dwarven capital. Kin to Geofram Bouldertoe, Golnir is a trusted contact for workers arriving in the city. He guides fresh hands and receives supply messages from nearby outposts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Golnir Bouldertoe?",a="Golnir Bouldertoe works in Ironforge's Great Forge, near the central smelting and blacksmithing areas with other trade merchants.",al={"golnir location","where is golnir","golnir bouldertoe ironforge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What goods does Golnir sell?",a="Golnir sells mining picks, coal, and flux to prospectors who dig and refine raw ore.",al={"golnir vendor wares","what does golnir sell","golnir inventory"},gp=true},{q="Is Golnir Bouldertoe involved in any quests?",a="Yes. Couriers carry messages from nearby dwarven settlements to the capital. Travelers bring dispatches from outposts such as Thelsamar, including messages linked to Gryth Thurden and incoming flights, directly to Golnir.",al={"golnir quests","ride to ironforge golnir"},gp=true},{q="Is Golnir related to anyone else in Dun Morogh?",a="Golnir shares his clan name with Geofram Bouldertoe, a mining trainer who works beside him in Ironforge's Great Forge.",al={"bouldertoe family","geofram bouldertoe relative"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Golnir Bouldertoe?",a="Golnir Bouldertoe is a dwarven merchant who works as a mining supplier within the Great Forge of Ironforge. He provides essential provisions, picks, and smelting supplies to the prospectors and smiths laboring at the city's molten heart.",al={"who is golnir","golnir bouldertoe lore","golnir identity"},it="identity",add="5f6dd933"},{q="Whose side is Golnir Bouldertoe on?",a="Golnir is a loyal subject of Ironforge and the Bronzebeard clan, standing firmly with the Grand Alliance. He keeps his trade situated in the kingdom's bustling center, serving fellow dwarves and visiting Alliance travelers alike.",al={"golnir faction","golnir allegiance","golnir side"},it="side",add="b602f757"},{q="Why is Golnir Bouldertoe here?",a="Golnir stays close to the Great Forge where the heat never dies and ore is constantly smelted. Because miners and blacksmiths from across Dun Morogh and beyond bring their finds directly to Ironforge's central hearth, Golnir keeps his shop nearby to outfit them with necessary gear.",al={"why is golnir in ironforge","golnir role great forge","why is golnir here"},it="why_here",add="7131f874"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners at the Great Forge rely on Golnir for tools of their craft, including spare picks and flux to smelt raw vein-work into refined bars.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves returning from their first journeys out in Coldridge or Kharanos, Golnir is an early contact in the capital. He welcomes travelers beside the mountain's fiery heart."},kw={"bouldertoe","coal","flux","golnir","great forge","ironforge","mining supplier"},rel={"subzone:great-forge","zone:ironforge","quest:6391","quest:6388","topic:dwarf"},src={"Golnir Bouldertoe"}}
E["npc:grand-mason-marblesten"] = {t="npc",n="Grand Mason Marblesten",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's Commons, Marblesten prepares a tribute to Sully Balloo. King Magni Bronzebeard commissioned the memorial for the dwarven soldier, who died in the Thandol Span tragedy. Marblesten seeks stone worthy of the work.",h="In Ironforge's Commons, Marblesten prepares a tribute to Sully Balloo.",sec={{t="Master of the Stone",b="Grand Mason Marblesten oversees civic projects and memorials in Ironforge's Commons. Dwarven stonemasons carve halls, pillars, and great effigies from the mountain, carrying on a centuries-old tradition. Marblesten is among the city's foremost masters of the chisel. Through his work, he preserves the history of the Bronzebeard line.",sp=0},{t="A King's Tribute",b="King Magni commissioned Marblesten to build a memorial to Sully Balloo, a soldier who died in the Thandol Span tragedy. The memorial honors Balloo and his grieving widow. For a tribute meant to last, Marblesten seeks Alterac Granite, one of the finest stones available. He asks travelers to bring it from Darrow Hill in Hillsbrad.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grand Mason Marblesten?",a="Grand Mason Marblesten is a senior dwarven stonemason in Ironforge's Commons. He oversees civic and royal sculpting projects, including King Magni Bronzebeard's commission for a memorial to Sully Balloo.",al={"who is marblesten","marblesten role","grand mason npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Grand Mason Marblesten?",a="You can find Grand Mason Marblesten in Ironforge's Commons, among stone blocks and architectural works near the city's shops and banks.",al={"marblesten location","where is marblesten","ironforge marblesten"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What monument is Marblesten working on?",a="Marblesten is building a memorial to Sully Balloo, a dwarven soldier who died in the Thandol Span tragedy. King Magni Bronzebeard commissioned it to honor Balloo and his grieving widow.",al={"what is he building","kings tribute quest","marblesten statue"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Marblesten need adventurers to gather materials?",a="Marblesten seeks one of the finest stones for a lasting memorial. He sends travelers to Darrow Hill in Hillsbrad to gather Alterac Granite.",al={"marblesten quests","why need stones","materials for monument"},it="motive"},{q="What does the title 'Grand Mason' mean in dwarven society?",a="Among dwarves, a Grand Mason is a master of stonecraft trusted with major state projects, royal architectural designs, and ceremonial memorials. Stoneworking is revered alongside blacksmithing.",al={"what is a grand mason","dwarf mason rank"}},{q="Is Marblesten an Alliance official or a private contractor?",a="Marblesten works within Ironforge for the kingdom and the Alliance. He coordinates with King Magni Bronzebeard's court on royal commissions.",al={"who does marblesten work for","marblesten faction"}},{q="Whose side is Grand Mason Marblesten on?",a="Marblesten is entirely loyal to Ironforge and the Alliance. Stationed right in the heart of the city's Commons, he serves King Magni Bronzebeard and the dwarven kingdom, dedicating his craft and masonry to honoring dwarven heritage and the throne.",al={"marblesten faction","who does marblesten serve","marblesten alliance"},it="side",add="a77cb24b"},{q="What does Grand Mason Marblesten want?",a="Marblesten is overseeing a royal monument and requires fine materials to see it completed. Through his work on 'A King's Tribute,' he seeks capable adventurers to help procure the essential resources needed for the memorial to the fallen soldier Sully Balloo, commissioned by King Magni.",al={"what does marblesten want","marblesten goal","why does marblesten need help"},it="wants",add="1dc5a337"},{q="Why is Grand Mason Marblesten in the Commons?",a="Marblesten makes his workshop in the bustling Commons of Ironforge to oversee the stonework of the great mountain fortress and organize construction efforts for the throne. The open plaza allows him to coordinate projects and enlist travelers passing through the city.",al={"why is marblesten in ironforge","why is marblesten here","marblesten commons ironforge"},it="why_here",add="98aae54f"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, stonecraft is an ancestral heritage. Helping Marblesten honors the craft of Khaz Modan and the memory of Sully Balloo.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners who work the rock of Dun Morogh and beyond know the care Marblesten gives to the quality of raw stone.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Sully Balloo's sacrifice recalls the soldiers lost in its wars."},kw={"a king's tribute","bronzebeard","commons","grand mason","ironforge","magni","marblesten","stonemason","sully balloo"},rel={"quest:686","zone:ironforge","subzone:commons","topic:dwarf"},src={"Grand Mason Marblesten"}}
E["npc:granis-swiftaxe"] = {t="npc",n="Granis Swiftaxe",z="ironforge",s="At the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, Granis Swiftaxe trains young Alliance fighters from Coldridge Pass. He prepares them for the road across Dun Morogh, then sends seasoned warriors to Ironforge.",h="At the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, Granis Swiftaxe trains young Alliance fighters from Coldridge Pass.",sec={{t="A Gruff Mentor in Kharanos",b="Granis Swiftaxe trains young warriors in the Thunderbrew Distillery as they cross Dun Morogh seeking instruction. Proud of the warrior’s path, he takes amusement in those from other callings who try to win his attention. Once a student proves their skill in combat, Granis sends them up the mountain path to Muren Stormpike, master trainer in Ironforge’s Military Ward.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Granis Swiftaxe?",a="Granis Swiftaxe trains young dwarf and gnome warriors on the ground floor of the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos. He teaches them the first martial techniques they need for travel across Dun Morogh.",al={"granis swiftaxe","who is granis","kharanos warrior trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Granis mock my character?",a="Granis has little patience for those who do not follow the warrior’s path. When someone of another class speaks to him, he scoffs that they would not survive a day under his training.",al={"granis rude quote","why is granis laughing at me","granis non warrior text"}},{q="Where does Granis send advancing warriors?",a="When a warrior has gained enough experience in Dun Morogh, Granis sends them to Muren Stormpike, a senior warrior trainer in Ironforge’s Military Ward.",al={"muren stormpike quest","granis questline","who does granis send you to"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is Granis related to other Swiftaxes in Khaz Modan?",a="Granis shares the Swiftaxe surname with other dwarves, but no family relationship is confirmed.",al={"swiftaxe family","granis swiftaxe relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Granis Swiftaxe on?",a="Granis stands firmly with the Ironforge dwarves and the broader Alliance. Stationed in Kharanos, he dedicates his martial expertise to drilling the next generation of defenders against the troggs, frost trolls, and other threats surrounding Dun Morogh.",al={"granis swiftaxe faction","who does granis fight for","granis alliance"},it="side",add="b8e95117"},{q="Why is Granis Swiftaxe in Kharanos?",a="Granis is stationed inside the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos to train fledgling Alliance warriors who set out from Coldridge Pass. Dun Morogh faces mounting pressure from native troggs and Wendigos, making his rigorous combat drills vital for local defense.",al={"why is granis here","granis swiftaxe location reason","what brought granis to kharanos"},it="why_here",add="760b1803"},{q="What does Granis Swiftaxe want?",a="Granis wants nothing less than hardened, disciplined warriors capable of holding the line for Khaz Modan. He has little patience for the weak or untrained, demanding relentless dedication from recruits before directing promising veterans to masters like Muren Stormpike in Ironforge.",al={"granis swiftaxe goals","what does granis want","granis purpose"},it="wants",add="cf3183bb"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a dwarf or gnome warrior leaving Coldridge Valley, you can learn early combat skills from Granis at the Thunderbrew Distillery.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you’ll find Granis’s stubborn pride and martial discipline among the comforts of local ale."},kw={"dun morogh","granis swiftaxe","kharanos","muren stormpike","thunderbrew distillery","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:thunderbrew-distillery","subzone:kharanos","quest:1679","zone:dunmorogh","topic:dwarf","quest:117"},src={"Granis Swiftaxe"}}
E["npc:greatfather-winter"] = {t="npc",n="Greatfather Winter",z="ironforge",s="As winter turns, Greatfather Winter is part of old legend and city festivities. Some say he lays snow across Azeroth so the land may rest and renew. In the cities, goblins of Smokywood Pastures shape how people know him.",h="As winter turns, Greatfather Winter is part of old legend and city festivities.",sec={{t="Myth and Renewal",b="Ancient tales say Greatfather Winter wanders the world late in the year. He spreads his snowy cloak, and nature sleeps before it is born anew. Dwarves call him an aspect or herald of the titans. They point to Dun Morogh's frosted crags as proof of his favor. Tauren honor his place in winter's turning, while crediting the Sun and Moon with the cold and storms that let the Earth Mother rest.\n\nAcross the lands, people gather and feast against the cold. They hold to the promise that life will return.",sp=0},{t="Smokywood Pastures and City Festivities",b="In Ironforge and Orgrimmar, goblins of Smokywood Pastures have reshaped the old spirit for city celebrations. The trading company made popular the image of Greatfather Winter as a cheerful elder in red, with a white beard, flying sleigh, holiday treats, and toys.\n\nSmokywood Pastures hires a dwarf in Ironforge and an orc in Orgrimmar to hear children's wishlists and accept milk and gingerbread cookies. Beneath lavishly decorated trees, the company also promotes its seasonal wares.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Is the Greatfather Winter in Ironforge the real spirit?",a="The Greatfather Winter by Ironforge's festive tree is an actor hired by Smokywood Pastures. The goblin company stages these appearances to delight children and sell seasonal confections. Ancient legends tell of an ethereal being who walks the world in winter.",al={"is greatfather winter real","who is the guy in ironforge","is he an actor"},it="identity"},{q="Why do dwarves revere Greatfather Winter?",a="Dwarves connect Greatfather Winter with the titans, their creators. They see the snow he spreads as a blessing and point to Dun Morogh's perpetually frigid peaks as proof of his favor.",al={"dwarf winter veil","dwarven father winter","ironforge greatfather winter"},it="fame"},{q="What does Greatfather Winter do with the cookies and milk brought to him?",a="In Smokywood Pastures' holiday tales, Greatfather Winter snacks on gingerbread cookies and ice cold milk while reading wishlists and spreading holiday cheer.",al={"treats for greatfather winter","why milk and cookies","gingerbread cookies quest"}},{q="How does the Horde view Greatfather Winter?",a="In Orgrimmar, Smokywood Pastures promotes the festivities with an orc portraying Greatfather Winter. Tauren respect winter as a time for the Earth Mother to rest and renew. They honor his part in the seasonal cycle without worshipping the titans.",al={"horde greatfather winter","orgrimmar greatfather winter","tauren winter veil"}},{q="Whose side is Greatfather Winter on?",a="He belongs to neither faction. In legend, Greatfather Winter is an ancient, supernatural force of nature who bestows seasonal renewal and bounty across the entire world, regardless of mortal allegiances. The figure you see sitting in Ironforge is sponsored by the goblin trade company Smokywood Pastures, who maintain a strictly neutral, profit-driven operation. In fact, Smokywood Pastures hires an orc counterpart to sit in Orgrimmar and spread holiday cheer among the Horde simultaneously.",al={"greatfather winter alliance or horde","is greatfather winter alliance","greatfather winter faction"},it="side",add="66677a0e"},{q="What does Greatfather Winter want?",a="The ancient spirit of myth seeks only to cloak the world in winter, giving the land necessary time for rest, rebirth, and eventual renewal while granting bounty to those who welcome him. The mortal impersonator you meet in Ironforge, however, is employed by Smokywood Pastures. Their goal is entirely festive and commercial: bringing cheer, handing out treats to good children, and driving enthusiastic sales for their holiday goods and toys.",al={"greatfather winter motives","what does greatfather winter want","why does greatfather winter give gifts"},it="wants",add="a8f1de98"},{q="Why is Greatfather Winter in Ironforge?",a="Smokywood Pastures stationed him beside the Winter Veil tree to anchor their seasonal festivities. During the weeks leading up to the holiday, the jolly figure meets with citizens and children to hear their holiday wishes, collect letters, and spread goodwill alongside his goblin helpers—all while helping Smokywood Pastures promote their seasonal wares.",al={"why is greatfather winter in ironforge","why is greatfather winter here","greatfather winter location ironforge"},it="why_here",add="daa32740"},{q="Who is Greatfather Winter tied to?",a="Dwarven tradition closely links the ancient spirit to the titans, believing he personifies their shaping power over Azeroth's seasons. In everyday practice, the festive Greatfather seen in the city is partnered with Smokywood Pastures, surrounded by their diminutive Little Helpers and festive snowmen.",al={"who is greatfather winter associated with","greatfather winter connections","who works with greatfather winter"},it="ties",add="8b922b4d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Greatfather Winter as an aspect of the titans who carved the world. Dun Morogh's snowy peaks bear witness to his touch.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can make gingerbread cookies and other festive treats for Smokywood Pastures and Greatfather Winter himself."},kw={"dun morogh","gingerbread cookies","great-father winter","greatfather winter","ironforge","orgrimmar","smokywood pastures","winter veil"},rel={"zone:ironforge","zone:orgrimmar","zone:dunmorogh","topic:dwarf","topic:tauren","topic:goblin","topic:titan","quest:7025"},src={"Greatfather Winter"}}
E["npc:high-priest-rohan"] = {t="npc",n="High Priest Rohan",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, High Priest Rohan guides the Church of the Holy Light from the Hall of Mysteries. He teaches young priests, helps them deepen their mastery of the Light, and keeps spiritual ties between Ironforge, Stormwind, and distant allies.",h="In Ironforge, High Priest Rohan guides the Church of the Holy Light from the Hall of Mysteries.",sec={{t="Shepherd of the Hall of Mysteries",b="In Ironforge’s Mystic Ward, High Priest Rohan paces the Hall of Mysteries as the Church of the Holy Light’s highest-ranking representative in the city. Dwarves once honored the titans, yet their priests have embraced the Light’s wisdom, compassion, and justice. Rohan patiently teaches young acolytes to wield holy magic and steel their minds against despair.",sp=0},{t="Bridges Across the Alliance",b="Once the priests in his care master the fundamentals, Rohan sends them abroad to learn from other traditions. Human and dwarven students go to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind City. Night elf disciples travel to Priestess Alathea at Darnassus’s Temple of the Moon, where they study mysteries such as Elune’s Grace. Rohan also sends healers to aid the Cenarion Circle’s druids in distant Azshara, wherever hardship calls.",sp=0},{t="The Exorcism Censer",b="Rohan keeps sacred relics for the Alliance priesthood and paladin brotherhoods. Among them is a blessed exorcism censer used for years to cleanse vile spirits. When the Order of the Silver Hand and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker need it for their knights’ holy calling, Rohan lends it freely. He asks only for charitable alms to replenish Ironforge’s dwindling food reserves for the needy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find High Priest Rohan?",a="Find High Priest Rohan pacing inside the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge’s Mystic Ward, on the city’s northern side. He walks between the holy library and the altar.",al={"rohan location","where is priest trainer ironforge","rohan map","hall of mysteries priest trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Rohan serve in Ironforge?",a="Rohan trains new priests, offers spiritual counsel, and directs them to advanced study across Azeroth. He is Ironforge’s senior priest trainer and the leading dwarven representative of the Church of the Holy Light in Khaz Modan.",al={"who is rohan","what does rohan do","rohan lore"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Rohan send priests to Darnassus or Stormwind?",a="Rohan sends human and dwarven initiates to Stormwind’s Cathedral of Light to learn prayers such as Desperate Prayer. Night elf priests return to Darnassus’s Temple of the Moon to study mysteries such as Elune’s Grace. He believes spiritual growth draws on diverse traditions.",al={"rohan class quests","desperate prayer rohan","temple of the moon quest"},it="allies"},{q="Why do paladins seek out Rohan?",a="Paladins sent by Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker seek Rohan’s blessed exorcism censer. He lends the relic for the Order of the Silver Hand’s rites and asks for a modest donation of supplies to feed Ironforge’s poor.",al={"paladin quest rohan","exorcism censer","emphasis on sacrifice"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Rohan send priests to Azshara?",a="Rohan sends healers to aid the Cenarion Circle’s night elf druids working in Azshara’s wild lands. He follows the Light’s call to charity and service.",al={"cenarion aid rohan","rohan cenarion circle"},it="motive"},{q="Does Rohan only train dwarves?",a="Rohan guides Alliance devotees of many races, including dwarves, humans, and night elves. His early instruction prepares them to study with mentors who know their traditions.",al={"can humans train with rohan","who does rohan train"},it="people"},{q="Who is High Priest Rohan?",a="High Priest Rohan is the highest-ranking member of the Church of the Holy Light residing in Ironforge. A venerable and devout dwarf, he serves as the principal spiritual mentor for priests within the mountain kingdom, guiding novices in the ways of devotion, healing, and holy wrath.",al={"who is rohan","high priest rohan","rohan lore"},it="identity",add="077c3151"},{q="Whose side is High Priest Rohan on?",a="Rohan stands firmly with the Kingdom of Ironforge, the Grand Alliance, and the Church of the Holy Light. He works closely with human clergy in Stormwind, the night elves of Darnassus, and even sends aid to neutral groups like the Cenarion Circle when lives need saving.",al={"rohan faction","is rohan alliance","rohan allegiance"},it="side",add="940e11c6"},{q="What does High Priest Rohan want?",a="Rohan is dedicated to spreading the virtues of the Holy Light and tending to those in need. He seeks to cultivate wisdom and resilience in young priests, care for Ironforge's impoverished residents, and dispatch aid wherever suffering threatens innocent lives across Azeroth.",al={"what does rohan want","rohan goals","rohan motivations"},it="wants",add="90c6beb0"},{q="Why is High Priest Rohan here in the Hall of Mysteries?",a="The Hall of Mysteries serves as Ironforge's sanctuary for divine study and arcane contemplation. Rohan paces its sacred halls to oversee the city's spiritual well-being, minister to visiting supplicants, and personally instruct rising priests before sending them out into the wider world.",al={"why is rohan in ironforge","why is rohan here","rohan hall of mysteries"},it="why_here",add="88d280c0"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, Rohan’s guidance and early training are essential. He later directs you to renowned mentors in Stormwind or Darnassus, where you can learn racial devotions.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin sent by Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker, you visit Rohan to borrow his exorcism censer. In return, you bring aid for Ironforge’s needy.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Rohan’s devotion to the Holy Light. The people of Khaz Modan hold deep spiritual conviction alongside their titan heritage.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance devotee, you can see Rohan keep Ironforge’s clergy connected with the Cathedral of Light, the Temple of the Moon, and the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"church of the holy light","exorcism censer","grayson shadowbreaker","hall of mysteries","high priest rohan","ironforge","mystic ward","priest trainer","rohan"},rel={"subzone:hall-of-mysteries","subzone:mystic-ward","zone:ironforge","npc:high-priestess-laurena","npc:priestess-alathea","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","quest:5634"},src={"High Priest Rohan"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-firebrew"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Firebrew",z="ironforge",s="At the Stonefire Tavern in Ironforge’s Commons, Innkeeper Firebrew gives travelers food and rest. His hearty dwarven fare welcomes mountaineers and visiting dignitaries beneath the mountain.",h="At the Stonefire Tavern in Ironforge’s Commons, Innkeeper Firebrew gives travelers food and rest.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Stonefire",b="Innkeeper Firebrew welcomes travelers at the Stonefire Tavern in the Commons. The tavern stands in the Commons’ central ring, and many arriving through the Great Gates find it first. Behind a counter of ale, stout, and roasted meat, Firebrew serves those bound for Dun Morogh’s snowy passes or deeper into the mountain kingdom.\n\nMiners, riflemen, and emissaries gather there to leave the drafty tunnels behind and trade tales around the hearth. The Stonefire remains a lively crossroads in the heart of Ironforge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Firebrew?",a="Innkeeper Firebrew can be found inside the Stonefire Tavern, along the southern edge of Ironforge’s Commons.",al={"firebrew location","where is innkeeper firebrew","ironforge tavern keeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of goods does Firebrew sell?",a="Firebrew sells standard innkeeper provisions, including robust dwarven rations. Travelers can buy Dwarven Stout and Mead, imported wines, meats, and hearty meals for long journeys.",al={"what does firebrew sell","firebrew drinks","stonefire tavern food"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is Firebrew part of any dwarven brewing family?",a="Firebrew bears the surname Firebrew, but his family relationships are not confirmed.",al={"firebrew family","who is firebrew related to"},it="ties"},{q="What services does he provide to travelers?",a="Firebrew lets Alliance travelers bind their hearthstones to the Stonefire Tavern. He also provides a warm bed where travelers can rest and recover beneath the mountain.",al={"can i bind hearthstone here","ironforge hearthstone inn"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Innkeeper Firebrew?",a="Innkeeper Firebrew is the dwarven proprietor of the Stonefire Tavern, located in the bustling Commons of Ironforge. A welcoming figure within the mountain city, he tends the hearth, serves ale, and provides food and lodging to locals and weary travelers alike.",al={"who is firebrew","innkeeper firebrew","stonefire tavern innkeeper"},it="identity",add="9fc434fc"},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Firebrew on?",a="Firebrew is loyal to the Kingdom of Ironforge and stands firmly with the Alliance. He keeps his tavern open to all allied adventurers seeking refuge from the cold winds of Dun Morogh or resting after long journeys across Azeroth.",al={"firebrew faction","firebrew alliance","is firebrew alliance"},it="side",add="3dd110f9"},{q="What does Innkeeper Firebrew want?",a="Firebrew is focused on running a lively and hospitable tavern. He wants to keep the Stonefire Tavern's hearth roaring, fill patrons' mugs with strong dwarven drink, and ensure visitors to the great forge city have a warm place to rest and bind their hearthstones.",al={"what does firebrew want","firebrew motive","firebrew goals"},it="wants",add="e30bdb86"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Firebrew here?",a="Firebrew manages the Stonefire Tavern in the Commons, making him the central host for travelers entering the heart of Ironforge. He stays right by the hearth to offer lodging, sell rations and drink, and provide a welcoming anchor for adventurers arriving in the capital.",al={"why is firebrew in ironforge","why is firebrew at the stonefire tavern"},it="why_here",add="b21a7171"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf returning from patrol across Khaz Modan, you can find the comforting warmth of home and a reliable mug of dwarven stout at Firebrew’s tavern.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler from abroad, you can rest at the central safe haven Firebrew keeps near Ironforge’s front gates, in King Magni Bronzebeard’s capital. Firebrew is the primary innkeeper there."},kw={"commons","dwarf","firebrew","hearthstone","innkeeper","ironforge","stonefire tavern"},rel={"subzone:stonefire-tavern","subzone:commons","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","quest:8353"},src={"Innkeeper Firebrew"}}
E["npc:krom-stoutarm"] = {t="npc",n="Krom Stoutarm",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Krom Stoutarm turns to the darker arts in the Hall of Explorers. A dwarven scholar and warlock, he studies arcane texts and demonic rites in the library. He guides Alliance warlocks seeking esoteric knowledge across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",h="In Ironforge, Krom Stoutarm turns to the darker arts in the Hall of Explorers.",sec={{t="A Darker Corner of the Hall",b="Krom Stoutarm pursues occult lore in the Hall of Explorers. While dwarven archaeologists there study titan artifacts with picks and shovels, Krom turns to massive tomes and the rites for binding demons. His work gives a warlock’s craft a place in Ironforge’s mountain halls, though many distrust those arts.",sp=0},{t="The Tome of the Cabal",b="Alliance warlocks seeking to bind powerful demons such as the felhunter turn to Krom Stoutarm. He knows of occult volumes scattered across distant lands. He sends summoners to recover torn pages and fragments of the infamous Tome of the Cabal, including from the centaur of Thousand Needles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Krom Stoutarm?",a="You can find Krom Stoutarm in the Library wing of the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge.",al={"krom stoutarm location","where is krom stoutarm","krom stoutarm ironforge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Krom Stoutarm play for players?",a="Krom guides Alliance warlocks through demonic rites, including the recovery of the Tome of the Cabal.",al={"what does krom do","krom stoutarm purpose","krom stoutarm quests"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Krom Stoutarm related to other Stoutarms?",a="Several dwarves share the Stoutarm surname, but no family relationship between Krom and the others is confirmed.",al={"krom relatives","sten stoutarm related"},it="ties"},{q="Why is a warlock permitted inside the Hall of Explorers?",a="Krom is a dwarf of Ironforge who once worked as a digger at the Uldaman excavation. Now an itinerant warlock, he gathers ancient texts in the library, and no one is known to have turned him away.",al={"why is krom in hall of explorers","ironforge warlock allowed"}},{q="Why is Krom connected to the Barrens?",a="Krom’s search for the Tome of the Cabal ends in the Barrens. Warlocks recover its torn halves from the centaur of Thousand Needles and from a lost shipment off the coast west of Southshore. Krom then sends the rebuilt tome to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.",al={"krom stoutarm barrens","why barrens quest krom"},it="why_here"},{q="Does Krom Stoutarm train spells?",a="Krom is a scholarly contact rather than a class trainer. He guides warlocks through particular rites of passage instead of teaching everyday grimoires.",al={"can krom train me","krom warlock trainer"},gp=true},{q="Who is Krom Stoutarm?",a="Krom Stoutarm is a dwarven warlock who studies dark lore from within the Library of the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. Unlike many practitioners of the fel arts who hide in shadowed basements and secluded covens, Krom operates openly among the scholars and excavators of the Explorers' League, delving into ancient relics, obscure arcana, and occult tomes.",al={"who is krom","krom stoutarm lore","who is krom stoutarm"},it="identity",add="6ca19015"},{q="Whose side is Krom Stoutarm on?",a="Krom Stoutarm is loyal to Ironforge and the Alliance. Though he practices warlock arts that draw suspicion and unease from many of his kin, he remains a respected scholar within the Hall of Explorers, offering his esoteric expertise and arcane knowledge solely to aid Alliance champions in their endeavors.",al={"krom stoutarm faction","krom stoutarm alliance or horde","who does krom serve"},it="side",add="23fb54c2"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As an Alliance warlock, you consult Krom while pursuing dark bindings, including the dangerous work of assembling the Tome of the Cabal.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see Krom’s place among the Hall of Explorers’ revered shelves as a rare exception, since dwarves usually reject the fell arts.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance practitioner, you can find an intellectual refuge with Krom inside Ironforge’s mountain stronghold."},kw={"hall of explorers","ironforge","krom stoutarm","library","stoutarm","tome of the cabal","warlock"},rel={"quest:1758","subzone:library-ironforge","subzone:hall-of-explorers","zone:ironforge","npc:sten-stoutarm","zone:barrens","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance"},src={"Krom Stoutarm"}}
E["npc:laris-geardawdle"] = {t="npc",n="Laris Geardawdle",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, Laris Geardawdle welcomes travelers with samples of noxious slime. The gnome researcher gives his academic life to studying oozes across Azeroth and their strange nature and origins.",h="In Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, Laris Geardawdle welcomes travelers with samples of noxious slime.",sec={{t="Scholar of Slime",b="In the Hall of Explorers Library, Laris Geardawdle studies how oozes begin. His dwarven colleagues pore over Titan tablets and ancient stone carvings. Laris searches Azeroth's vile, gelatinous horrors for alchemical and biological secrets.\n\nHe asks roving explorers to gather caustic samples from remote corners of the world. With those samples, he tests his unusual ideas about how these mindless puddles of malice come to life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Laris Geardawdle?",a="Laris Geardawdle is a gnome researcher in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers Library. He studies oozes and slimes, and the strange way they come into being.",al={"laris","geardawdle","who is laris"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Laris Geardawdle?",a="You can find Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge's northern wing, inside the Hall of Explorers and its Library.",al={"laris location","where is laris","find laris geardawdle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is he studying oozes?",a="Laris Geardawdle studies oozes because his curious, eccentric mind has led him to form theories about how living slime begins. He believes caustic residue from different oozes can explain how these strange organisms form and replicate.",al={"why oozes","laris slime research","ooze study"},it="wants"},{q="What tasks does he offer adventurers?",a="Laris Geardawdle asks travelers to collect ooze samples in dangerous lands. In A Little Slime Goes a Long Way, he gives them empty ooze containers and sends them to Felwood to take samples from oozes they slay. Then he asks them to seek pure, uncorrupted samples.",al={"laris quests","a little slime goes a long way"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Laris Geardawdle on?",a="Laris Geardawdle stands firmly with the Alliance and the Gnomeregan Exiles. Operating out of the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge alongside dwarven scholars and researchers, he contributes his keen mind and eccentric biological theories toward advancing Alliance knowledge and understanding of strange phenomena across the world.",al={"laris geardawdle faction","laris geardawdle alliance","is laris geardawdle friendly"},it="side",add="a960bc4a"},{q="Why is Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge?",a="Following the fall of Gnomeregan, many gnomes sought refuge among their dwarven allies in Ironforge. Laris Geardawdle made his home in the Library within the Hall of Explorers, an ideal sanctuary where he can pursue his eccentric academic research and catalog his theories on the origin of oozes with full access to extensive historical and natural archives.",al={"why is laris geardawdle here","laris geardawdle hall of explorers","why is laris in ironforge"},it="why_here",add="114e8ed2"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you share Laris Geardawdle's drive to seek knowledge in places everyone else overlooks. Sometimes that means reaching into foul swamp muck.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can find Laris Geardawdle in the Hall of Explorers. His work brings eccentric natural science to the League's historical digging."},kw={"gnome","hall of explorers","ironforge","laris geardawdle","library","ooze","slime"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:hall-of-explorers","subzone:library-ironforge","quest:4512","topic:gnome"},src={"Laris Geardawdle"}}
E["npc:lieutenant-nevell"] = {t="npc",n="Lieutenant Nevell",z="ironforge",s="Outside Ironforge in Dun Morogh, Lieutenant Nevell keeps watch for the Scourge. This Argent Dawn officer coordinates local defenders and warns newcomers of undead threats near the dwarven kingdom.",h="Outside Ironforge in Dun Morogh, Lieutenant Nevell keeps watch for the Scourge.",sec={{t="A Watch in the Snow",b="Lieutenant Nevell watches Ironforge's snowy approaches for the Scourge. Though the Argent Dawn is best known for holding the line in Lordaeron's shattered Plaguelands, its watch reaches farther south. From outside Ironforge, Nevell directs recruits and capable adventurers toward the front when Scourge activity stirs in Dun Morogh's mountain passes. So the dwarven city's borders remain under watch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Nevell?",a="Lieutenant Nevell serves the Argent Dawn near Ironforge in Dun Morogh. He rallies local defenders and investigates signs of the Scourge near the dwarven realm.",al={"nevell role","who is nevell","lieutenant nevell"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn outside Ironforge?",a="The Argent Dawn watches for undead incursions across the continent, though its main presence is in Lordaeron. Officers such as Nevell monitor Dun Morogh and coordinate defenses against Scourge threats.",al={"argent dawn in dun morogh","argent dawn ironforge"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Lieutenant Nevell ask adventurers to do?",a="Lieutenant Nevell sends capable adventurers beyond Ironforge's gates to scout and fight nearby Scourge forces before the undead can establish a foothold in the mountain passes.",al={"nevell quests","investigate the scourge"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Lieutenant Nevell on?",a="Lieutenant Nevell serves the Argent Dawn, a dedicated neutral order committed to protecting Azeroth from the Scourge. Though human, he stands outside the gates of Ironforge as an ally to all who oppose the undead menace, coordinating defenses alongside the dwarves rather than serving the Alliance military directly.",al={"lieutenant nevell faction","who does lieutenant nevell fight for","is nevell argent dawn"},it="side",add="4853a4a6"},{q="Who is Lieutenant Nevell tied to?",a="Nevell answers directly to the leadership of the Argent Dawn. Stationed on the slopes of Dun Morogh, he acts as a liaison between the order and the defenders of Ironforge, rallying local adventurers and mountain guards to confront any creeping threat of the Scourge in the region.",al={"nevell connections","lieutenant nevell argent dawn ties","who does nevell report to"},it="ties",add="5e43a7a7"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you have the Argent Dawn watching over your mountain home against necromancy on Dun Morogh's cold slopes.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion entering Ironforge, you see that the war against the Scourge reaches beyond the north."},kw={"argent dawn","dun morogh","ironforge","lieutenant nevell","nevell","scourge"},rel={"quest:9261","topic:argent-dawn","zone:ironforge","zone:dunmorogh","topic:scourge","npc:lieutenant-orrin"},src={"Lieutenant Nevell"}}
E["npc:lomac-gearstrip"] = {t="npc",n="Lomac Gearstrip",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's Tinker Town, Lomac Gearstrip pursues gnomish inventions. He formulated the NG-5 explosive and stays in contact with fellow researchers in Kalimdor.",h="In Ironforge's Tinker Town, Lomac Gearstrip pursues gnomish inventions.",sec={{t="A Spark in Tinker Town",b="Lomac Gearstrip works on gnomish ordnance in Ironforge's Tinker Town. Like many gnomes who fled Gnomeregan's tragedy, he brought his tinkering operations to the dwarven capital. His workshop centers on volatile chemical mixtures and specialized munitions meant to overcome heavily defended enemy strongholds.",sp=0},{t="The NG-5 Explosive",b="Lomac's proudest contribution to combat engineering is the NG-5 explosive. The compound is made for great destructive force and demands precise handling and rare chemical reagents. To refine and use such hazardous inventions in the field, Lomac stays in touch with former colleagues in distant theaters. They exchange technical orders and dangerous supplies across the Great Sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac works in Tinker Town, the gnomish quarter in eastern Ironforge.",al={"lomac gearstrip location","where is lomac","find lomac gearstrip"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Lomac Gearstrip famous for inventing?",a="Lomac is best known for formulating the NG-5 explosive, made to bring great firepower to gnomish endeavors.",al={"what did lomac make","lomac invention","ng-5 explosive creator"},it="fame"},{q="Why does Lomac deal with contacts in Kalimdor?",a="Lomac keeps in touch with former research peers and colleagues in frontier regions such as Stonetalon Mountains. They coordinate hazardous chemical ingredients and test his explosives in active operations.",al={"lomac stonetalon","why stonetalon quest","lomac colleagues"},it="why_here"},{q="What kind of tasks does Lomac offer to adventurers?",a="Lomac entrusts Alliance couriers with carrying purchase orders and volatile chemical reagents between Ironforge and researchers abroad. These deliveries often involve his NG-5 explosive experiments.",al={"lomac quests","ineptitude chemicals fun","an old colleague quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the Purchase Order Receipt tied to Lomac?",a="Lomac authored the Purchase Order Receipt, a manifest for organizing and documenting shipments of specialized equipment and dangerous volatile reagents between tinkerers.",al={"purchase order receipt","lomac receipt"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is Lomac affiliated with Gnomeregan's refugees?",a="Yes. Lomac belongs to the displaced Gnomeregan community living under the hospitality of Ironforge's dwarves while continuing his engineering work.",al={"is lomac from gnomeregan","lomac faction"},it="side"},{q="Who is Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac Gearstrip is an ambitious gnomish inventor and tinker operating out of Tinker Town within the dwarven stronghold of Ironforge. Deeply engrossed in volatile experimentation and chemical engineering, he is best known for developing potent ordnances like the NG-5 explosive. Despite the distance across the Great Sea, he maintains contacts and business arrangements stretching as far as Kalimdor to acquire the rare materials and field testing he needs.",al={"who is lomac","who is gearstrip","lomac gearstrip lore"},it="identity",add="e46167fb"},{q="What does Lomac Gearstrip want?",a="Lomac Gearstrip is driven by his explosive engineering projects, most notably the refinement of his prized NG-5 charge. To keep his chemical trials moving forward, he requires couriers, volatile compounds, and field tests conducted with his concoctions. He relies on travelers and old acquaintances across the world to fulfill purchase orders and procure the rare reagents necessary to perfect his volatile inventions.",al={"what does lomac want","lomac gearstrip goals","why does lomac need help"},it="wants",add="6618560a"},{q="Who is Lomac Gearstrip tied to?",a="Lomac maintains ties with distant associates and fellow tinkers, including an old colleague based abroad who assists with orders and specialized testing. Working from Tinker Town, he operates comfortably alongside both the Gnomeregan exiles and Ironforge's resident craftsmen, directing couriers and adventurers to liaise between his workbench in the Eastern Kingdoms and testing grounds across Kalimdor.",al={"who does lomac work with","lomac gearstrip associates","lomac old colleague"},it="ties",add="ca50cdb6"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Lomac's NG-5 explosive reflects advanced gnomish pyrotechnics and may inspire tinkerers interested in powerful blasting compounds.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Lomac shares Tinker Town's resilient drive, pursuing demanding technical research while exiled from Gnomeregan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance operatives traveling between Ironforge and expedition outposts in Kalimdor often handle sensitive munitions and volatile formulas for Lomac."},kw={"an old colleague","gnome engineer","ineptitude + chemicals = fun","ironforge","lomac gearstrip","ng-5 explosive","stonetalon","tinker town"},rel={"subzone:tinker-town","zone:ironforge","quest:1072","quest:1073","zone:stonetalon","topic:gnome"},src={"Lomac Gearstrip"}}
E["npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker",z="ironforge",s="At Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker trains champions of the Light and guides promising knights. A veteran paladin commander of the Knights of the Silver Hand, he also oversees the sacred trials senior paladins must complete to claim their holy chargers.",h="At Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker trains champions of the Light and guides...",sec={{t="Master of the Silver Hand",b="In Stormwind City, Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker leads the Silver Hand's work and stands among the Alliance's foremost defenders. A veteran of the order, he trains recruits in arms and tests their faith in the Light. When promising knights are ready, he sends them north to the contested front lines of the Western Plaguelands. There, they aid Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp.",sp=0},{t="The Trials of the Holy Charger",b="Paladins seeking a sacred warhorse must prove their virtue and make sacrifices under Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker's guidance. The trials include acts of charity, such as helping Ironforge's impoverished through High Priest Rohan. They also demand perilous journeys to exorcise Terrordale and the cleansing of ancient spirits within Dire Maul. At Scholomance, an initiate must face the death knight Darkreaver and use the Light to free an unholy steed from servitude.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker?",a="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker is inside the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square, Stormwind City. He stands in the main halls, overseeing the paladins of the Silver Hand.",al={"where is grayson shadowbreaker","shadowbreaker location","where is lord grayson"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Lord Grayson's role for paladins?",a="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker trains Alliance paladins. He sends young knights to the front lines against the Scourge in Lordaeron and guides the sacred trials to make holy barding and claim a paladin charger.",al={"what does grayson do","grayson shadowbreaker purpose","why visit lord grayson"},it="purpose"},{q="Did Lord Grayson lose an eye?",a="No account from these days tells whether Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker lost an eye, or how. He is known as a veteran lord of the Silver Hand and one of the Alliance's foremost paladins.",al={"how did grayson lose his eye","why is grayson missing an eye","grayson eyepatch"},it="history"},{q="What is his connection to the Forsaken?",a="No known account ties Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker or his family to the Forsaken. He is a paladin of the Silver Hand who sends knights to fight the Scourge in Lordaeron.",al={"grayson sister","does grayson have undead family"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Grayson send paladins to Grimand Elmore?",a="Grimand Elmore forged the barding for Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker's own charger years ago. Grayson sends worthy initiates to Grimand to craft their Arcanite Barding, which must balance physical endurance with spiritual harmony.",al={"grayson and grimand elmore","who makes the paladin barding","arcanite barding quest"},it="item"},{q="Who is Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker?",a="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker is one of the foremost paladins of Stormwind and the Alliance. A battle-hardened veteran of the Knights of the Silver Hand, he serves as a senior master of the holy order, training and guiding promising knights in the ways of the Light.",al={"who is grayson shadowbreaker","who is lord grayson","about grayson shadowbreaker"},it="identity",add="70324968"},{q="Whose side is Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker on?",a="Lord Grayson stands firmly with the Grand Alliance, the kingdom of Stormwind, and the Order of the Silver Hand. He is dedicated completely to the Holy Light and the defense of the living against the Scourge and other dark threats.",al={"grayson shadowbreaker faction","who does grayson serve","is grayson alliance"},it="side",add="2db8c97e"},{q="What does Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker want?",a="Lord Grayson seeks to forge the next generation of holy warriors to push back the darkness consuming Azeroth. He tests paladins through arduous spiritual and martial trials, sending them to fight the Scourge in the Plaguelands and proving their worthiness to earn a blessed charger.",al={"grayson shadowbreaker goals","what does grayson want","grayson motive"},it="wants",add="88e74201"},{q="Why is Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral of Light?",a="He is stationed within Stormwind's Cathedral of Light to oversee the development of the city's paladins. From this central bastion of faith, he coordinates missions against the Scourge and guides senior champions through the demanding trials required to summon their holy warhorses.",al={"why is grayson in stormwind","why is grayson here","grayson cathedral of light"},it="why_here",add="a5a2c568"},{q="Who is Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker tied to?",a="Grayson works closely with High Priest Rohan of Ironforge, the blacksmith Grimand Elmore, and commanders fighting the Scourge in the north like Ashlam Valorfist.",al={"grayson shadowbreaker allies","who does grayson know","grayson squires"},it="ties",add="c41cec02"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can look to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker as a senior spiritual mentor in the Alliance. He guides you in the fight against the Scourge in Lordaeron and leads the trials to summon a true charger.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can count on Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker, a veteran of the Silver Hand, to strengthen Stormwind's defense and aid expeditions to the contested northern kingdoms."},kw={"cathedral of light","charger","grayson","grimand elmore","paladin","scholomance","shadowbreaker","silver hand"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","quest:1700","zone:stormwind","npc:high-priest-rohan","subzone:chillwind-camp","subzone:scholomance","subzone:dire-maul","topic:light"},src={"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker"}}
E["npc:nissa-firestone"] = {t="npc",n="Nissa Firestone",z="ironforge",s="Above Ironforge’s Great Forge, Nissa Firestone teaches field medicine to travelers and soldiers.",h="Above Ironforge’s Great Forge, Nissa Firestone teaches field medicine to travelers and soldiers.",sec={{t="A Healer Above the Anvils",b="Nissa Firestone tends patients upstairs in the Ironforge Physician shop. The Great Forge’s clang and heat reach her there, while she binds their wounds. Dwarven warriors can endure much, yet blades and claws still break their skin. Before travelers and soldiers set out into Dun Morogh’s snows or farther afield, Nissa teaches basic bandaging and field dressings. These skills can help keep them and their allies alive.",sp=0},{t="Triage and Advanced Trauma",b="Nissa Firestone teaches field medics how to use cloth and lint. When she has taught all she can, she directs them to specialized triage officers in distant outposts. Skilled healers go where Alliance casualties are heaviest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nissa Firestone?",a="Nissa Firestone is a dwarf who teaches first aid at the Ironforge Physician shop on the Great Forge’s southern perimeter.",al={"who is nissa firestone","nissa firestone role","ironforge first aid trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Nissa Firestone?",a="Nissa Firestone works upstairs in the Ironforge Physician shop, on the southern edge of the Great Forge ring in Ironforge.",al={"nissa firestone location","where is nissa","ironforge physician location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Nissa Firestone teach?",a="Nissa Firestone teaches Alliance adventurers First Aid, including how to prepare bandages and antidotes for injuries in the field.",al={"what does nissa teach","first aid ironforge","learn bandages ironforge"},gp=true},{q="Can Nissa teach master-level triage?",a="No. When a medic reaches advanced proficiency, Nissa directs them elsewhere through the Alliance Trauma assignment, toward seasoned field surgeons near active war zones.",al={"alliance trauma quest","master first aid ironforge","first aid over 225"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Nissa Firestone on?",a="Nissa Firestone stands firmly with Ironforge and the Alliance. Stationed high in the capital, she dedicates her medical knowledge to keeping Ironforge's defenders and Alliance travelers alive through field dressing and trauma care.",al={"nissa firestone faction","is nissa alliance","who does nissa serve"},it="side",add="f16b91f7"},{q="Why is Nissa Firestone in Ironforge?",a="Nissa works out of the Ironforge Physician shop above the Great Forge. From this central position within the dwarven capital, she can tend to the city's sick and injured while training adventurous field medics to bind wounds and staunch bleeding before they march into battle.",al={"why is nissa here","nissa firestone location why","what brought nissa to ironforge"},it="why_here",add="bc93403c"},{q="What does Nissa Firestone want?",a="As a physician and trainer, Nissa's primary aim is ensuring that Alliance fighters know how to patch themselves up in the field. When promising medics outgrow her tutelage, she directs them to advanced field surgeons who can teach wartime triage.",al={"what does nissa want","nissa firestone goals","nissa firestone motive"},it="wants",add="2ef2db38"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf returning from a skirmish with troggs or frost trolls, you find in Nissa the practical, no-nonsense tradition of Ironforge medicine.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer passing through Khaz Modan, you can learn essential ways to survive from trainers like Nissa, without divine or arcane magic."},kw={"alliance trauma","bandages","first aid","great forge","healer","ironforge physician","nissa firestone"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:great-forge","quest:6625","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance"},src={"Nissa Firestone"}}
E["npc:prospector-stormpike"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Stormpike",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Prospector Stormpike sends aid to distant archaeological digs. The blunt, short-tempered dwarf of the renowned Stormpike clan can also decipher coded messages with a sharp mind.",h="In Ironforge, Prospector Stormpike sends aid to distant archaeological digs.",sec={{t="Scholar of the Hall of Explorers",b="From the Library of the Hall of Explorers, Prospector Stormpike coordinates excavations across Khaz Modan and beyond. He sends supplies to distant sites, even blasting powder. Idle chatter tries his patience, yet he is devoted to uncovering dwarven history. His keen mind can break intricate ciphers and help scouts face secret threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Stormpike?",a="Prospector Stormpike is an archaeologist and logistics coordinator of the renowned Stormpike clan. He works in the Library of Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.",al={"who is stormpike","prospector stormpike lore","stormpike npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Prospector Stormpike?",a="You can find Prospector Stormpike inside the Library, in the eastern reaches of Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.",al={"stormpike location","where is prospector stormpike"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of work does he do?",a="Stormpike manages supplies and reports for archaeological digs. He sends blasting powder to field prospectors such as Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan, and helps scouts break complex coded messages.",al={"stormpike quests","what does stormpike do"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Southshore need his help?",a="Southshore's Alliance authorities need Stormpike to decipher intercepted letters written by the secretive Argus Wake cult.",al={"argus wake cipher","southshore stormpike"}},{q="Whose side is Prospector Stormpike on?",a="Prospector Stormpike is loyal to the Kingdom of Ironforge and the Alliance. As an operative of the dwarven Explorers' League, his field duties and archaeological research directly serve King Magni Bronzebeard and the interests of the dwarven realm.",al={"stormpike faction","prospector stormpike alliance","who does stormpike serve"},it="side",add="676ebbc6"},{q="What does Prospector Stormpike want?",a="Prospector Stormpike wants to decipher vital intelligence and coordinate archaeological expeditions without needless disruption. He oversees research for excavations like Ironband's Excavation Site in Loch Modan and applies his expertise in cryptanalysis to untangle encoded messages, demanding utmost focus and impatience with idle distractions.",al={"what does stormpike need","prospector stormpike goal","stormpike motives"},it="wants",add="b4a2ac01"},{q="Why is Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge?",a="You can find Prospector Stormpike stationed in the Library of Ironforge's Hall of Explorers because it serves as the operational nerve center for the Explorers' League. From here, he reviews field reports, translates recovered relics, and deciphers intercepted correspondence requiring scholarly attention.",al={"why is stormpike here","prospector stormpike library","why hall of explorers stormpike"},it="why_here",add="1b565b81"},{q="Who is Prospector Stormpike tied to?",a="He is a member of the influential Stormpike clan, an esteemed dwarven lineage renowned across Khaz Modan. Beyond his clan, he works directly with fellow field prospectors such as Prospector Ironband and assists Alliance leaders in Southshore by breaking enemy ciphers.",al={"stormpike clan connections","prospector stormpike allies","stormpike league ties"},it="ties",add="dbd365e1"},{q="Why is Prospector Stormpike famous or feared?",a="Prospector Stormpike is renowned for his brilliant knack for deciphering complex, encrypted documents, alongside a notorious, fiery temper. Few scholars possess both his sharp cryptanalytic mind and his volcanic lack of patience for anyone wasting his time.",al={"stormpike reputation","why is prospector stormpike known","stormpike hot temper"},it="fame",add="d5ca9c54"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see the Explorers' League spirit in Stormpike's driven, no-nonsense approach. He treats ancient research and logistics as matters of dwarven pride.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can rely on Stormpike's skill with ciphers in operations against secretive human cults such as the Argus Wake in northern lands."},kw={"argus wake","explorers league","hall of explorers","ironforge","joren ironband","library","prospector stormpike","stormpike clan"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge","subzone:hall-of-explorers","zone:ironforge","quest:301","quest:302","subzone:southshore","topic:dwarf"},src={"Prospector Stormpike"}}
E["npc:roetten-stonehammer"] = {t="npc",n="Roetten Stonehammer",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, Roetten Stonehammer organizes expeditions for Reclaimers Inc. He hires adventurers to recover salvage in distant lands such as Desolace.",h="In Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, Roetten Stonehammer organizes expeditions for Reclaimers Inc.",sec={{t="Business in the Library",b="Roetten Stonehammer handles recovery work for Reclaimers Inc. from the Library in the Hall of Explorers. He connects mercenaries with salvage work across Kalimdor. His associates seek valuable cargo, wreckage, and rare reagents in dangerous lands such as Desolace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Roetten Stonehammer?",a="Roetten Stonehammer works in the Library of Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. He coordinates expeditions and hires adventurers for Reclaimers Inc.'s recovery work abroad.",al={"who is roetten","who is roetten stonehammer","roetten stonehammer lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is Reclaimers Inc.?",a="Reclaimers Inc. salvages lost shipments, gathers rare reagents, and investigates valuable wrecks in dangerous lands such as Desolace.",al={"what is reclaimers inc","reclaimers inc","reclaimers business"},it="ties"},{q="Where does Roetten send adventurers?",a="Roetten sends travelers across the sea to Desolace in western Kalimdor. His partners seek shipwreck salvage and reagents along its rugged coast and barren wilderness.",al={"roetten stonehammer quests","where does roetten send you","reclaimers business in desolace"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Roetten Stonehammer on?",a="Roetten Stonehammer is allied with Ironforge and the Alliance, operating openly within the Hall of Explorers. His business ventures, particularly on behalf of Reclaimers Inc., serve Alliance interests by hiring dependable travelers to recover lost assets and supplies in distant, hazardous lands.",al={"roetten stonehammer alliance or horde","who does roetten stonehammer serve","roetten stonehammer faction"},it="side",add="c52b1d4d"},{q="What does Roetten Stonehammer want?",a="Roetten is seeking capable adventurers to assist with overseas salvage and recovery operations for Reclaimers Inc. He directs hired help toward dangerous wildernesses like the barren shores of Desolace, aiming to secure salvage from lost shipments and gather exotic reagents necessary for his associates' work.",al={"what is roetten stonehammer looking for","roetten stonehammer motive","why does roetten stonehammer need help"},it="wants",add="4b23d3f4"},{q="Why is Roetten Stonehammer here?",a="You can find Roetten wandering the grand Library within Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. He bases himself here to consult ancient archives, stay in close contact with fellow scholars and prospectors, and recruit daring explorers passing through the dwarven capital.",al={"why is roetten in ironforge","what is roetten doing in hall of explorers","roetten stonehammer library"},it="why_here",add="f41f4afa"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can find Roetten in Ironforge's grand archives, where archaeological curiosity meets commercial salvage.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to Roetten in Ironforge for expeditions across the sea to Desolace in Kalimdor."},kw={"desolace","hall of explorers","ironforge","library","reclaimers inc","roetten stonehammer","salvage"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge","subzone:hall-of-explorers","zone:ironforge","quest:1453","zone:desolace","topic:dwarf"},src={"Roetten Stonehammer"}}
E["npc:royal-historian-archesonus"] = {t="npc",n="Royal Historian Archesonus",z="ironforge",s="At the High Seat, Royal Historian Archesonus records calamities for the Ironforge crown. A dwarven scholar in King Magni Bronzebeard’s service, she writes of disasters in the northern human kingdoms and oversees study of ancient dwarven tragedies, including the Dark Iron kingdom’s scorched remains.",h="At the High Seat, Royal Historian Archesonus records calamities for the Ironforge crown.",sec={{t="Chronicler of Catastrophe",b="Royal Historian Archesonus keeps Ironforge’s records near King Magni Bronzebeard’s throne in the High Seat. Her studies reach beyond the Khaz Modan mountains. She wrote 'The Fall of Lordaeron and the Scouring of the Eastweald' and 'On Plagues, Curses, and Blights.' In them, she traces the Scourge’s ruin of humanity’s northern realm. She records the truth of ruinous magic and political collapse with care.",sp=0},{t="The Ashes of Thaurissan",b="Royal Historian Archesonus oversees research into the War of the Three Hammers and Thaurissan’s destruction. She seeks relics and charred tablets from the Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan in the Burning Steppes, and sends adventurers there to search. Her work examines the cataclysm that scorched the Burning Steppes and bound the Dark Iron clan to the Firelord.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Royal Historian Archesonus?",a="Find Royal Historian Archesonus in the High Seat of Ironforge, near King Magni Bronzebeard’s throne room.",al={"archesonus location","where is royal historian archesonus","archesonus ironforge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What books did Royal Historian Archesonus write?",a="Royal Historian Archesonus wrote 'The Fall of Lordaeron and the Scouring of the Eastweald' and 'On Plagues, Curses, and Blights.' Her books record the downfall of the human north and the necrotic afflictions spread by the Scourge.",al={"archesonus books","what did archesonus write","archesonus lore books"}},{q="Why is Archesonus interested in the Ruins of Thaurissan?",a="Royal Historian Archesonus studies ancient dwarven history and sends scouts into the Burning Steppes to recover lost relics from the Ruins of Thaurissan. She seeks to piece together the catastrophe that destroyed the ancient Dark Iron capital.",al={"archesonus thaurissan quest","why does she want ruins of thaurissan","smoldering ruins of thaurissan"},it="wants"},{q="What is her role in Ironforge?",a="Royal Historian Archesonus is Ironforge’s official Royal Historian, chief chronicler, and archivist for King Magni Bronzebeard. She compiles records of dwarven antiquity and wider events threatening the Alliance.",al={"archesonus title","what does royal historian do","who is archesonus"},it="identity"},{q="Whose side is Royal Historian Archesonus on?",a="Royal Historian Archesonus serves King Magni Bronzebeard and the Kingdom of Ironforge, firmly aligning her with the Alliance. Stationed directly within the High Seat, her scholarship and archival research support the royal court's understanding of ancient dwarven history, neighboring lands, and the lingering threats to their realm.",al={"archesonus faction","who does archesonus serve","is archesonus alliance"},it="side",add="d5335835"},{q="Why is Royal Historian Archesonus in the High Seat?",a="Archesonus stays in the High Seat because it serves as the center of government for Ironforge and the seat of King Magni Bronzebeard. As the royal historian, she conducts her archival studies alongside the dwarven leadership, where she can advise the throne and commission adventurers to uncover relics and forgotten histories.",al={"why is archesonus in the high seat","archesonus location why","why is royal historian archesonus here"},it="why_here",add="48b31094"},{q="Who is Royal Historian Archesonus tied to?",a="Archesonus is tied directly to King Magni Bronzebeard's royal court in Ironforge. Her scholarly position places her among the monarch's trusted advisers and record-keepers, documenting major catastrophes across the Eastern Kingdoms and seeking physical evidence from ancient ruins like those left by the Dark Iron clan.",al={"archesonus ties","who does archesonus work for","archesonus connections"},it="ties",add="3b340abe"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you share a people whose painful lessons from the War of the Three Hammers remain in Ironforge’s records. Those records are meant to keep the Bronzebeard clan from repeating the Dark Irons’ hubris.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can read Archesonus’s grim account of Lordaeron’s fall. Her works preserve it for southern allies, so they understand the plague and the forces that broke humanity’s northern kingdoms."},kw={"archesonus","high seat","historian","ironforge","lordaeron","royal historian archesonus","thaurissan"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:high-seat","subzone:ruins-of-thaurissan","topic:lordaeron","topic:dwarf"},src={"Royal Historian Archesonus"}}
E["npc:tiza-battleforge"] = {t="npc",n="Tiza Battleforge",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge guides young paladins through the ways of the Holy Light. She teaches virtue, charity, and self-sacrifice, then tests initiates before they may wield its gift of resurrection.",h="In Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge guides young paladins through the ways of the Holy Light.",sec={{t="Mentor of the Mystic Ward",b="Tiza Battleforge guides paladins in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. Tutors across the Alliance send initiates to her for deeper study of the Light. Brandur Ironhammer sends them from Ironforge, Azar Stronghammer from Dun Morogh, and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker from Stormwind.\n\nTiza teaches that the Holy Light asks more than skill in battle. Its servants must offer humble service, show compassion, and stand firm against the Scourge and other threats.",sp=0},{t="The Trials of Divinity",b="Tiza gives young paladins the Tome of Divinity to study. Then she sends them to offer charity, beginning with those in humble need, such as John Turner. Next, she tests their faith and skill by asking them to aid her husband, Muiredon Battleforge, against the Dark Iron dwarves.\n\nThose who pass these trials and use the Symbol of Life to revive fallen allies earn Tiza's trust. Then they may wield the sacred art of resurrection.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza Battleforge is a dwarven paladin of the Knights of the Silver Hand. In Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries, she mentors paladins seeking a deeper bond with the Holy Light.",al={"who is tiza","tiza battleforge lore","paladin trainer tiza"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza is in the Hall of Mysteries, in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, where spiritual and arcane learning are taught.",al={"tiza location","where is tiza battleforge","hall of mysteries paladin trainer"},gp=true},{q="What is the Tome of Divinity she gives to paladins?",a="The Tome of Divinity is a sacred text of the Holy Light's teachings and virtues. Tiza gives it to paladins to study before their trials of charity, courage, and mercy.",al={"tome of divinity tiza","tiza book quest","what is tome of divinity"}},{q="Why does Tiza send paladins to help her husband Muiredon?",a="Tiza sends paladins to aid her husband, Muiredon Battleforge, against Dark Iron dwarves while he assists his companion Narm Faulk. The danger tests their bravery and readiness to use the Symbol of Life to revive fallen comrades.",al={"tiza husband quest","muiredon battleforge connection","why help muiredon"},it="motive"},{q="What ability does Tiza teach worthy paladins?",a="After worthy paladins complete her charity trials and rescue Muiredon's fallen comrade, Tiza teaches them Redemption, the sacred rite of resurrection.",al={"tiza paladin spell","what spell does tiza teach","resurrection paladin trainer ironforge"},gp=true},{q="What is her connection to Brandur Ironhammer?",a="Brandur Ironhammer is a fellow dwarven paladin trainer in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. Tiza once told him his jealousy was a spiritual weakness, and Brandur vowed to overcome it.",al={"tiza and brandur","brandur ironhammer tiza","brandur jealousy"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Tiza Battleforge on?",a="Tiza stands proudly with the Alliance, the kingdom of Ironforge, and the Knights of the Silver Hand. As a devout paladin, her ultimate allegiance is to the Holy Light and the defense of Azeroth against evils such as the Scourge and the treacherous Dark Iron dwarves.",al={"tiza battleforge faction","who does tiza serve","tiza battleforge alliance"},it="side",add="28fe0e8a"},{q="What does Tiza Battleforge want?",a="Tiza seeks to cultivate true virtue, charity, and steadfast faith in novice paladins. Beyond testing their martial might and devotion through sacred trials, she gathers intelligence on local dangers—such as Dark Iron incursions—to warn the city council and keep Ironforge secure.",al={"tiza battleforge goal","what does tiza want","tiza motive"},it="wants",add="5d20b420"},{q="Why is Tiza Battleforge here in the Hall of Mysteries?",a="She resides in the Hall of Mysteries within Ironforge's Mystic Ward to guide aspiring dwarven paladins. Operating at the heart of the city's holy order, she mentors recruits sent by Alliance commanders, testing their selflessness and dedication to the Silver Hand before initiating them into higher mysteries of the Light.",al={"why is tiza in ironforge","tiza battleforge location reason","why is tiza here"},it="why_here",add="075b45b0"},{q="Why is Tiza Battleforge respected among the dwarves?",a="Tiza is known as one of the most respected paladins in Ironforge. Seasoned veterans across the Alliance, from Stormwind's Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker to local paladin trainers, hold her wisdom in high esteem and trust her judgment implicitly to test the moral fiber of new recruits.",al={"tiza battleforge reputation","is tiza battleforge famous","tiza respect"},it="fame",add="90c1fa9e"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a dwarven paladin, you face Tiza Battleforge's tests through the Tome of Divinity. Those who prove worthy may learn to resurrect fallen allies.",["race:Dwarf"]="Tiza shows how deeply the Holy Light and the Silver Hand are rooted in dwarven culture. She guides Khaz Modan's defenders against threats such as the Dark Iron clan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Tiza works with mentors from Stormwind to Kharanos to uphold shared standards of virtue and martial readiness across Alliance lands."},kw={"dwarf","hall of mysteries","ironforge","muiredon battleforge","mystic ward","paladin","redemption","silver hand","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},rel={"subzone:hall-of-mysteries","zone:ironforge","quest:1641","quest:2997","npc:brandur-ironhammer","npc:azar-stronghammer","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},src={"Tiza Battleforge"}}
E["quest:1453"] = {t="quest",n="Reclaimers' Business in Desolace",z="ironforge",s="Roetten Stonehammer sends travelers from Ironforge across the sea to Desolace for paid work with the Reclaimers. At Nijel's Point, Kreldig Ungor needs help recovering lost treasures and relics.",h="Roetten Stonehammer sends travelers from Ironforge across the sea to Desolace for paid work with the...",sec={{t="A Call to the Wasteland",b="Beyond the sea, Desolace is a harsh stretch of Kalimdor ruled by warring centaur clans. The Reclaimers seek profit among its forgotten ruins and barren lands. For those willing to face the danger, the journey may pay well.",sp=0},{t="Nijel's Point and the Reclaimers",b="The route runs west through the Stonetalon Mountains and into northern Desolace. High among the cliffs, Nijel's Point is an Alliance outpost where Kreldig Ungor welcomes new hands. The Reclaimers recover heirlooms, magical artifacts, and family treasures lost across the war-torn world. For the right price, Kreldig and his associates retrieve those valuables from the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Roetten Stonehammer offers paid work in Ironforge and sends you across the sea to meet his associate in Kalimdor.",al={"quest giver","who starts reclaimers business","roetten stonehammer location"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Nijel's Point?",a="Nijel's Point lies in Desolace's northeastern crags. From the Stonetalon Mountains, travel south into Desolace, then follow the cliffs east to the torchlit path climbing to the Alliance outpost.",al={"find nijels point","how to get to nijels point","nijels point location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the Reclaimers?",a="The Reclaimers are a venture led by dwarven operatives such as Kreldig Ungor. For paying clients, they recover lost heirlooms, antiquities, and magical relics from dangerous places.",al={"what are reclaimers","reclaimers faction","reclaimers lore"},it="people"},{q="What threats await in Desolace?",a="Warring centaur tribes, undead remnants, and hostile wildlife threaten travelers in Desolace, an arid wasteland beyond the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"desolace dangers","what is in desolace"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Kreldig Ungor?",a="Kreldig Ungor is a dwarf at Nijel's Point in Desolace. He organizes salvage work and relic hunts across the region, recruiting capable travelers to face its ruins and centaur camps.",al={"kreldig ungor lore","who is kreldig"},it="target"},{q="Is this quest required to quest in Desolace?",a="No. You can travel to Nijel's Point without Roetten Stonehammer, though he offers background and directions before you set out.",al={"do i need this quest","is reclaimers business required"},gp=true},{q="Why does Roetten Stonehammer send you to Desolace?",a="Roetten Stonehammer acts as a liaison for the Reclaimers back in the safety of Ironforge. His associates out at Nijel's Point are facing dangerous ground in Desolace and need steady, capable hands to handle contracts. By steering able adventurers like you toward Kreldig Ungor, Roetten ensures their treasure-hunting outfit stays staffed and profitable despite the hostile centaur lands.",al={"why send to desolace","roetten stonehammer motive","why help kreldig ungor"},it="motive",add="7014e979"},{q="Why does Roetten Stonehammer recruit adventurers instead of going himself?",a="Operating a salvage outfit across continents requires eyes and ears in major cities just as much as muscle in the field. Roetten remains in Ironforge to direct incoming talent and broker opportunities, leaving the grueling trek through the Stonetalon Mountains and the perils of Desolace to hardened travelers ready to risk their necks for coin.",al={"why does roetten need me","why not go himself","why recruit adventurers"},it="why_me",add="f82b8baa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Nijel's Point is the main Alliance sanctuary in the western wastes of central Kalimdor. Hostile centaur clans surround it.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can find dwarven enterprise even in Kalimdor's bleakest corners, from the Explorers' Guild to independent salvage groups like the Reclaimers."},kw={"centaur","desolace","ironforge","kreldig ungor","nijel's point","reclaimers","roetten stonehammer","stonetalon"},rel={"npc:roetten-stonehammer","npc:kreldig-ungor","subzone:nijel-s-point","zone:desolace","zone:stonetalon","topic:centaur"},m={start="Roetten Stonehammer",["end"]="Kreldig Ungor",faction="Alliance",id=1453},src={"Reclaimers' Business in Desolace"}}
E["quest:1645"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge puts the Tome of Divinity into a dwarven paladin's hands. Its teachings begin trials of devotion to the Light and readiness to defend Azeroth from dark forces such as the Scourge.",h="In Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge puts the Tome of Divinity into a dwarven paladin's hands.",sec={{t="A Calling to Virtue",b="From across the eastern kingdoms, promising paladin initiates come to Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries after mastering the martial and spiritual basics. There, young dwarven paladins learn what sets a champion of the Holy Light apart from an ordinary warrior. Taking up this calling means pledging a life to duty, self-sacrifice, and spiritual discipline.",sp=0},{t="The Book of Divinity",b="The novice receives the Book of Divinity as a guide to its duties, virtues, and spiritual teachings. Its words show how sacred power can be wielded against wicked threats. Yet study is only the first step. The initiate must carry those lessons into acts of faith across Khaz Modan and beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Tome of Divinity quest?",a="The Tome of Divinity begins advanced training for dwarven paladins. Tiza Battleforge gives initiates a holy book and sends them on trials to prove their virtue and learn to call fallen allies back from death.",al={"what does tome of divinity do","tome of divinity purpose","why do this quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza Battleforge trains paladins in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. She guides dwarven paladins toward greater virtue, tests their devotion to the Light, and prepares them to face threats such as the Scourge.",al={"tiza battleforge","who is the paladin trainer in ironforge","who gives tome of divinity"},it="identity"},{q="Why must initiates study the Book of Divinity?",a="The Book of Divinity teaches the duties and virtues demanded by the Holy Light. Its teachings prepare initiates for the spiritual discipline needed to wield sacred powers.",al={"what is the book of divinity","why read the book","book of divinity lore"},it="item"},{q="What major threats are dwarven paladins preparing to fight?",a="Dwarven paladins prepare to defend Azeroth from dangers across the land, especially the encroaching undead menace of the Scourge.",al={"who do paladins fight","why train paladins ironforge","paladin purpose"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this training take place?",a="The training begins in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries, in the city's northern quarters. Scholars, priests, mages, and paladins gather there for prayer and study.",al={"where is tiza battleforge","ironforge paladin location","hall of mysteries paladin"},it="place"},{q="What comes next after receiving the book?",a="After reading and reflecting on the Book of Divinity, the initiate faces practical trials from Tiza Battleforge. These call for compassion, duty, and sacrifice beyond the city gates.",al={"what happens next","next quest tome of divinity","where do i go after getting the book"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tiza Battleforge want you to study the Tome of Divinity?",a="Tiza Battleforge oversees the training of paladins within Ironforge. She views it as her solemn duty to guide initiates toward true virtue and devotion to the Holy Light. With the looming menace of the Scourge and other perils threatening Azeroth, she seeks to ensure that every defender she trains understands their spiritual responsibilities and is prepared to wield greater holy powers in defense of the realm.",al={"why does tiza want this done","tiza battleforge motive","why study tome of divinity"},it="motive",add="b6d4c081"},{q="Why does Tiza Battleforge ask you to undertake this trial instead of handling it herself?",a="Tiza cannot walk the path of virtue for you. As an instructor of the Holy Light, her responsibility is to guide and teach, but the devotion, understanding, and inner strength required of a true paladin must come from within the initiate. To earn the blessings and abilities of the Light, you must personally prove your capability and dedication through study and service.",al={"why me tome of divinity","why doesn't tiza do it","why must i study the tome"},it="why_me",add="a71115f0"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, this rite carries you from martial training into the deeper virtues of the Holy Light, toward powers of redemption and resurrection.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, taking up the Tome of Divinity strengthens the bond of faith between the Bronzebeard kingdom and the human knights of the Silver Hand."},kw={"book of divinity","hall of mysteries","holy light","ironforge","paladin","redemption","scourge","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:tiza-battleforge","zone:ironforge","topic:light","topic:scourge"},m={start="Tiza Battleforge",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1645},src={"The Tome of Divinity (dwarf 1)"}}
E["quest:1679"] = {t="quest",n="Muren Stormpike",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Muren Stormpike awaits warriors sent from Kharanos for formal training. Granis Swiftaxe sends recruits who have proved their mettle in Dun Morogh to the city's Military Ward.",h="In Ironforge, Muren Stormpike awaits warriors sent from Kharanos for formal training.",sec={{t="A Summons to Ironforge",b="Granis Swiftaxe sends promising warriors from Kharanos to Ironforge after they face local threats in Dun Morogh. He knows rough skirmishes can teach only so much. In the Military Ward, senior fighters oversee formal training for those bound for battle.",sp=0},{t="The Master of Arms",b="At the Hall of Arms, you meet Muren Stormpike, a veteran of a storied dwarven clan. He wants proof that his new charges can endure real combat, not tavern tales. Reporting to him opens the way to learn defensive arts, control an enemy's aggression, and earn iron arms for the front line.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find Muren Stormpike?",a="Granis Swiftaxe, the warrior trainer in Kharanos, sends you after you prove your basic fighting skill in Dun Morogh.",al={"who gives muren stormpike quest","where do i get muren stormpike","quest giver muren stormpike"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Muren Stormpike located?",a="Muren Stormpike is in the Hall of Arms, in the Military Ward on Ironforge's eastern side.",al={"where is muren stormpike","muren stormpike location","how to find muren"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this quest important for warriors?",a="Reporting to Muren begins advanced warrior training. It leads to instruction in Defensive Stance and Taunt, along with a reliable early weapon.",al={"what does muren stormpike unlock","why do muren stormpike","muren stormpike rewards"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Muren Stormpike?",a="Muren Stormpike is a veteran combat instructor in Ironforge and a member of the Stormpike clan, a renowned dwarven family of warriors and expeditionary engineers.",al={"who is muren","muren stormpike lore","is muren stormpike clan"},it="identity"},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. Only warrior novices ready for specialized martial training can take it.",al={"can non warriors do muren stormpike","is muren stormpike warrior only","muren stormpike classes"},gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Muren?",a="After you speak with Muren, he tests your resolve by sending you into a combat trial against Vejrek.",al={"what is next after muren stormpike","next quest after muren stormpike","vejrek quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Granis Swiftaxe send you to Muren Stormpike?",a="Granis Swiftaxe sees real promise in your fighting ability, but Kharanos can only offer you the basics. To advance your martial training and learn what it truly means to be a warrior, he refers you to Muren Stormpike, a seasoned veteran stationed at the Hall of Arms in Ironforge.",al={"granis swiftaxe motive","why send to muren","why speak to muren stormpike"},it="motive",add="61377fd6"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, this summons marks your passage from recruit to disciplined soldier, ready to hold the line and protect allies.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf fighter, reporting to the Hall of Arms connects you with the martial traditions and tactical discipline of the mountain clans.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnomish warrior, you rely on Ironforge's Hall of Arms to learn traditional heavy frontline combat after the fall of Gnomeregan drove your people to Dun Morogh."},kw={"defensive stance","granis swiftaxe","hall of arms","ironforge","kharanos","military ward","muren stormpike","warrior trainer"},rel={"npc:granis-swiftaxe","zone:ironforge","subzone:military-ward","subzone:kharanos","zone:dunmorogh","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Granis Swiftaxe",["end"]="Muren Stormpike",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1679},src={"Muren Stormpike (quest)"}}
E["quest:1704"] = {t="quest",n="Klockmort Spannerspan",z="ironforge",s="In Tinkertown, Furen Longbeard's fire-hardened mail findings reach Klockmort Spannerspan. The dwarf smith trusts his gnomish colleague to discover what the new techniques can do.",h="In Tinkertown, Furen Longbeard's fire-hardened mail findings reach Klockmort Spannerspan.",sec={{t="A Colleague in Tinkertown",b="You carry Furen's notes from Stormwind to Ironforge, then on to Tinkertown. There, Klockmort Spannerspan works as a blacksmith and can test the discoveries in his own craft.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Excitement",b="Gnomish blacksmiths are rare among their dwarven hosts. Klockmort is eager to move beyond traditional metalwork, and the notes excite him with the promise of a breakthrough. He is ready to try the fiery techniques in his own unusual projects.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Klockmort Spannerspan?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan is a gnomish blacksmith in Tinkertown, within Ironforge. He works with dwarven smiths such as Furen Longbeard on metalworking techniques.",al={"klockmort spannerspan","who is klockmort","gnome blacksmith ironforge"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Furen Longbeard send you to Klockmort?",a="Furen Longbeard writes down what he discovers while crafting fire-hardened mail. He sends you to Klockmort because the gnome is keen to invent and can experiment with Furen's findings.",al={"why deliver notes","furen's notes","furen longbeard klockmort"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Klockmort Spannerspan?",a="You can find Klockmort Spannerspan in Tinkertown, the gnome district in eastern Ironforge. He works among its workbenches and machinery.",al={"klockmort location","where is klockmort","klockmort ironforge"},gp=true},{q="What happens after giving Klockmort the notes?",a="Furen's breakthrough excites Klockmort, and he begins planning his own metalworking projects. He sends you to gather unusual materials such as iron coral.",al={"quest continuation","what next after klockmort","iron coral quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest limited to warriors?",a="Yes. This delivery is part of an armor-crafting chain for Alliance warriors training under veteran weapon and armor masters.",al={"warrior only","can anyone do this quest","class requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why does Klockmort say he cannot tell day from night?",a="Ironforge lies beneath the mountains of Dun Morogh. In Tinkertown, stone vaults and glowing lamps keep craftsmen from seeing the sun or sky.",al={"klockmort day night dialogue","way down here dialogue"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you follow a path toward durable battle gear, from dwarven hearths to gnomish invention. You earn the attention of Tinkertown's finest.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you see Klockmort bring dwarven metalworking together with gnomish experimentation in Tinkertown.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you carry Furen's notes in an exchange of advanced smithing techniques among Ironforge's master artisans."},kw={"blacksmith","fire hardened","furen","ironforge","klockmort","longbeard","notes","spannerspan","tinkertown"},rel={"quest:1701","quest:1708","npc:furen-longbeard","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Furen Longbeard",["end"]="Klockmort Spannerspan",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1704},src={"Klockmort Spannerspan (quest)"}}
E["quest:1708"] = {t="quest",n="Iron Coral",z="ironforge",s="In Tinker Town, Klockmort Spannerspan seeks searing coral for a new suit of armor. The gnome blacksmith hopes to test new smithing methods with this rare sea material on the Wetlands coast.",h="In Tinker Town, Klockmort Spannerspan seeks searing coral for a new suit of armor.",sec={{t="A Fusion of Crafts",b="Klockmort Spannerspan has shared discoveries with Furen Longbeard, a master dwarven smith. Now he hopes to unite Furen's skill in metallurgy with his own tinkering. Mountain ore alone will not give him the resilient armor he seeks. So he needs searing coral, a material hardened by the sea.",sp=0},{t="Diving the Wetlands Shore",b="Searing coral grows underwater off the Wetlands coast, south of Menethil Harbor. You need to bring back twenty clusters while aquatic predators prowl below. Then carry the harvest to Ironforge. Klockmort plans to smelt and hammer the coral into experimental armor plating.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Klockmort Spannerspan?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan is a skilled gnome blacksmith in Tinker Town, Ironforge. He loves mechanical tinkering and new approaches to metallurgy, and works with dwarven artisans on armor-making methods.",al={"klockmort","who gives iron coral","quest giver iron coral"},it="identity"},{q="What is searing coral?",a="Searing coral is a rare ocean growth on the seabed south of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. An inventive smith can smelt and hammer it into armor reinforcement because of its unusual chemical and physical qualities.",al={"searing coral lore","what is searing coral used for"},it="item"},{q="Where do I find the searing coral?",a="Search underwater along the Wetlands coast south of Menethil Harbor. Divers must pry the mineral-rich branches loose from the seabed.",al={"searing coral location","where is iron coral located","wetlands coral location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Klockmort need searing coral instead of metal ore?",a="Klockmort hopes searing coral will make armor lighter and more durable than armor made from Ironforge ore alone. He is adapting smithing techniques learned from the dwarf Furen Longbeard.",al={"why coral for armor","coral metallurgy"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How is Furen Longbeard involved in this task?",a="Furen Longbeard developed new armor-crafting techniques with your help. Grateful for your aid, he shared his trade secrets with Klockmort, inspiring the gnome's protective designs.",al={"furen connection","furen longbeard iron coral"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after bringing the coral to Klockmort?",a="With twenty loads of searing coral, Klockmort begins smelting and hammering it at his workbench. His work leads to experimental gear in Klockmort's Creation.",al={"iron coral follow up","next quest iron coral"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Klockmort Spannerspan want the searing coral collected?",a="Klockmort is an enthusiastic gnome inventor eager to experiment. Having learned innovative smithing techniques from Furen Longbeard, he wants to combine Furen's methods with his own engineering know-how to forge an exceptionally tough suit of armor. To craft it, he specifically requires the unique properties of searing coral harvested from the Wetlands coast.",al={"why does klockmort want coral","klockmort motive iron coral","why make iron coral armor"},it="motive",add="f5cb4716"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Klockmort's search for strange coastal minerals as a way to improve traditional craft through experiment.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see master smith Furen Longbeard's metallurgic discoveries at work in this collaboration between gnomes and dwarves in Tinker Town.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can appreciate Klockmort's attempt to smelt an ocean deposit into hardened armor plating.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can recognize the value of testing unusual materials to make better protection."},kw={"armor smelting","furen longbeard","iron coral","ironforge","klockmort spannerspan","menethil harbor","searing coral","tinker town","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1704","quest:1709","npc:furen-longbeard","zone:ironforge","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor"},m={start="Klockmort Spannerspan",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=1708,ri={"Searing Coral"}},src={"Iron Coral (quest)"}}
E["quest:1709"] = {t="quest",n="Klockmort's Creation",z="ironforge",s="In Tinker Town, Klockmort Spannerspan puts Furen Longbeard's forging method to work on rare materials. The result is armor made to endure.",h="In Tinker Town, Klockmort Spannerspan puts Furen Longbeard's forging method to work on rare materials.",sec={{t="A Fusion of Disciplines",b="Using Furen Longbeard's methods, Klockmort finishes a pair of armored gauntlets in Tinker Town. Dwarven metalworking and gnomish mechanical skill come together in gauntlets built to endure punishment that would crush ordinary steel.",sp=0},{t="Unrivaled Resilience",b="Klockmort says a siege engine could run over the armor without leaving lasting distortion. Peculiarly treated rare components give it resilience. Dwarven forging and gnomish ingenuity join in armor built to withstand the fiercest frontline battles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Klockmort Spannerspan?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan is a skilled gnome blacksmith in Tinker Town, Ironforge. He lends his hand to intricate mechanical work and joins dwarven craftsmen such as Furen Longbeard to make unusual, durable gear.",al={"klockmort","who is klockmort","gnome in tinker town"},it="identity"},{q="Who designed the process to make this armor?",a="Furen Longbeard, an accomplished dwarven armorsmith, devised the forging process. Klockmort followed Furen's exact methods to treat the materials and finish the armor.",al={"who made the process","furen longbeard armor","furen method"},it="origin"},{q="Why did a gnome blacksmith make this armor?",a="Klockmort wanted to try Furen Longbeard's new technique on armor of his own. Since you had helped Furen, Klockmort offered you the finished armor in return for gathering the searing coral he needed.",al={"why a gnome","gnome blacksmithing","engineering armor"},it="purpose"},{q="What makes this armor special compared to standard plate?",a="Klockmort says the finished armor combines remarkable spring and elasticity with rigid durability. He claims that even if a heavy siege engine flattened it, the metal would snap back into its original shape.",al={"how strong is it","siege engine armor","armor durability"},it="power"},{q="Where does this armor fit in the path of a warrior's training?",a="The armor belongs to a series of tasks for promising Alliance warriors seeking resilient gear custom-forged by Ironforge's finest minds.",al={"warrior quest armor","why do this quest","warrior reward"}},{q="Where is Klockmort found?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan works among the workshops, clanking gears, and steam vents of Tinker Town, Ironforge's gnomish quarter.",al={"klockmort location","where is spannerspan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Klockmort Spannerspan helping make this armor?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan took on the task to test Furen Longbeard's radical crafting theory. Dwarven smithing rarely relies on precision gnomish engineering, so assembling the gauntlets offered Klockmort a chance to prove that combining Furen's methods with gnomish mechanics could produce a suit resilient enough to survive even a siege engine.",al={"why does klockmort help","klockmort spannerspan motive","why is klockmort forging this"},it="motive",add="fd9fc5fd"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you reach an important milestone with these gauntlets, custom-tempered to endure the crushing blows of frontline combat.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you see how your people's ingenuity aids heavy armor making, joining mechanical precision with dwarven craft.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you see the value of testing unconventional tempering methods with rare materials from the sea."},kw={"furen longbeard","iron coral","ironforge","klockmort","siege engine","spannerspan","tinker town","warrior armor"},rel={"quest:1708","quest:1704"},m={start="Klockmort Spannerspan",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1709},src={"Klockmort's Creation"}}
E["quest:1715"] = {t="quest",n="The Slaughtered Lamb",z="ironforge",s="Gnome warlocks from Ironforge now seek their training in Stormwind. The Slaughtered Lamb gives them a place to learn from human warlocks, while King Magni Bronzebeard keeps watch over dark practitioners at home.",h="Gnome warlocks from Ironforge now seek their training in Stormwind.",sec={{t="Exile and Scrutiny",b="Before Gnomeregan fell, Khaz Modan's aspiring warlocks studied with tinker-mages and demonic scholars in the techno-city. Then disaster scattered those schools and drove the gnomes into exile. The survivors crowded into Ironforge's underground caverns, where King Magni Bronzebeard and the dwarven guard watch them. They cannot openly practice demonic arts or perform dangerous rituals, so senior instructors like Lago Blackwrench send students away.",sp=0},{t="The Mage Quarter's Secret Cellar",b="From Ironforge, gnome students travel south to the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. Twisting stone passages and stairs descend from the tavern's taproom to a hidden sanctum where human warlocks gather. Gakin the Darkbinder oversees them there. In its shadowed rooms, instructors can teach novices to summon and bind minor demons without drawing the city marshals' immediate anger.",sp=0},{t="Growing Strain in the Shadows",b="Stormwind's coven welcomes capable hands, though refugee novices bring new strain. Human mentors already risk discovery by the city's paladins and authorities. As more practitioners arrive from Khaz Modan, Gakin and his colleagues find their sanctuary growing crowded. The steady flow from the dwarven mountain could expose their hidden gathering. Yet neither the gnomes nor the human warlocks have an easier choice.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't gnome warlocks train in Ironforge?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard watches warlocks closely in Ironforge. Since Gnomeregan fell, displaced practitioners have no private academy, and summoning demons in the dwarven mountain risks discovery.",al={"why send to stormwind","ironforge warlock training","why gnomeregan warlock leave"},it="why_here"},{q="Where were Khaz Modan warlocks trained before?",a="Before Gnomeregan fell, Khaz Modan warlocks trained with tinker-mages and demonic scholars in the techno-city. The disaster scattered those schools and sent survivors into exile.",al={"gnomeregan warlock history","past warlock training khaz modan"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Gakin the Darkbinder?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder is a human warlock who oversees the hidden sanctum beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind. He teaches apprentices, including gnome novices from Ironforge, to summon and bind demons.",al={"who is gakin","gakin role"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Slaughtered Lamb?",a="The Slaughtered Lamb is a tavern in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. Its cellar hides a gathering place for warlocks, out of the city authorities' sight.",al={"slaughtered lamb tavern","where is slaughtered lamb"},it="place"},{q="Why is Gakin frustrated with the newcomers?",a="Gakin fears that an influx of refugee gnomes will draw attention to Stormwind's hidden coven. Space and teachers are limited, and too much warlock activity could expose them to the authorities.",al={"gakin complaining","why is gakin mad"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Lago Blackwrench?",a="Lago Blackwrench is a gnome warlock trainer who lives in Ironforge's dark alleys. He sends promising novices to Stormwind to continue their training.",al={"lago blackwrench","quest giver slaughtered lamb"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lago Blackwrench send you to Stormwind?",a="Lago Blackwrench has no choice if you are to advance your demonic craft. Ever since the fall of Gnomeregan drove gnome practitioners into Ironforge, King Magni Bronzebeard has kept a watchful, suspicious eye on dark magic within his mountain stronghold. Unable to operate their own proper training sanctums under dwarven surveillance, Ironforge's exiled warlocks are forced to swallow their pride and dispatch promising novices south to human masters.",al={"why send to stormwind","blackwrench motive","why go to slaughter lamb"},it="motive",add="2a96a15b"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="For young Alliance warlocks, the journey carries them into a hidden network of practitioners across racial lines.",["race:Gnome"]="In exile, gnomes crowd into Ironforge and depend on human hospitality after losing their academies in Gnomeregan.",["race:Dwarf"]="Ironforge's authorities watch demonic practice closely. Dwarf warlocks keep to the shadows and send their students elsewhere."},kw={"gakin the darkbinder","gnomeregan","ironforge","lago blackwrench","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","warlock"},rel={"subzone:slaughtered-lamb","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:ironforge","zone:gnomeregan","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Lago Blackwrench",["end"]="Gakin the Darkbinder",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1715},src={"The Slaughtered Lamb (quest)"}}
E["quest:1717"] = {t="quest",n="Gakin's Summons",z="ironforge",s="From Ironforge, Gakin's Summons sends promising Alliance warlocks south to Stormwind. Beneath the Mage Quarter, Gakin the Darkbinder awaits to oversee their progress in commanding greater fiends.",h="From Ironforge, Gakin's Summons sends promising Alliance warlocks south to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Message from the Underground",b="Demonology stays hidden across Alliance lands. In Ironforge, Lago Blackwrench quietly watches wandering practitioners for the brotherhood in Stormwind. When a warlock masters their first minions, word travels quickly. Lago sends word to leave the snowy mountains of Khaz Modan and report south without delay.",sp=0},{t="Return to the Slaughtered Lamb",b="Beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Gakin the Darkbinder coordinates the city's warlocks. He sees every capable student as a valuable but hazardous investment. His summons marks the threshold of true demonic binding. Now begin the trials to subjugate a succubus from the Twisting Nether.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me this summons?",a="Lago Blackwrench, a warlock trainer in Ironforge, delivers the summons on behalf of Gakin the Darkbinder, who leads demonology instruction in Stormwind.",al={"who gives quest","who starts this","lago blackwrench"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Gakin the Darkbinder?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder lives in the dark, winding catacombs beneath The Slaughtered Lamb, a tavern in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"gakin location","where is gakin","slaughtered lamb location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Gakin summoning me?",a="You have advanced far enough in your craft to undertake the rituals that summon and subjugate a succubus, adding to your demonic arsenal.",al={"quest purpose","what is this for","why summoned"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after I speak to Gakin?",a="After you speak to Gakin, he sends you on Devourer of Souls. You will travel into dangerous lands to gather the ritual components needed to conjure and bind a succubus.",al={"next step","what follows this","quest chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is a warlock in Ironforge taking orders from Stormwind?",a="Alliance warlocks keep a discreet network out of necessity. Ironforge and Stormwind practitioners stay in contact and direct promising apprentices to Gakin, who has specialized ritual equipment and lore beneath The Slaughtered Lamb.",al={"ironforge warlocks","gnome warlocks stormwind","warlock organization"},it="ties"},{q="Can I ignore this summons if I want to stay in Khaz Modan?",a="You can delay your visit to Stormwind, but learning to summon a succubus requires completing Gakin's trial. The journey is essential for any aspiring warlock.",al={"is this required","can i skip","do i need to go to stormwind"},gp=true},{q="Why does Lago Blackwrench send you to Stormwind?",a="Lago Blackwrench has explicit instructions from fellow practitioners in Stormwind to watch for promising warlocks traveling through Ironforge. The coven has already invested considerable time and resources into your dark arts, and Lago wants to ensure you do not wander astray or perish before advancing your craft under Gakin the Darkbinder's tutelage.",al={"why does lago want this done","lago blackwrench motive","why does lago send me to stormwind"},it="motive",add="27281f2a"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you are sent from Ironforge back to Stormwind to begin the multi-part ritual that binds your succubus minion.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how the covert warlock network keeps in touch across its capitals while demonology stays hidden from civilian eyes.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome warlock training under Lago Blackwrench in Ironforge, you are sent to Stormwind's underground network for deeper demonic teachings."},kw={"gakin","gakin's summons","ironforge","lago blackwrench","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","succubus","warlock"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1472","quest:1471","quest:1738","subzone:mage-quarter","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:1685"},m={start="Lago Blackwrench",["end"]="Gakin the Darkbinder",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1717},src={"Gakin's Summons (Succubus)"}}
E["quest:1793"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Valor",z="ironforge",s="In Stormwind and Ironforge, young Alliance paladins face a trial of courage and duty. Their mentors ask them to prove they can fight with skill and protect the innocent.",h="In Stormwind and Ironforge, young Alliance paladins face a trial of courage and duty.",sec={{t="The Measure of a Paladin",b="Young paladins in Stormwind and Ironforge must face terrible danger without faltering. Their instructors test their resolve in the Cathedral of Light and the Hall of Mysteries. Dragons and demons may threaten those who cannot defend themselves. The paladins must stay beside them.",sp=0},{t="Virtues of the Order",b="A holy warrior needs bravery as much as a weapon and shield. The trial teaches paladins that strength means little without a firm vow to shelter the helpless. When danger threatens the Alliance, its defenders must hold their ground and protect those in their care.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Tome of Valor?",a="The Tome of Valor tests whether an Alliance paladin has the courage and selfless resolve to protect the vulnerable. Mentors of the Holy Light use the trial to judge an initiate's readiness to advance in the order.",al={"what is tome of valor","tome of valor purpose","why do tome of valor"},it="purpose"},{q="Who directs paladins on this trial?",a="Senior paladins in Alliance capitals guide initiates through the trial. Duthorian Rall calls them from the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind, while Tiza Battleforge does so from Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries.",al={"who gives tome of valor","tome of valor questgiver","who starts tome of valor"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where does this trial lead?",a="The initial call leads into a series of trials that test a paladin's resolve. They take the initiate into danger in defense of the realm and the innocent.",al={"what comes after tome of valor","tome of valor follow up","tome of valor quest chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is bravery so heavily emphasized for paladins?",a="Bravery helps a paladin keep faith and protect others when horrors such as demons or dragons threaten. Without courage, fear can break a warrior's spirit.",al={"why valor","why courage matters to paladins"},it="history"},{q="Do dwarf and human paladins undertake the same test?",a="Human paladins train through Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, while dwarves train in Ironforge. Both traditions teach courage, duty, and defense of the helpless under the Light.",al={"is it different for dwarfs","ironforge tome of valor","stormwind tome of valor"},it="people"},{q="What core lessons are outlined in the trial?",a="The trial teaches paladins to face danger with courage, shield the weak, and keep faith when terror comes.",al={"tome of valor lessons","what does the tome teach"}},{q="Why do the paladin masters want you to take this trial?",a="Times are growing increasingly perilous across Azeroth, threatened by looming evils like demons and dragons. While you have already proven that the Holy Light answers your call, Duthorian Rall and Tiza Battleforge know that raw faith alone is not enough. They need to test the mettle beneath your flesh to ensure you possess the unwavering bravery required of a true paladin before greater perils strike your homeland.",al={"why take trial","duthorian rall motive","tiza battleforge trial why"},it="motive",add="81822402"},{q="Why must you undertake this trial instead of senior paladins or guards?",a="This journey is not an errand of defense that city guards or veteran knights can handle for you. It is a personal rite of passage. The masters must see how your own spirit holds up when faced with hardship, testing your personal capacity to protect the weak, hold onto your faith, and stand firm in the face of terror.",al={"why me tome of valor","why send player valor","why cant guards do it"},it="why_me",add="f91e68e3"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a rite that asks you to put duty to others ahead of your own safety as you become a trusted defender of the Holy Light.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you face this trial under Duthorian Rall's watch in the Cathedral of Light. It carries Stormwind's devotion to the Silver Hand's founding ideals.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you train in Ironforge, where mentors like Tiza Battleforge ask you to show that your fortitude is guided by holy purpose.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you prepare to defend settlements against threats ranging from local bandits to monstrous invaders."},kw={"cathedral of light","duthorian rall","holy light","ironforge","paladin trial","silver hand","tiza battleforge","tome of valor"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:light"},m={start="Duthorian Rall (Stormwind City), Tiza Battleforge (Ironforge)",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1793},src={"The Tome of Valor"}}
E["quest:1802"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of the Cabal",z="ironforge",s="From Ironforge, your search for the Tome of the Cabal leads to a lost manuscript and a sunken ship. Its scattered pages hold rites for binding a felhunter.",h="From Ironforge, your search for the Tome of the Cabal leads to a lost manuscript and a sunken ship.",sec={{t="A Divided Grimoire",b="Only one copy of the Tome of the Cabal was ever written. Violence tore it apart and defaced its pages, sending the remnants to distant corners of the world. A tattered manuscript crossed the sea to Kalimdor, where centaur clans took it. The other half sailed from Lordaeron toward Khaz Modan, but the vessel sank before reaching port.",sp=0},{t="Across Sea and Canyon",b="Two dangers guard the missing pages. Those lost at sea washed ashore on the Hillsbrad coast, west of Southshore. Shoreline murlocs near Azurelode Mine took the waterlogged relics and wreckage. The dry half rests in an ancient chest deep in the centaur caverns of Splithoof Hold in Thousand Needles. Once the pieces are together, Krom Stoutarm can inspect the lost text before it returns to Strahad Farsan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of the Cabal?",a="The Tome of the Cabal is a rare demonic grimoire, and only one copy exists. Its arcane knowledge holds the incantations and binding rites warlocks need to summon and subdue a felhunter from the Twisting Nether.",al={"tome of the cabal lore","what is this book","tome cabal"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Krom Stoutarm and why does he want the tome?",a="Krom Stoutarm is an Ironforge dwarf who studies rare and forgotten texts. He tells Alliance warlocks where the tome's pieces ended up, asking only to study them once they are recovered.",al={"who is krom stoutarm","why does krom want the book","krom stoutarm ironforge"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the two pieces of the book end up?",a="The Moldy Tome washed ashore on the Hillsbrad coast, west of Southshore near Azurelode Mine, where coastal murlocs scavenged it. The Tattered Manuscript lies in a battered chest deep in a centaur cavern at Splithoof Hold in Thousand Needles, Kalimdor.",al={"where are the tome pieces","book locations","tattered manuscript location"},it="place"},{q="Why was the tome torn apart in the first place?",a="Only one copy of the Tome of the Cabal was ever transcribed. In its murky past, someone deliberately defaced it, tore a large section from the binding, and carried it to Kalimdor. The rest was lost at sea on a voyage to Menethil Harbor.",al={"why was the book ripped","who vandalized the tome"},it="history"},{q="Who is Strahad Farsan and what does he have to do with this quest?",a="Strahad Farsan is an experienced warlock who lives near Ratchet in the Barrens. He directs aspiring summoners to recover the tome and learn the rites for summoning and binding a felhunter under his tutelage.",al={"who is strahad","strahad farsan","strahad connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why is the Moldy Tome covered in sea grime?",a="The Moldy Tome was aboard a ship sailing from the Lordaeron coast to Menethil Harbor, but the ship never arrived. Its wreck drifted near the Hillsbrad shore, where coastal murlocs near Azurelode Mine gathered the damp, moldy pages.",al={"why is moldy tome wet","hillsbrad tome murlocs"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Moldy Tome?",a="The Moldy Tome represents the waterlogged remains of the primary binding of the Tome of the Cabal. It was lost at sea off the coast of Hillsbrad Foothills when a transport ship sailing toward Menethil Harbor sank. Reclaiming it recovers the core of the grimoire's sinister teachings.",al={"moldy tome","what is the moldy tome","why find moldy tome"},it="item",add="7c4e226c"},{q="What is the Tattered Manuscript?",a="The Tattered Manuscript is the section torn from the original Tome of the Cabal before the book was lost. Carried far across the sea, it ended up in the hands of the Galak centaur within Thousand Needles, containing the missing rites needed to assemble the complete text.",al={"tattered manuscript","what is the tattered manuscript","centaur manuscript"},it="item",add="aa350fa4"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, recovering the grimoire's torn halves marks a rite of passage. Its pages hold the summoning rites needed to draw a felhunter from the Nether and enslave it.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance practitioner, you can rely on Ironforge contacts such as Krom Stoutarm to trace rare demonic relics across continents without drawing open suspicion from church or crown."},kw={"azurelode mine","felhunter","ironforge","krom stoutarm","moldy tome","splithoof hold","strahad farsan","tattered manuscript","tome of the cabal"},rel={"npc:krom-stoutarm","quest:1758","quest:1471","quest:1798","subzone:splithoof-hold","subzone:azurelode-mine","zone:thousandneedles","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Krom Stoutarm",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1802,ri={"Moldy Tome","Tattered Manuscript"}},src={"Tome of the Cabal (Alliance, 2)"}}
E["quest:2039"] = {t="quest",n="Find Bingles",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Gnoarn starts a search for Find Bingles after more than a week without word. Bingles Blastenheimer vanished during a flight toward fallen Gnomeregan, and searchers are sent to Loch Modan's shores. There, Bingles is alive and needs mechanical salvage.",h="In Ironforge, Gnoarn starts a search for Find Bingles after more than a week without word.",sec={{t="A Missing Pilot",b="Gnome aviator Bingles Blastenheimer was sent from Tinker Town in Ironforge to scout the irradiated ruins of Gnomeregan from the air. More than a week has passed without word. Gnoarn fears Bingles may have blown himself out of the sky, a danger of gnome engineering. His last report placed him somewhere above Loch Modan's waters.",sp=0},{t="Down at the Loch",b="Searchers find Bingles alive along the Loch Modan shoreline, far from a tragic pile of wreckage. He is unfazed by his long absence and takes slight offense that anyone doubted his piloting. Rather than return promptly to report to Gnoarn, he asks his rescuer to recover tools and Blastencapper explosives stolen by troggs. He wants them so he can resume his duties for the gnomish movement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bingles Blastenheimer?",a="Bingles Blastenheimer is an eccentric gnomish aviator and mechanic. He was sent to scout fallen Gnomeregan from the air, then crashed near Loch Modan.",al={"who is bingles","bingles blastenheimer lore","who is the pilot"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Bingles flying over Gnomeregan?",a="After Gnomeregan fell to troggs and radiation, gnomish leaders and tinkerers kept watch over it. Bingles flew above the city to scout enemy positions and conditions as part of the effort to reclaim their home.",al={"bingles mission","why was bingles flying","gnomeregan recon"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Bingles located?",a="Bingles is along Loch Modan's southeastern shore, trying to sort out his downed flying machine.",al={"where is bingles","find bingles location","where to find bingles"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Gnoarn?",a="Gnoarn is a gnome coordinator in Tinker Town, Ironforge. He tracks gnomish personnel and missions, and begins the search when Bingles fails to return on schedule.",al={"who is gnoarn","quest giver gnoarn"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after finding Bingles?",a="After Bingles is found, adventurers can recover his wrench, screwdriver, hammer, and Blastencapper explosives from troggs on the Loch's islands.",al={"what next after find bingles","wing nut quest","bingles follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Bingles hurt from the crash?",a="Bingles is unharmed, though his pride is ruffled because Gnoarn doubted his flying skills. He is focused on recovering the tools and explosives the troggs stole from him.",al={"is bingles injured","did bingles die"}},{q="Why does Gnoarn want Bingles found?",a="Bingles was sent on a critical reconnaissance flight over fallen Gnomeregan and has failed to report back for more than a week. Given the erratic nature of gnome machinery and Bingles's knack for disaster, Gnoarn fears the pilot has blown himself up somewhere in the wilderness. He needs someone to search the region near Loch Modan, where Bingles was last spotted, to determine his fate.",al={"why find bingles","gnoarn motive","why send to look for bingles"},it="motive",add="b67b7bf8"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, recovering Bingles helps sustain hope for retaking Gnomeregan, where every scout and flying machine counts.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know the hazards of gnomish aviation, where a lost wing nut or an engine blast is part of field work.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout, you help bridge the communications gap between Ironforge's halls and field operations across Loch Modan."},kw={"bingles","blastenheimer","flying machine","gnoarn","gnomeregan","ironforge","loch modan","reconnaissance","tinker town"},rel={"npc:bingles-blastenheimer","npc:gnoarn","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:gnomeregan"},m={start="Gnoarn",["end"]="Bingles Blastenheimer",faction="Alliance",id=2039},src={"Find Bingles"}}
E["quest:2041"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Shoni",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Alliance travelers are sent to Stormwind to find Shoni the Shilent, whose unit prepares for Gnomeregan.",h="In Ironforge, Alliance travelers are sent to Stormwind to find Shoni the Shilent, whose unit prepares for...",sec={{t="A Call from Tinkertown",b="After Gnomeregan fell to radiation, surviving gnomes made an exile quarter in Ironforge. Its engineers, tinkers, and strategists keep seeking a way back into their lost home. Tinkertown directs the effort, but the preparations reach beyond Khaz Modan. Now adventurers are sent south to Stormwind, where military gear for fighting underground is being prepared.",sp=0},{t="Subterranean Ambitions",b="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Shoni the Shilent commands an elite crew trained for underground assault. Her sappers need gyrodrillmatic excavationators to burrow toward the sectors held by troggs. The Deeprun Tram runs beneath the mountains between Ironforge and Stormwind, making the journey to Shoni straightforward.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shoni the Shilent?",a="Shoni the Shilent is a gnomish officer in Stormwind City. She commands an underground assault unit that builds and deploys heavy excavation gear to help retake Gnomeregan.",al={"who is shoni","shoni the shilent","who is the npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Shoni the Shilent?",a="Shoni is in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, near the blacksmithing trainers and forges, just steps from the Deeprun Tram terminal.",al={"where is shoni","shoni location","shoni coordinates"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do I get to Stormwind from Ironforge?",a="The fastest way from Ironforge to Stormwind is the Deeprun Tram on the northeastern side of Tinkertown. It carries travelers beneath the mountains straight to Stormwind's Dwarven District.",al={"travel to stormwind","ironforge to stormwind","how to reach stormwind"},gp=true},{q="What does Shoni need help with?",a="Shoni is outfitting an underground assault crew and needs components for her gyrodrillmatic excavationators. The effort eventually sends adventurers to Westfall and the Deadmines.",al={"shoni quest goal","what does shoni want"},it="purpose"},{q="Is this quest required to get Underground Assault?",a="No. This is an optional lead. You can go straight to the Dwarven District in Stormwind and speak with Shoni to take up Underground Assault.",al={"is speak with shoni mandatory","can i skip to shoni"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="How does this connect to Gnomeregan?",a="Gnomish leaders are gathering forces and excavation technology to breach Gnomeregan's defenses. Shoni's team is developing the underground drills needed to break into the contaminated city.",al={"why gnomeregan","gnome connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why does the quest giver send you to Shoni the Shilent?",a="The gnomes are fighting an uphill battle to reclaim their fallen home of Gnomeregan. Shoni the Shilent commands an underground assault crew preparing specialized gyrodrillmatic excavationators for the war effort, but her operations in Stormwind lack hands. Central command in Ironforge needs able adventurers willing to travel south and bolster her critical engineering project before their offensive can advance.",al={"why speak with shoni","why send to shoni","why visit shoni"},it="motive",add="3fdd7df6"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome in Ironforge, you can help reclaim your irradiated home by following Shoni's orders and joining the effort to retake Gnomeregan.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see that Shoni's project calls for gyrodrillmatic excavationators, complex gnomish machines built for deep-earth tunneling.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can use the Deeprun Tram to move personnel between Ironforge and Stormwind."},kw={"deeprun tram","dwarven district","gnomeregan","gyrodrillmatic excavationator","ironforge","shoni the shilent","stormwind","tinkertown","underground assault"},rel={"npc:shoni-the-shilent","quest:2040","subzone:dwarven-district","subzone:deeprun-tram","zone:stormwind","zone:ironforge","zone:gnomeregan","zone:deadmines"},m={level="15",faction="Alliance",id=2041},src={"Speak with Shoni"}}
E["quest:291"] = {t="quest",n="The Reports",z="ironforge",s="From Kharanos, Senir Whitebeard sends word to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge about the Frostmane threat to Dun Morogh. He asks you to leave his scout unnamed.",h="From Kharanos, Senir Whitebeard sends word to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge about the Frostmane threat...",sec={{t="A Dispatch to the Capital",b="The report carries news from deep inside Frostmane Hold, where the trolls threaten Dun Morogh. Senir wants you to take it straight to Barin Redstone and keep the scout from the snowy crags unnamed.",sp=0},{t="Friction in the High Seat",b="Senator Barin Redstone grows angry when Senir’s report reaches Ironforge’s royal court. He resents Senir invoking King Magni’s authority to approve his operations. His anger reveals the Senate’s resentment of the King’s decrees and the field work carried out in his name.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Senir Whitebeard?",a="Senir Whitebeard is a dwarven mountaineer stationed near Kharanos in Dun Morogh. He oversees scouting and military reconnaissance against Frostmane trolls encroaching on dwarven settlements.",al={"senir whitebeard","who gives the reports","whitebeard kharanos"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Senator Barin Redstone?",a="Barin Redstone is a sour, aristocratic dwarf senator who lives in Ironforge’s throne room near King Magni Bronzebeard. Common petitioners annoy him easily.",al={"barin redstone","who is the senator","redstone ironforge"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Senator Redstone angry about the report?",a="Senir warns you that Senator Redstone is sour. You learn why the senator is angry when you deliver the report.",al={"why is redstone mad","why does the senator yell","senate vs magni"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Why does Senir Whitebeard ask to keep your help secret?",a="Senir Whitebeard asks you to keep your help secret so his superiors will believe he completed the arduous scouting himself. He does not want to admit that an adventurer carried out the work.",al={"why does senir take credit","whitebeard stole credit","senir's secret"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the report delivered?",a="You deliver the report to Senator Barin Redstone in the High Seat of Ironforge, the great chamber where King Magni Bronzebeard holds court.",al={"where to turn in the reports","barin redstone location","the reports turn in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does this quest reveal about Ironforge politics?",a="Delivering the report introduces Ironforge’s Senate and the officials who receive frontier reports. Redstone’s response offers a glimpse of Ironforge politics.",al={"ironforge government lore","dwarf senate lore","magni vs senate"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="Why does Senir Whitebeard need you to deliver the report instead of doing it himself?",a="Senir Whitebeard remains stationed out in Dun Morogh to oversee field operations against local threats like the Frostmane trolls. More importantly, he wants the Senate and his superiors to believe he is laboring tirelessly on the front lines, leaving courier duties and the unpleasant task of facing a grumpy senator to an expendable traveler.",al={"why send me with report","why doesnt senir deliver report","why me reports"},it="why_me",add="bde96c47"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see the balance between King Magni’s crown and the dwarven Senate’s parliamentary power when you deliver the dispatch in the High Seat.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Ironforge’s civic layout and the bureaucracy that shapes Alliance domestic policy."},kw={"barin redstone","dwarf senate","frostmane","high seat","ironforge","kharanos","magni bronzebeard","senir whitebeard","the reports"},rel={"npc:senir-whitebeard","quest:287","subzone:kharanos","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Senir Whitebeard",["end"]="Senator Barin Redstone",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=291},src={"The Reports"}}
E["quest:2948"] = {t="quest",n="Gnome Improvement",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Talvash del Kissel offers to improve a ring he made in Gnomeregan. He needs silver and moss agate for a delicate lattice over its old band.",h="In Ironforge, Talvash del Kissel offers to improve a ring he made in Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="A Gnomish Artisan in Exile",b="Talvash del Kissel fled Gnomeregan after the trogg invasion and radiation brought the city down. Now the gnome refugee lives in Ironforge's Mystic Ward. The jeweler and tinkerer is short on coin and out of stock, but determined to prove his skills remain sharp in exile.",sp=0},{t="Upgrading the Old Band",b="Talvash is glad to see his simple ring design again, cleaned by the Sparklematic 5200. Yet he considers the old band dated. He offers to improve it with silver and moss agate lattice work, showing his skill with metal and gemstones.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Talvash del Kissel?",a="Talvash del Kissel is a gnome jeweler and craftsman living in exile in Ironforge. Before Gnomeregan fell, he ran a small jewelry shop there. One of his rings can be recovered and brought to him in the Mystic Ward.",al={"talvash","talvash del kissel","gnome jeweler ironforge"},it="identity"},{q="What is the history behind the ring being upgraded?",a="Talvash made the ring as one of several plain bands in his Gnomeregan shop. A Dark Iron dwarf carried one into the ruins, where adventurers can retrieve it and clean it in the Sparklematic 5200. Talvash offers to add silver and moss agate lattice work to improve it.",al={"where does the ring come from","grime encrusted ring origin"},it="history"},{q="Why does Talvash ask the player to provide the reagents?",a="Talvash ran out of materials and is short on money after fleeing Gnomeregan. He asks for silver and moss agate to make the lattice work.",al={"why do i need silver and moss agate","why does talvash have no materials"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this quest chain begin?",a="The trail begins in Gnomeregan, where a Grime-Encrusted Ring can be found on enemies. Clean it in the Sparklematic 5200, then follow the initials 'TdK' to Talvash in Ironforge.",al={"how to start gnome improvement","ring questline start"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Is Talvash bitter about his situation in Ironforge?",a="Talvash laments his unjust financial hole, but keeps his spirits and professional pride. He believes that once back on his feet, he will be renowned across Azeroth for crafting the finest trinkets.",al={"talvash backstory","talvash personality"},it="ties"},{q="Does the Horde have access to this quest?",a="No. Horde adventurers who clean Grime-Encrusted objects in Gnomeregan are sent to Nogg in Orgrimmar instead of Talvash in Ironforge.",al={"can horde do gnome improvement","horde ring upgrade"},gp=true},{q="What is the Silver Bar for?",a="Talvash needs the refined metal to reshape your original ring into a more intricate piece of jewelry. He uses the silver bar to forge a detailed lattice work directly onto the band, giving the simple design far greater elegance and durability than his early craftwork possessed.",al={"why silver bar","talvash silver bar","what does he need silver for"},it="item",add="2e3e2066"},{q="What is the Moss Agate for?",a="The moss agate serves as the decorative centerpiece for the ring's upgrade. By setting the polished green gem into the newly crafted silver lattice, Talvash intends to add flair and showcase his true expertise as an artisan, transforming a rudimentary trinket into a far more impressive work.",al={"why moss agate","talvash moss agate","what does he need agate for"},it="item",add="a02fa77a"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Talvash's pride in his craft, even after exile from his homeland and the loss of his materials.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can provide the silver and moss agate Talvash needs for his jewelry work.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can help refugees from Gnomeregan through the ties between the fallen capital and Ironforge."},kw={"brilliant gold ring","gnome improvement","gnomeregan","ironforge","moss agate","silver bar","talvash"},rel={"npc:talvash-del-kissel","quest:2947","quest:2945","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},m={start="Talvash del Kissel",faction="Alliance",id=2948,ri={"Moss Agate","Silver Bar"}},src={"Gnome Improvement"}}
E["quest:2997"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of Divinity",z="ironforge",s="Azar Stronghammer sends promising dwarven paladins from Dun Morogh to Ironforge for deeper instruction. There, Tiza Battleforge awaits in the Hall of Mysteries, where the trials begin in service to the Holy Light.",h="Azar Stronghammer sends promising dwarven paladins from Dun Morogh to Ironforge for deeper instruction.",sec={{t="A Call to the High Seat",b="Dwarven initiates guard Dun Morogh's snowbound villages and roads. When Azar sees that a defender is ready for deeper spiritual instruction, he sends that candidate from field duties to Ironforge. There, the city's holy elders can guide them.",sp=0},{t="The Hall of Mysteries",b="The summons takes you through the Mystic Ward to the Hall of Mysteries. Sacred relics and solemn study fill its halls. Tiza Battleforge tests your readiness for self-sacrifice, mercy, and the moral duties of your calling.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Azar Stronghammer calls a promising dwarven paladin from field duties in Dun Morogh and sends you to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge. The trials teach you about the Holy Light and are required to earn the power of resurrection.",al={"why do i need this quest","what is tome of divinity for","tome of divinity purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza Battleforge is a veteran dwarven paladin and respected mentor in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. She guides young paladins through spiritual instruction and the sacred trials of the Tome of Divinity.",al={"who is tiza","tiza battleforge lore","who is battleforge"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Hall of Mysteries located?",a="The Hall of Mysteries lies in the Mystic Ward in western Ironforge. Priests, paladins, and mages gather there, at the spiritual and arcane center of the dwarven capital.",al={"where is hall of mysteries","find hall of mysteries","hall of mysteries ironforge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sends the paladin on this errand?",a="Azar Stronghammer, a paladin trainer in Dun Morogh, sends promising initiates to Ironforge after they prove their dedication to defending local dwarven settlements.",al={"who starts tome of divinity","quest giver tome of divinity","azar stronghammer"},it="origin"},{q="Why must dwarven paladins study in Ironforge?",a="Azar teaches basic combat in the field, while the Hall of Mysteries holds the formal teachings, sacred texts, and elders of the Holy Light. Senior mentors such as Tiza Battleforge guide the study of advanced rites and spiritual doctrines.",al={"why go to ironforge","why train in ironforge"},it="why_here"},{q="What follows after speaking with Tiza Battleforge?",a="Speaking with Tiza begins the dwarven trials of the Tome of Divinity. They challenge you to show devotion, compassion, and sacrifice in service to the Light.",al={"what comes next","next quest after tome of divinity","what does tiza give me"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Azar Stronghammer want you to visit Ironforge?",a="Azar Stronghammer recognizes that your time as an apprentice aiding Dun Morogh is coming to a close. To truly serve as a champion of the Holy Light, you require deeper instruction in its mysteries, principles, and obligations. He directs you to Ironforge because Tiza Battleforge is entrusted with testing and guiding promising young paladins toward their true calling.",al={"why does azar send you","azar stronghammer motive","why go see tiza battleforge"},it="motive",add="d775d5e6"},{q="Why does Azar Stronghammer send you specifically?",a="This journey is not an errand that a city guard or an established veteran could undertake for you. It marks your personal progression as a paladin. Azar sends you to Tiza Battleforge because you alone must answer the call of the Light, prove your dedication to its virtues, and accept the burdens expected of a holy warrior.",al={"why send me","why azar sends you","why paladin player"},it="why_me",add="a7a63213"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you join practical military service in the snows with the deep spiritual discipline expected of a holy warrior.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you join your kin's endurance with the teachings of the Holy Light in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you share reverence for the Light with dwarven defenders of Khaz Modan and your human allies in Lordaeron and Stormwind."},kw={"azar stronghammer","dun morogh","hall of mysteries","holy light","ironforge","mystic ward","paladin","redemption","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:tiza-battleforge","npc:azar-stronghammer","subzone:hall-of-mysteries","subzone:mystic-ward","zone:ironforge","zone:dunmorogh","topic:light"},m={start="Azar Stronghammer",["end"]="Tiza Battleforge",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=2997},src={"Tome of Divinity (Azar Stronghammer)"}}
E["quest:2999"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of Divinity",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, young dwarven paladins are sent to Tiza Battleforge to learn the Holy Light's deeper duties. Their rite of passage reaches beyond martial training and toward sacred vows.",h="In Ironforge, young dwarven paladins are sent to Tiza Battleforge to learn the Holy Light's deeper duties.",sec={{t="The Call to the High Seat",b="You have defended Anvilmar and Kharanos from troggs and frost trolls, proving your discipline in battle. Now Brandur Ironhammer, your trainer, sends you upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries. Senior paladins there prepare initiates for the order's spiritual duties.",sp=0},{t="Guidance from Tiza Battleforge",b="Tiza Battleforge teaches that the Light asks more than swordplay and hammer blows. It asks for compassion, justice, and self-sacrifice. Seeking her begins your formal study of the Tome of Divinity, a sacred path toward the power to resurrect the fallen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Brandur Ironhammer sends young dwarven paladins from their trainer to senior paladin Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge. This begins the trials for studying the Tome of Divinity and gaining the power of spiritual resurrection.",al={"what does this quest do","tome of divinity start","why do this quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Brandur Ironhammer?",a="Brandur Ironhammer trains dwarven paladins in the Hall of Mysteries, in Ironforge's Mystic Ward. He watches over young paladins and sends promising initiates upstairs to Tiza Battleforge when they are ready for greater sacred duties.",al={"who gives this quest","brandur role","brandur ironhammer lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza Battleforge is a respected veteran paladin upstairs in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. She teaches younger paladins what the Holy Light demands beyond martial skill.",al={"where is tiza","tiza battleforge role","who is tiza"},it="target"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Speaking with Tiza Battleforge begins the Tome of Divinity trials. They test a paladin's devotion, mercy, and willingness to protect and restore life in service to the Light.",al={"next quest","what comes after","tome of divinity chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why must dwarven paladins seek out the Tome of Divinity?",a="A paladin must learn selflessness and spiritual duty to return a fallen ally to life. The Tome of Divinity guides initiates through formal lessons and tests of faith needed to channel such potent holy power.",al={"why tome of divinity","paladin res quest lore","redemption dwarf"}},{q="Do humans receive this same instruction in Ironforge?",a="Human paladins follow a parallel path through the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind. Brandur Ironhammer's summons to Tiza Battleforge is for dwarves training in Ironforge.",al={"can humans do this","is this dwarf only","human tome of divinity"}},{q="Why does Brandur Ironhammer send you to Tiza Battleforge?",a="Brandur Ironhammer recognizes that your time training in Dun Morogh has prepared you for deeper responsibilities within the Order. Rather than keeping you bound to local troubles, he wants you to advance in your calling. Tiza Battleforge is revered among dwarven paladins as a mentor who guides younger initiates when they are ready to learn what the Holy Light truly demands of them.",al={"why does brandur send you","brandur ironhammer motive","why talk to tiza battleforge"},it="motive",add="1a85ab42"},{q="Why must you speak to Tiza yourself instead of Brandur handling it?",a="The path of a paladin is deeply personal and cannot be walked by proxy. Brandur Ironhammer can guide your early martial training, but spiritual progression demands that you present yourself directly before your elders. Tiza Battleforge must evaluate your devotion and resolve firsthand before she can entrust you with sacred teachings like the Tome of Divinity.",al={"why me tome of divinity","why must i go to tiza","why doesn't brandur go"},it="why_me",add="264c72ef"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you move from martial drills toward the spiritual duties of the Holy Light. The trials lead toward the power of Redemption.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you join devotion to the Holy Light with Khaz Modan's traditions of duty and brotherhood. You answer the call in Ironforge's mountain halls."},kw={"brandur ironhammer","hall of mystics","ironforge","paladin","redemption","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:brandur-ironhammer","npc:tiza-battleforge","zone:ironforge","zone:dunmorogh","topic:light"},m={start="Brandur Ironhammer",["end"]="Tiza Battleforge",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=2999},src={"Tome of Divinity (Brandur Ironhammer)"}}
E["quest:3000"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of Divinity",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, dwarf paladins return for deeper training in the Holy Light. Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker sends them home, and Tiza Battleforge guides them toward the sacred trials of the Tome of Divinity.",h="In Ironforge, dwarf paladins return for deeper training in the Holy Light.",sec={{t="A Summons Home",b="Dwarf paladins keep their spiritual and martial roots in Khaz Modan, even when they serve Stormwind or travel through human lands. When Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker judges that a dwarf has gained enough field training, he sends them home. There they learn the duties expected of a full Knight of the Silver Hand.",sp=0},{t="The Hall of Mysteries",b="In Ironforge, you are directed to the Mystic Ward and the Hall of Mysteries. Tiza Battleforge waits upstairs, where she mentors young dwarven paladins. She prepares them to bear the burden of the Holy Light through sacred trials recorded in the Tome of Divinity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker send me back to Ironforge?",a="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker sends you back because dwarven paladins learn the deeper tenets and trials of the Holy Light from their own kin. Tiza Battleforge guides that training.",al={"why go to ironforge","why grayson sends me away","why visit tiza"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza Battleforge is one of Ironforge's most respected dwarven paladins. She mentors young paladins upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries and oversees their trials.",al={"tiza battleforge","who is tiza","paladin trainer tiza"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tiza Battleforge?",a="You can find Tiza Battleforge upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries, in Ironforge's Mystic Ward.",al={"where is tiza","tiza battleforge location","how to find tiza"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity records the holy teachings and trials paladins undergo to master the Holy Light, especially resurrection and devotion to fallen allies.",al={"tome of divinity meaning","what is the tome","paladin book"},it="item"},{q="Can human paladins do this version of the quest?",a="No. This summons directs dwarven paladins to their homeland's instructors. Human paladins pursue their trials with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker and Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.",al={"can humans do this","is this quest dwarf only"},gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Tiza Battleforge?",a="After you introduce yourself to Tiza Battleforge, she gives you formal dwarven trials from the Tome of Divinity. They test your readiness to wield the Light's redemptive power.",al={"what comes next","next quest after tome of divinity","after speaking to tiza"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker choose me for this?",a="Lord Grayson recognizes your growing potential as a paladin, but he respects the distinct traditions of your people. Rather than instructing you entirely within the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind, he knows that young dwarven paladins must be grounded in the teachings of their own elders. He sends you home because it is time for your next sacred rite, and Tiza Battleforge is the revered mentor who guides dwarves through that spiritual milestone.",al={"why me tome of divinity","why does grayson send me","why dwarf paladin"},it="why_me",rc="Dwarf",add="c5356bb5"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you return from human lands to Ironforge, your ancestral home in Khaz Modan, to train under your own elders.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you begin a major rite of passage by studying the Tome of Divinity and mastering the gift of resurrection.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the close spiritual ties between dwarves and humans in the shared training and mutual respect between Stormwind's paladins and Ironforge's mentors."},kw={"dwarf paladin","hall of mysteries","ironforge","lord grayson shadowbreaker","mystic ward","redemption","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:tiza-battleforge","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","subzone:hall-of-mysteries","subzone:mystic-ward","zone:ironforge","topic:light"},m={start="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker",["end"]="Tiza Battleforge",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=3000},src={"Tome of Divinity (Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker)"}}
E["quest:301"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Ironforge",z="ironforge",s="Jern Hornhelm sends Ironband’s report to Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge. The dig in southern Loch Modan has run short of blasting supplies, and the Explorers’ League must attend to it.",h="Jern Hornhelm sends Ironband’s report to Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Courier for the League",b="The Explorers’ League funds and oversees archaeological expeditions across Khaz Modan, and supplies them. Ironband’s dig in southern Loch Modan has run short of blasting supplies. Its overseers cannot simply requisition more nearby.\n\nAt the Thelsamar inn, Jern Hornhelm entrusts you with Ironband’s written report. You carry it over the mountain passes to Prospector Stormpike at the League’s headquarters in Ironforge.",sp=0},{t="The Stormpike Temper",b="Prospector Stormpike brings his clan’s fierce resolve to his work for the League. In Ironforge’s grand Library and Hall of Explorers, he expects the digs to produce results swiftly.\n\nIronband’s report leaves him outraged. It says nothing of a massive shipment of blastpowder sent weeks ago. That missing record points to a dangerous break in Loch Modan’s supply lines.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does this report need to go all the way to Ironforge?",a="The Explorers’ League controls the distribution of valuable supplies such as blastpowder. Field digs need approval from senior prospectors at the Hall of Explorers before ordering explosives.",al={"why go to ironforge","why take report to stormpike","ironforge report reason"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Prospector Stormpike?",a="Prospector Stormpike is a senior Explorers’ League official based in Ironforge. He belongs to the proud Stormpike clan and is known for his short temper and impatience with stalled digs and missing supplies.",al={"who is stormpike","prospector stormpike lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where did Ironband's original blastpowder go?",a="A shipment of blasting powder was sent weeks ago, but Ironband’s report does not say he received it. Troggs or bandits may have ambushed the wagon on Loch Modan’s roads.",al={"what happened to blastpowder","missing blastpowder","where is the powder"}},{q="Where do you find Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge?",a="You can find Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge’s Assembly of Explorers, also called the Library or Hall of Explorers, in the city’s northeastern wing.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","assembly of explorers location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives you the report in Thelsamar?",a="Jern Hornhelm gives you the report at the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar. He coordinates reports and messages between Ironband’s remote camp and the city leadership.",al={"who starts report to ironforge","jern hornhelm role"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Stormpike reads the report?",a="After reading the report, Stormpike is furious about the missing munitions and stalled progress. He orders you to arrange a new shipment of blastpowder and take it straight back to Prospector Ironband.",al={"what comes next","next quest after report to ironforge"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Jern Hornhelm want this report sent to Ironforge?",a="Prospector Ironband's excavation in Loch Modan has ground to a halt because the crew ran out of blastpowder. Jern Hornhelm cannot requisition more supplies on his own authority; he needs formal approval from the Explorers' League headquarters in Ironforge. Delivering the progress report to Prospector Stormpike is the only administrative way to secure a fresh supply of powder and keep the dig moving forward.",al={"why send report","jern hornhelm motive","why does jern want blastpowder"},it="motive",add="601d3943"},{q="Why does Jern Hornhelm send you instead of going himself?",a="Jern Hornhelm has his hands full managing logistics in Thelsamar and supporting the local excavation efforts. Beyond that, Prospector Stormpike is notorious for having a short, fiery temper when dealing with delays and setbacks. Entrusting an expendable courier to brave Stormpike's wrath spares Jern the direct fury of his superiors while keeping his focus on local operations.",al={"why send me","why not go himself","why does hornhelm need me"},it="why_me",add="499fe615"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Explorers’ League’s procedures and Clan Stormpike’s legendary temper from life in your capital’s halls.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how the Alliance links distant research camps in mountain valleys with Ironforge’s military and scholarly leadership."},kw={"blastpowder","explorers' league","ironband's compound","jern hornhelm","loch modan","prospector stormpike","report to ironforge","thelsamar"},rel={"npc:prospector-stormpike","npc:jern-hornhelm","topic:explorers-league","quest:298","quest:302","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Jern Hornhelm",["end"]="Prospector Stormpike",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=301},src={"Report to Ironforge"}}
E["quest:302"] = {t="quest",n="Powder to Ironband",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, the Explorer's League sends blasting powder south to Prospector Ironband's dig in Loch Modan. Prospector Stormpike approves the request, and the shipment goes to Thelsamar before continuing to Ironband's Excavation.",h="In Ironforge, the Explorer's League sends blasting powder south to Prospector Ironband's dig in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Bureaucracy and Blasting Powder",b="The Explorer's League sends blasting powder from Ironforge to Prospector Ironband's expedition in southern Loch Modan. When the dig runs short, word reaches the League's leaders. Prospector Stormpike approves the request and sends the runner to Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar, the valley's main supply hub.",sp=0},{t="A Missed Departure",b="Earlier wagons through Loch Modan have vanished or faced harassment from local troggs. Stormpike orders you to guard the powder wagon yourself. But when you reach the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar, Jern Hornhelm has already sent it south with Huldar and two dwarven porters. You hurry down the road to catch them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is blasting powder being sent to Ironband?",a="Prospector Ironband leads a dwarven archaeological dig in southern Loch Modan. His team has used its blasting powder while digging through dense rock, as trogg aggression grows.",al={"why need powder","ironband blasting powder","what is powder for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Prospector Stormpike?",a="Prospector Stormpike is a senior officer of the Dwarven Explorer's League in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. He reviews field requests, approves critical equipment, and manages supplies for major dig sites across Khaz Modan.",al={"stormpike role","who gave quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Jern Hornhelm?",a="Jern Hornhelm is an Explorers' League contact in Thelsamar, Loch Modan. He prepares supplies and organizes transport teams bound for the valley's more dangerous frontiers.",al={"jern hornhelm location","where is jern hornhelm"},it="identity"},{q="Why was personal escort requested for this shipment?",a="Earlier shipments bound for Ironband's excavation failed to arrive. Troggs spilling from the hills and dig sites make Loch Modan's main road increasingly dangerous.",al={"why escort powder","trogg attacks on wagons"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you arrive in Thelsamar?",a="Jern Hornhelm has already sent the wagon with Huldar and the porters Miran and Saean. You follow the southern road to catch them before trouble strikes.",al={"did i miss the wagon","where is the shipment"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="How does this quest fit into the Explorer's League storyline?",a="This delivery carries the dig site's request through the League's authorities in Ironforge and back into the field through Thelsamar. The expedition can then keep excavating.",al={"ironband chain","excavation questline"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Prospector Stormpike send an adventurer instead of official guards?",a="Prospector Stormpike operates out of the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge, focused on administrative matters and securing permits rather than fielding troops. With prior blasting powder shipments already falling prey to danger along the Loch Modan roads, he trusts a capable traveler who is already heading into the field to personally see that Jern Hornhelm's supply train reaches the dig site safely.",al={"why send me","why not send guards to ironband","why an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="8773e6dd"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, helping secure powder for an excavation supports the holy work of uncovering your people's mysterious origins.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, helping keep Loch Modan's roads safe supports the ties between Ironforge and the eastern frontiers.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know blasting powder helps miners and excavators break through deep bedrock."},kw={"explorers league","huldar","ironforge","jern hornhelm","loch modan","powder to ironband","prospector stormpike","thelsamar"},rel={"quest:301","npc:prospector-stormpike","npc:jern-hornhelm","npc:huldar","subzone:thelsamar"},m={start="Prospector Stormpike",["end"]="Jern Hornhelm",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=302},src={"Powder to Ironband"}}
E["quest:3681"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of Divinity",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Master Brandur Ironhammer sends promising human paladins south for deeper training. At Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Master Duthorian Rall guides their study of the sacred Tomes of Divinity.",h="In Ironforge, Master Brandur Ironhammer sends promising human paladins south for deeper training.",sec={{t="A Summons from Stormwind",b="Stormwind calls promising holy warriors south to the Cathedral of Light. Senior priests and paladin mentors await them there, keeping the Silver Hand's traditions alive in the Church of the Holy Light among human lands.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Cathedral",b="Master Brandur Ironhammer knows when a student is ready for deeper study of the faith. You can reach Stormwind's Cathedral District by the Deeprun Tram or across the mountain passes. There, Duthorian Rall prepares initiates to study the sacred Tomes and learn the rites of redemption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is an Ironforge trainer sending me to Stormwind?",a="Stormwind's Cathedral of Light handles advanced Alliance paladin instruction. Brandur Ironhammer sends promising initiates to Master Duthorian Rall for the trials tied to the sacred Tomes of Divinity.",al={"why go to stormwind","why send to duthorian rall","ironforge to stormwind paladin"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Brandur Ironhammer?",a="Brandur Ironhammer is a dwarven paladin trainer in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries, in the Mystic Ward. He watches over initiates, teaches martial devotion, and guides them toward higher study as their bond with the Holy Light grows.",al={"brandur ironhammer","who is brandur"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is a senior paladin trainer and prelate in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He tests aspiring paladins through spiritual trials before entrusting them with the Tomes of Divinity.",al={"duthorian rall","who is duthorian"},it="identity"},{q="What are the Tomes of Divinity?",a="The Tomes of Divinity are sacred texts and doctrinal handbooks of the Church of the Holy Light. They teach paladins the rites of resurrection, self-sacrifice, and compassion.",al={"what is tome of divinity","tome of divinity meaning"},it="item"},{q="What is the fastest way to reach Stormwind from Ironforge?",a="The Deeprun Tram is the quickest and safest route from Ironforge to Stormwind. From Tinker Town, it carries travelers beneath the mountains and into Stormwind.",al={"how to get to stormwind","deeprun tram to stormwind"},gp=true},{q="Is this trial required for all Alliance paladins?",a="No. Human paladins study the Tomes under Duthorian Rall at Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. Dwarven paladins begin their own Tome of Divinity trials in Ironforge with Tiza Battleforge.",al={"do dwarves have to do this","paladin class quest requirement"}},{q="Why does Brandur Ironhammer send you to Stormwind?",a="Brandur Ironhammer is answering an official summons from Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. The leaders of the Silver Hand have requested promising paladins report south for rigorous, advanced instruction. Recognizing your growing strength and devotion, Brandur knows you have reached a critical point in your calling where standard training in Ironforge is no longer enough; you are ready to study the sacred Tomes directly under Duthorian Rall.",al={"brandur ironhammer motive","why does brandur send me","brandur ironhammer stormwind"},it="motive",add="538cdf30"},{q="Why are you chosen for this task instead of someone else?",a="You are chosen because the summons specifically calls for developing paladins who have proven ready for the deeper mysteries of the Holy Light. Neither guards nor seasoned veterans can undertake this journey for you, as the Tomes of Divinity represent an intensely personal spiritual and martial trial required to advance within the Silver Hand.",al={"why me tome of divinity","why send me stormwind paladin","why not another paladin"},it="why_me",add="3ec0b7fd"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you grow from a martial novice into an ordained servant of the Holy Light, able to channel its deepest restorative miracles.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you follow Khaz Modan's proud paladin traditions and take up the Tomes of Divinity in Ironforge. Human paladins are summoned to Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you share holy warrior training in Stormwind, strengthening the spiritual and military bond between Ironforge and Stormwind."},kw={"brandur ironhammer","cathedral of light","duthorian rall","ironforge","paladin","redemption","stormwind","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:brandur-ironhammer","npc:duthorian-rall","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light"},m={start="Brandur Ironhammer",["end"]="Duthorian Rall",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=3681},src={"Tome of Divinity (5)"}}
E["quest:385"] = {t="quest",n="Crocolisk Hunting",z="ironforge",s="At Farstrider Lodge, Marek Ironheart seeks trackers to hunt Loch Modan's crocolisks. Their hides and meat bring steady trade, though hunting along the lake's shores and rocky islets is dangerous.",h="At Farstrider Lodge, Marek Ironheart seeks trackers to hunt Loch Modan's crocolisks.",sec={{t="A Lucrative Quarry",b="Crocolisks haunt the shallows and muddy banks, making crossings and fishing perilous. Across Khaz Modan, craftsmen and tailors seek their hides for rugged armor and leather goods. Rustic taverns pay well for the lean tail meat.",sp=0},{t="Jaws in the Shallows",b="Loch Modan's crocolisks gather mainly around the rocky islets. Their crushing jaws and sharp teeth make them dangerous quarry. Dwarven veterans like Marek Ironheart carry scars from wrestling them into submission. He warns that one misstep in the water can cost a limb. Skinning and butchering one takes patience, sturdy steel, and a willingness to enter its hunting ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are crocolisks hunted in Loch Modan?",a="Merchants and craftsmen value crocolisk hides for rugged clothing and leather armor, while local cooks prize the meat. Farstrider Lodge trades these goods to supply traders passing through Khaz Modan.",al={"why hunt crocolisks","crocolisk meat skin use","why marek wants crocs"},it="purpose"},{q="Where are the crocolisks usually found?",a="Crocolisks live in Loch Modan's muddy shallows and along its banks, especially around the rocky islands in the lake's center.",al={"crocolisk location","where to find crocs loch modan","where are crocolisks"},gp=true},{q="Who is Marek Ironheart?",a="Marek Ironheart is a veteran dwarven mountaineer and hunter stationed at Farstrider Lodge in southeastern Loch Modan. He trades in local wildlife materials and recounts close calls with the Loch's fiercest beasts.",al={"marek ironheart","who gives crocolisk hunting","quest giver marek"},it="identity"},{q="What makes hunting them so hazardous?",a="Loch Modan's crocolisks are aggressive, territorial predators with powerful jaws and sharp teeth. Hunters face them in deep water or on isolated islets, where the terrain favors sudden attacks by the reptiles.",al={"are crocs dangerous","danger of crocolisks","why are crocs hard to hunt"},it="danger"},{q="Is crocolisk meat actually safe and edible?",a="Yes. Properly dressed and roasted, crocolisk meat is prized by frontier cooks and tavern patrons across the dwarven lands for its firm texture and rich flavor.",al={"can you eat crocolisk","crocolisk meat edible","croc taste"}},{q="What is the Farstrider Lodge?",a="Farstrider Lodge is an outpost in southeastern Loch Modan. It gives Alliance hunters, trackers, and mountaineers a haven and a place to prepare to watch the valley's wild reaches.",al={"what is farstrider lodge","farstrider lodge purpose","where is farstrider lodge"},it="place"},{q="Why does Marek Ironheart want crocolisks hunted?",a="Marek Ironheart conducts steady trade out of Farstrider Lodge with merchants who pay good coin for crocolisk hides and flesh. The fierce reptiles hold the islands in the Loch, making hunting hazardous, but quality specimens fetch a reliable profit from craftsmen and eager buyers.",al={"marek ironheart motive","why hunt crocolisks","why does marek want crocs"},it="motive",add="148d1050"},{q="What is the Crocolisk Meat for?",a="Marek gathers crocolisk meat to sell to visiting traders and travelers. While wrestling the ferocious beasts is perilous, certain adventurous patrons and merchants specifically enjoy the taste and pay well for fresh cuts.",al={"crocolisk meat use","why collect crocolisk meat","what is crocolisk meat used for"},it="item",add="2fb1eb6c"},{q="What is the Crocolisk Skin for?",a="The skins are prized by merchants and tanners for crafting durable clothing and sturdy leather armor. Marek sells the hides you bring back to sustain the lodge's trade with passing buyers.",al={"crocolisk skin use","why collect crocolisk skins","what is crocolisk hide for"},it="item",add="31a07b3d"},{q="Why are the crocolisks found in Loch Modan?",a="The crocolisks are ferocious native predators that have entrenched themselves primarily across the islands and shores of Loch Modan. Their thick hides and savage jaws make them a defining danger of the freshwater lake.",al={"loch modan crocs origin","why are crocolisks here","who are the crocs"},it="target",add="0bb4b9c6"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can test your nerve at Farstrider Lodge against Loch Modan's aquatic dangers.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can make hearty stews and roasts with tough, lean crocolisk meat.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can take pride in taming Loch Modan's wilderness and earn an honest living hunting crocolisks."},kw={"crocolisk hunting","crocolisk meat","crocolisk skin","dwarf hunter","farstrider lodge","loch modan","marek ironheart","the loch"},rel={"npc:marek-ironheart","subzone:farstrider-lodge","subzone:the-loch","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Marek Ironheart",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=385,ri={"Crocolisk Meat","Crocolisk Skin (Classic)"}},src={"Crocolisk Hunting"}}
E["quest:4512"] = {t="quest",n="A Little Slime Goes a Long Way",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Laris Geardawdle seeks ooze samples from Felwood for his studies. He hopes to learn why the Royal Apothecary Society gathers them and what interests the Undercity's alchemists.",h="In Ironforge, Laris Geardawdle seeks ooze samples from Felwood for his studies.",sec={{t="A Peculiar Obsession",b="Laris Geardawdle studies oozes with the Explorers' League. Most of its scholars seek titan relics or dwarven genealogies, but these living puddles resist ordinary classification. They appear in wetlands, cursed woods, and damp ruins. Laris has seen Forsaken apothecaries collecting slime across Lordaeron, and wants to know what draws them to it.",sp=0},{t="The Primordial Secretion",b="Laris believes oozes may be primordial secretions tied to Azeroth's creation. He thinks they are neither vermin nor magical byproducts. To test his theory, you travel across the ocean to Felwood's blighted canopy. There, you gather Cursed and Tainted Oozes in specially made jars.",sp=0},{t="Proving Gnomish Worth",b="For Laris and many displaced gnomes, these studies carry personal weight. Since Gnomeregan fell to troggs and radiation, thousands have taken refuge in Ironforge's Great Forge. A discovery for the Explorers' League could answer dwarven skeptics. It could show that welcoming gnomes into the mountain city has become an enduring asset to Alliance science.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Laris Geardawdle?",a="Laris Geardawdle is a gnomish researcher and scholar in Ironforge. He works with the Explorers' League to study the biological origins of oozes and slimes across Azeroth.",al={"laris geardawdle","who is the quest giver","gnome ooze guy"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Laris care so much about ooze?",a="Laris suspects oozes are primordial secretions tied to Azeroth's origins. The Royal Apothecary Society's eager collection of slime samples has made him determined to learn their secret properties before the Horde does.",al={"why study slimes","why ooze jars","ooze theory"},it="motive"},{q="Where do you gather the ooze samples?",a="You gather samples from Cursed Oozes and Tainted Oozes in Felwood's corrupted forests in northern Kalimdor. You use empty glass containers Laris provides.",al={"where are the oozes","tainted ooze location","cursed ooze location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken collecting oozes?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society experiments with toxins, blights, and biological horrors to advance Forsaken alchemy. Its interest in raw oozes suggests they may contain virulent or mutagenic compounds.",al={"undercity oozes","royal apothecary society slime","why do forsaken want ooze"},it="conflict"},{q="How does this quest connect to the fall of Gnomeregan?",a="After Gnomeregan was lost to troggs and radiation, Laris felt the pressure of life as a refugee in Ironforge. He hopes a major scientific triumph for the Explorers' League will prove that giving gnomes refuge was worthwhile to their dwarven hosts.",al={"gnomeregan connection","dwarf gnome relations","gnome refugees ironforge"},it="history"},{q="What happens after you deliver the samples?",a="Laris begins testing the specimens in his Ironforge laboratory setup. He develops his theories about ooze taxonomy and elemental origins.",al={"slime quest follow up","what next after ooze jars"},it="next_step"},{q="What are the Filled Ooze Jars for?",a="The jars hold fresh samples extracted from the remains of cursed and tainted oozes found in Felwood. Laris Geardawdle requires them for scientific experimentation in Ironforge. He hopes to uncover the true nature of ooze creatures and prove his controversial theory that slimes are connected to the primordial creation of Azeroth itself.",al={"filled cursed ooze jar","filled tainted ooze jar","what are the ooze jars used for","ooze samples use"},it="item",add="930e16d1"},{q="What creatures are you sent after in Felwood?",a="You are sent to hunt the cursed and tainted oozes lurking in the corrupted wilds of Felwood. Felwood has been heavily warped by demonic magic, producing bizarre and volatile mutations. Laris wants specimens from these particular slimes to compare against other varieties found across Azeroth and see how environmental corruption alters their makeup.",al={"what are we fighting","cursed ooze target","tainted ooze felwood","who do we kill"},it="target",add="8c5a6c23"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Laris's drive to rebuild gnomish pride and reputation after Gnomeregan's heartbreaking loss.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may favor stone and metal over gelatinous sludge. The Explorers' League benefits from Laris's unusual drive.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can learn from the Royal Apothecary Society's gathering habits about the sinister brews the Undercity may be concocting."},kw={"cursed ooze","explorers league","felwood","gnomeregan","ironforge","laris geardawdle","ooze","royal apothecary society","slime","tainted ooze"},rel={"npc:laris-geardawdle","zone:felwood","zone:ironforge","topic:explorers-league","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome","zone:undercity"},m={start="Laris Geardawdle",faction="Alliance",id=4512,ri={"Filled Cursed Ooze Jar","Filled Tainted Ooze Jar"}},src={"A Little Slime Goes a Long Way"}}
E["quest:4513"] = {t="quest",n="A Little Slime Goes a Long Way",z="ironforge",s="Laris Geardawdle seeks pure oozes across Kalimdor. His Felwood-tainted samples showed that oozes absorb and reflect their surroundings. Clean specimens may show him how they adapt to the places they inhabit.",h="Laris Geardawdle seeks pure oozes across Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Matter of Purity",b="Laris Geardawdle needs clean samples for his study. The tainted ones showed how oozes take on the traits of their surroundings, but left him without a clear comparison. He seeks samples untouched by demonic taint or urban filth, so he can study ooze life on its own.",sp=0},{t="Tracking the Primal Slime",b="In Un'Goro Crater, Glutinous Oozes thrive in an isolated, primordial wilderness. Their samples give Laris the pure material he needs to study how oozes interact with Azeroth's living biomes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Laris Geardawdle need pure ooze samples?",a="Laris's earlier specimens carried Felwood's corruption. To test his belief that slimes adapt to and reflect their surroundings, he needs pure samples from an unpolluted habitat for comparison.",al={"why pure ooze","laris pure slime","what is pure ooze"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the pure oozes located?",a="Glutinous Oozes live in the prehistoric wilderness of Un'Goro Crater, far south in Kalimdor.",al={"where find pure ooze","pure sample jars location","where are pure slimes"},gp=true},{q="Who is Laris Geardawdle?",a="Laris Geardawdle is a gnomish researcher in Ironforge. He is devoted to uncovering the nature of Azeroth's slimes and oozes.",al={"who is laris","laris geardawdle lore"},it="identity"},{q="What makes oozes so interesting to researchers?",a="Oozes absorb and reflect the magical, environmental, and corruptive traits of the regions they inhabit.",al={"why study slime","ooze lore"}},{q="Does this follow an earlier task for Laris?",a="Yes. Laris first asked for oozes to study, but those samples carried Felwood's demonic taint. Now he seeks untarnished slimes.",al={"previous quest laris","what came before this"},it="history"},{q="What does Laris intend to do with the samples?",a="Laris plans to compare pure samples with corrupted ones. He hopes to learn how changes in an environment affect living creatures and Azeroth's wider population.",al={"laris ooze research","what is slime used for"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Filled Pure Sample Jar for?",a="These jars hold uncorrupted slime taken from oozes living in pristine wilderness. Laris Geardawdle discovered that slimes in Felwood took on that forest's demonic taint, revealing that oozes naturally absorb and reflect the traits of their surrounding environment. He needs jars of pure, uncontaminated slime to serve as a baseline for his research into how these creatures adapt and how such pollution might impact Azeroth as a whole.",al={"filled pure sample jar","pure sample jar purpose","what are sample jars for"},it="item",add="d7a6aa80"},{q="What are the pure oozes you are sent to find?",a="You are sent to harvest samples from glutinous oozes found in the primeval, untamed basin of Un'Goro Crater. Unlike the slimes dwelling in Felwood, which have absorbed demonic corruption, Un'Goro's oozes dwell in a thriving, untouched wilderness. Because oozes take on the essence of their environment, these specimens offer Laris the pure, unpolluted slime he needs to understand their biology before outside blight alters them.",al={"pure oozes","which oozes are pure","glutinous oozes"},it="target",add="df064ff1"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can appreciate Laris's careful method. He isolates variables and seeks an uncontaminated control group before drawing broad conclusions.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you travel from Ironforge into Kalimdor's untamed wilds to support gnomish research."},kw={"felwood","glutinous ooze","ironforge","laris geardawdle","ooze research","pure sample jars","un'goro crater"},rel={"npc:laris-geardawdle","quest:4512","zone:ironforge","zone:ungoro","zone:felwood"},m={start="Laris Geardawdle",faction="Alliance",id=4513,ri={"Filled Pure Sample Jar"}},src={"A Little Slime Goes a Long Way (2)"}}
E["quest:467"] = {t="quest",n="Stonegear's Search",z="ironforge",s="At Steelgrill's Depot, Pilot Stonegear seeks rare ore to strengthen his tank's weapons. He asks you to find fresh fuel for its firepower.",h="At Steelgrill's Depot, Pilot Stonegear seeks rare ore to strengthen his tank's weapons.",sec={{t="A Tinkerer's Ambition",b="Pilot Longbeard or Mountaineer Kadrell may send you to hear Stonegear's proposal. The ambitious pilot wants his siege engine to hit harder, and word of his plans has spread through Ironforge and Loch Modan.",sp=0},{t="Heading to Steelgrill's Depot",b="At the proving ground and staging yard just east of Kharanos, Stonegear seeks prospectors to search for rare, volatile ore. He believes it can greatly increase his tank's firepower.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest?",a="Pilot Longbeard in Ironforge or Mountaineer Kadrell along the road in Loch Modan can direct you to Pilot Stonegear.",al={"quest giver","who starts stonegear search","where to get quest"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Pilot Stonegear?",a="Pilot Stonegear is at Steelgrill's Depot in Dun Morogh, just down the path northeast of Kharanos.",al={"stonegear location","where is pilot stonegear","steelgrills depot stonegear"},gp=true},{q="What does Pilot Stonegear need?",a="Pilot Stonegear enjoys modifying his siege engine. He seeks rare mineral deposits to increase the firepower of his tank's munitions.",al={"stonegear goal","why does stonegear want me","what does stonegear want"},it="wants"},{q="What quest follows this one?",a="After you report to Pilot Stonegear at the depot, he sends you to find Incendicite, a volatile ore in the wetlands.",al={"next quest","stonegear follow up","what comes after stonegears search"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quest Alliance-only?",a="Yes. Pilot Stonegear and his contacts serve Ironforge's military and the Alliance.",al={"can horde do stonegears search","faction requirement"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why is the depot interested in wild ores?",a="Dwarven engineers and tank pilots experiment with incendiary compounds, pyrotechnics, and volatile elements. They seek an edge for their war machines against troggs, dark irons, and wild beasts.",al={"why siege engine ore","dwarf tank gunpowder"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do the quest givers send you to Pilot Stonegear?",a="Both Pilot Longbeard and Mountaineer Kadrell know that Pilot Stonegear is obsessed with tinkering on his siege engine and constantly looking to augment its firepower. When rumors reached them of a rare, explosive ore that Stonegear wants tracked down, they immediately thought of pointing a roaming adventurer his way rather than letting his restless ambition go unanswered.",al={"why send to stonegear","why does kadrell want this done","longbeard motive"},it="motive",add="51f66015"},{q="Why do they need an adventurer instead of handling it themselves?",a="Pilot Longbeard has duties tending to his own machine and affairs, while Mountaineer Kadrell is tasked with patrolling and guarding Loch Modan against threats. Investigating distant rumors of exotic ore for a tank enthusiast requires someone with wandering boots and free time, making a capable traveler the ideal scout for Stonegear's ambitions.",al={"why send me","why not longbeard or kadrell","why need an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="96f84a87"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarven mountaineer or mechanist, you can take pride in helping a fellow pilot at Steelgrill's Depot refine Khaz Modan's arsenal.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnomish innovator, you can appreciate Pilot Stonegear's drive to push siege weapons beyond standard safety limits.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner who seeks exotic, combustible earth, you may find Stonegear's rumors of rare underground ore worth pursuing.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer who works with high explosives, you can respect Stonegear's dedication to increasing his tank's firepower."},kw={"dun morogh","incendicite","kadrell","longbeard","pilot stonegear","siege engine","steelgrill's depot","stonegear"},rel={"npc:pilot-stonegear","quest:466","subzone:steelgrill-s-depot","zone:dunmorogh"},m={start="Pilot Longbeard, Mountaineer Kadrell",["end"]="Pilot Stonegear",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=467},src={"Stonegear's Search"}}
E["quest:5639"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="ironforge",s="High Priest Rohan sends you from Ironforge to Stormwind to learn healing and survival. There, High Priestess Laurena teaches dwarven acolytes the deeper mysteries of the Church.",h="High Priest Rohan sends you from Ironforge to Stormwind to learn healing and survival.",sec={{t="A Summons to Stormwind",b="In Ironforge's Mystic Ward, Rohan guides dwarven initiates devoted to the Holy Light. Seeing your discipline and faith, he sends you southwest to Stormwind. Human and dwarven clerics share close spiritual ties, and the city's grand halls hold advanced teaching.",sp=0},{t="The Cathedral of Light",b="You reach Stormwind by the Deeprun Tram and climb to Cathedral Square. In the Cathedral of Light, High Priestess Laurena tests you on the Church's behalf. She teaches the desperate prayers a priest calls upon in battle, seeking divine aid when strength fails and death draws near.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="High Priest Rohan sends you. He leads the dwarven clergy in the Hall of Mysteries, in Ironforge's Mystic Ward.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","rohan location"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I need to go to complete this?",a="Go to the Cathedral of Light in the heart of Cathedral Square, Stormwind City. High Priestess Laurena waits inside the main sanctuary.",al={"where is laurena","where to turn in","stormwind turn in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the best way to get to Stormwind from Ironforge?",a="Take the Deeprun Tram, built by the gnomes, from eastern Ironforge to Stormwind's Dwarven District.",al={"how to get to stormwind","travel to stormwind","tram location"},gp=true},{q="Why must a dwarf priest go to a human city to train?",a="The Church of the Holy Light is rooted in human tradition, and the Cathedral of Light is its chief seat of learning. Dwarven and human priesthoods work together, sharing teachings and traditions across the Alliance.",al={"why stormwind","dwarf human church","why laurena"},it="why_here"},{q="What ability does this training unlock?",a="This training begins your study of Desperate Prayer. It is an instant plea for self-preservation that rapidly restores a priest's health in dire danger.",al={"quest reward","what spell do i get","desperate prayer ability"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Does this quest involve combat?",a="No combat is involved. You travel safely from Ironforge to Stormwind as an emissary and present yourself to High Priestess Laurena.",al={"is there fighting","quest combat","travel quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does High Priest Rohan send you to Stormwind?",a="High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind has reached out requesting your presence, deeming you ready to prove your worth for the next level of your sacred training. Rohan honors this call from the Cathedral of Light, trusting that your tutelage under Laurena will strengthen your devotion and deepen your command over the Light's blessings.",al={"why rohan send you","why go to stormwind priest","rohan motive desperate prayer"},it="motive",add="c0c688ec"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you leave Ironforge's local training and enter the wider hierarchy of the Church of the Holy Light.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a young Khaz Modan dwarf, your journey to Stormwind offers an early glimpse of human culture, grand architecture and shared spiritual devotion.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Ironforge and Stormwind's spiritual bond in the way their priesthoods share training and work together."},kw={"cathedral of light","desperate prayer","ironforge","laurena","mystic ward","priest","rohan","stormwind"},rel={"npc:high-priest-rohan","npc:high-priestess-laurena","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light"},m={start="High Priest Rohan",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=5639},src={"Desperate Prayer (Ironforge)"}}
E["quest:5645"] = {t="quest",n="A Lack of Fear",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, High Priest Rohan tests promising dwarven disciples. In the Mystic Ward, he teaches them as their strength of spirit grows.",h="In Ironforge, High Priest Rohan tests promising dwarven disciples.",sec={{t="A Summons to Ironforge",b="Local mentors send priests serving the Alliance abroad to senior clergy of their order. For dwarven disciples, that summons brings you to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge's Mystic Ward. There, basic spiritual practice gives way to deeper uses of holy magic, tested through trials.",sp=0},{t="The Trials of Fortitude",b="Dwarven tradition teaches that the Light is a shield in physical conflict. When you report to High Priest Rohan, you show that you have endured trials in the wider world. Now you must prove your mettle and master fear on the front lines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Local priest trainers send seasoned initiates to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge for advanced instruction and the spiritual gifts taught by the city's priesthood.",al={"why do i have to go to rohan","what does a lack of fear do","priest quest level 20 ironforge"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is High Priest Rohan?",a="High Priest Rohan leads the dwarven priesthood in Ironforge. In the Hall of Mysteries in the Mystic Ward, he teaches disciples steadfast devotion and martial resilience.",al={"who is rohan","high priest rohan lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can High Priest Rohan be found?",a="High Priest Rohan can be found in the Hall of Mysteries, in the Mystic Ward in Ironforge's western quarters.",al={"where is rohan","rohan location","how to find high priest rohan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this called 'A Lack of Fear'?",a="The name points to Fear Ward, the Holy Light's protection against panic and supernatural terror. Every priest, of any race, learns it from a priest trainer at level 20.",al={"meaning of lack of fear","fear ward quest"},it="name"},{q="Who sends the priest to Ironforge?",a="Local trainers send initiates to Ironforge. High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind and Priestess Alathea in Darnassus direct students to honor their heritage or study with Rohan.",al={"who starts a lack of fear","quest givers for lack of fear"},it="origin"},{q="Does this quest involve combat?",a="No. You travel to Ironforge and speak with High Priest Rohan.",al={"do i have to fight","is there combat in a lack of fear"},gp=true},{q="Why are you being summoned to High Priest Rohan?",a="Priest trainers in other cities recognize that your faith and combat prowess have grown significantly. High Priest Rohan in Ironforge oversees the training of Alliance priests in the region, particularly the unique disciplines and rites of the dwarves. He has summoned you because you have proven yourself ready to face your next trial and learn more advanced sacred teachings.",al={"why see rohan","a lack of fear motive","why send to ironforge"},it="motive",add="54793667"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, this summons marks your coming of age in the priesthood. You can learn holy techniques refined by Ironforge's stalwart clergy.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, returning to Rohan honors your people's faith, physical fortitude, and martial grit in service to the Holy Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance priest, you study alongside clergy from other capitals. Alliance priesthoods send acolytes across borders to learn from masters in Ironforge."},kw={"alathea","fear ward","hall of mysteries","ironforge","laurena","mystic ward","priest","rohan"},rel={"npc:high-priest-rohan","zone:ironforge","subzone:mystic-ward","topic:light"},m={start="High Priest Rohan / High Priestess Laurena / Priestess Alathea",["end"]="High Priest Rohan",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=5645},src={"A Lack of Fear"}}
E["quest:5677"] = {t="quest",n="Arcane Feedback",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, human acolytes seeking deeper teaching are sent back to Stormwind. There, the Cathedral of Light holds the traditions of their people.",h="In Ironforge, human acolytes seeking deeper teaching are sent back to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Gentle Redirection",b="High Priest Rohan welcomes a human priest who seeks deeper spiritual teaching in Ironforge’s Mystic Ward. Dwarven and human priests both serve the Holy Light, yet each people keeps its own rites, disciplines, and prayers of defense. Rohan reserves Ironforge’s teachings for his own clergy. So he sends human priests back to Elwynn to learn the traditions of humankind.",sp=0},{t="Return to the Cathedral",b="After reaching Stormwind City, the acolyte finds High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light. Laurena is relieved that Rohan’s guidance has brought the traveler to her, and welcomes them as their powers begin to grow. In the Cathedral, human priests can keep learning Stormwind’s spiritual practices. There they prepare to wield the Holy Light against the threats around the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does High Priest Rohan refuse to teach human priests?",a="High Priest Rohan respects human practitioners, but dwarven clergy keep rites and blessings passed down through their own people. He sends human priests to Stormwind, where their mentors preserve those teachings.",al={"why send to stormwind","why rohan won't train","dwarf priest won't train me"},it="motive"},{q="Who is High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena leads and trains priests in Stormwind City’s Cathedral of Light. She guides promising human priests through their intermediate studies and rites.",al={"high priestess laurena","who is laurena","cathedral priest trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can High Priest Rohan be found?",a="High Priest Rohan can be found in the Hall of Mysteries, in Ironforge’s Mystic Ward.",al={"rohan location","where is high priest rohan","find rohan"},gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Intermediate human priests are sent from dwarven lands to the Cathedral of Light, their main place of racial training. There they can pursue spiritual teachings shaped for their people.",al={"arcane feedback quest purpose","why do this quest","what does this quest do"},it="purpose"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you learn that each people follows the Holy Light through its own traditions.",["race:Human"]="As a human priest, you are sent from dwarven sanctuaries to Stormwind. At the Cathedral of Light, you learn the sacred ways taught to your people.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you honor your alliance with humans while keeping Khaz Modan’s specific rites among your own people."},kw={"arcane feedback","cathedral of light","high priest rohan","high priestess laurena","ironforge","mystic ward","priest quest","stormwind"},rel={"npc:high-priest-rohan","npc:high-priestess-laurena","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="High Priest Rohan",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=5677},src={"Arcane Feedback (Ironforge)"}}
E["quest:6388"] = {t="quest",n="Gryth Thurden",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Gryth Thurden can send you back toward Loch Modan with a parcel. You carry the Honorary Picks from Golnir Bouldertoe for Brock Stoneseeker's mining apprentices, and the city's gryphon roost offers a way over the mountain roads.",h="In Ironforge, Gryth Thurden can send you back toward Loch Modan with a parcel.",sec={{t="A Courier for the Miners",b="You have traveled from Loch Modan to the Great Forge, where Golnir Bouldertoe gives you Honorary Picks for Brock Stoneseeker's mining apprentices. He points you to Ironforge's gryphon network instead of the mountain passes on foot. Carry the bundle across the city to the master handler, who can arrange your flight back.",sp=0},{t="Taking Wing to Thelsamar",b="Gryth Thurden oversees Ironforge's flight roosts in the great mountain hall. Gryphon routes link the city with dwarven settlements across Khaz Modan. After scouting the route and speaking with the local handler, you can ask Gryth to arrange transport back to Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar. The picks are bound for Brock Stoneseeker's apprentices, and the route joins mountain settlements by air.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Honorary Picks for?",a="Golnir Bouldertoe crafted the Honorary Picks in Ironforge as ceremonial tools for the students of Brock Stoneseeker, a mining instructor stationed in Thelsamar.",al={"honorary picks","why honorary picks","picks for brock"},it="item"},{q="Who is Gryth Thurden?",a="Gryth Thurden oversees Ironforge's flight routes from the dwarven capital to settlements across Khaz Modan and beyond.",al={"who is gryth thurden","ironforge gryphon master","gryth thurden lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Gryth Thurden located in Ironforge?",a="Gryth Thurden is at the Great Forge's flight roost, near Ironforge's main central thoroughfare and gates.",al={"gryth thurden location","where to find gryth thurden","ironforge flight master"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do I need to talk to Thorgrum Borrelson first?",a="Gryth Thurden can send a rider to Thelsamar only after you have spoken with Thorgrum Borrelson, the handler stationed in Loch Modan. Handlers dispatch riders along charted routes.",al={"thorgrum borrelson requirement","why need thelsamar flight path","cant fly to thelsamar"},gp=true},{q="What happens after giving the picks to Gryth Thurden?",a="After inspecting the parcel, Gryth prepares a gryphon flight so you can return to Thelsamar and deliver the tools directly to Brock Stoneseeker.",al={"what next after gryth thurden","next quest after gryth thurden"},it="next_step"},{q="Who sends you to Gryth Thurden?",a="Golnir Bouldertoe, an artisan working around Ironforge's Great Forge, gives you the picks and directs you to Gryth.",al={"who starts gryth thurden","who gives this quest"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Golnir Bouldertoe send you to Gryth Thurden?",a="Golnir Bouldertoe has prepared the Honorary Picks meant for Brock Stoneseeker's mining students out in Thelsamar. Instead of having you hike back down through the snowy pass on foot, Golnir directs you to Gryth Thurden, Ironforge's gryphon master, so you can learn how to arrange a gryphon flight directly back across the mountains.",al={"why send to gryth","golnir bouldertoe motive","why gryth thurden picks"},it="motive",add="05b277d3"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you rely on gryphons to cross treacherous peaks. They are a practical necessity and a point of ancestral pride linking the mountain halls.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you help Brock Stoneseeker's apprentices in Loch Modan with ceremonial picks forged in Ironforge to honor their craft.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can rely on Ironforge's gryphon roosts to carry envoys between Dun Morogh, Loch Modan, and the broader kingdoms."},kw={"flight master","golnir bouldertoe","gryth thurden","honorary picks","ironforge","loch modan","thelsamar","thorgrum borrelson"},rel={"zone:ironforge","quest:6392","npc:golnir-bouldertoe","npc:thorgrum-borrelson","subzone:thelsamar"},m={start="Golnir Bouldertoe",["end"]="Gryth Thurden",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6388},src={"Gryth Thurden (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6391"] = {t="quest",n="Ride to Ironforge",z="ironforge",s="Brock Stoneseeker sends you from Thelsamar to Ironforge with the names of his finest mining students. You carry his list to Golnir Bouldertoe at the Great Forge.",h="Brock Stoneseeker sends you from Thelsamar to Ironforge with the names of his finest mining students.",sec={{t="Taking to the Skies",b="Thorgrum Borrelson carries you from Thelsamar over Dun Morogh's snowy ridges to the mountain fortress. For many young mountaineers and travelers, this is their first flight on a gryphon.",sp=0},{t="Honors of the Deep Mountain Guild",b="At the Great Forge, Golnir Bouldertoe carves the students' names into ceremonial honorary picks. These honors recognize their hard work in Loch Modan's quarries and mines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this flight start and end?",a="Thorgrum Borrelson carries you from Thelsamar in Loch Modan to the flight roost by Ironforge's Great Forge.",al={"flight path route","where do i fly","ride destination"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Brock's List?",a="Brock Stoneseeker's list names his finest mining students in Thelsamar, so the guild in Ironforge can honor their diligence.",al={"brocks list lore","who is brock","what is the paper"},it="item"},{q="Who is Golnir Bouldertoe?",a="Golnir Bouldertoe represents the Deep Mountain Mining Guild at Ironforge's Great Forge. He receives rosters from local trainers and carves the students' names into honorary picks.",al={"golnir role","where is golnir","who is golnir bouldertoe"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after you deliver the list?",a="Once Golnir receives the roster, he sends you to Gryth Thurden, Ironforge's master gryphon handler, to learn about the kingdom's aerial routes.",al={"next quest","what to do after","follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why use a gryphon instead of walking?",a="The mountain road and tunnels reach Ironforge's Gates, but flying by gryphon shows how quickly Alliance travelers can move between settlements.",al={"why fly","can i walk to ironforge","why gryphon"},it="purpose"},{q="What is an honorary pick?",a="An honorary pick is a ceremonial tool the Deep Mountain Mining Guild gives to outstanding students of mining. Regional instructors teach them the basics of excavation and geology.",al={"honorary picks","pick reward","mining pick ceremony"}},{q="Why does Thorgrum Borrelson want you to ride to Ironforge?",a="Thorgrum Borrelson is Thelsamar's gryphon master in Loch Modan, and his trade depends on travelers taking wing from his roost. By arranging your flight to Ironforge to deliver Brock's list of promising mining students to Golnir Bouldertoe, he introduces you to the speed and convenience of gryphon travel while ensuring important guild correspondence reaches the capital without delay.",al={"thorgrum borrelson motive","why send to ironforge","why deliver brocks list"},it="motive",add="d8819fd3"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you see how the Deep Mountain Mining Guild honors promising miners from Loch Modan's pits by carving their names into picks.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a young Bronzebeard dwarf, your gryphon flight into the Great Forge marks a proud passage from rural outposts to the heart of the kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can rely on gryphon routes to link Khaz Modan's frontline garrisons with its capital."},kw={"brock's list","deep mountain mining guild","golnir bouldertoe","great forge","gryphon","kharanos","ride to ironforge","thorgrum borrelson"},rel={"npc:thorgrum-borrelson","npc:golnir-bouldertoe","zone:ironforge","subzone:great-forge"},m={start="Thorgrum Borrelson",["end"]="Golnir Bouldertoe",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6391},src={"Ride to Ironforge (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6392"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Brock",z="ironforge",s="You carry Brock Stoneseeker’s missive to Ironforge and receive Honorary Picks for his apprentices. Gryth Thurden can fly you back to Thelsamar.",h="You carry Brock Stoneseeker’s missive to Ironforge and receive Honorary Picks for his apprentices.",sec={{t="Taking to the Skies",b="Gryth Thurden oversees Ironforge’s gryphon flights from the city’s central platform. To fly to Thelsamar, you first need to have met its handler, Thorgrum Borrelson. Then Gryth can carry you and the picks over the mountains, returning Brock’s message and tools to the Loch.",sp=0},{t="Picks for the Pupils",b="Brock Stoneseeker teaches mining in Thelsamar and needs tools for his apprentices. The Honorary Picks will let young miners work the rich copper and tin veins in the hills around the Loch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brock Stoneseeker?",a="Brock Stoneseeker is a dwarf mining trainer in Thelsamar, Loch Modan. He teaches new miners to gather ore and stone from the surrounding hills.",al={"brock stoneseeker","who is brock","brock in thelsamar"},it="people"},{q="Why do I need to fly on a gryphon to finish this quest?",a="Gryth Thurden can fly you to Thelsamar because you have already visited its roost and spoken with Thorgrum Borrelson. Gryphons carry travelers only to aeries they have visited.",al={"why fly","flight path quest","gryphon ride"},gp=true},{q="What are the Honorary Picks for?",a="The Honorary Picks are mining tools Brock Stoneseeker needs for his new students in Loch Modan.",al={"honorary picks","what are the picks"},it="item"},{q="Who is Gryth Thurden?",a="Gryth Thurden is Ironforge’s gryphon master, stationed at the Great Forge. He manages flights to and from the capital across Khaz Modan and beyond.",al={"gryth thurden","ironforge flight master"},it="people"},{q="Can I just walk back to Thelsamar instead of flying?",a="You can walk back to Thelsamar and deliver the Honorary Picks to Brock Stoneseeker. The journey introduces you to gryphon routes, and Brock needs the tools safely in his hands.",al={"can i walk back","do i have to take gryphon"},gp=true},{q="Where in Thelsamar is Brock located?",a="Brock Stoneseeker is outdoors near Thelsamar’s forge and anvil, where he helps miners in Loch Modan.",al={"where is brock","brock stoneseeker location","find brock"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gryth Thurden want me to deliver the picks?",a="Gryth Thurden manages Ironforge's gryphon roosts and keeps the kingdom's flight routes connected. Brock Stoneseeker down in Thelsamar is waiting on an urgent shipment of Honorary Picks for his mining students. Since you have already charted the path between Ironforge and Thorgrum Borrelson's roost, Gryth uses this delivery both to fulfill Brock's supply needs and to ensure you master the art of gryphon travel across Khaz Modan.",al={"why does gryth want this","gryth thurden motive","why send picks to brock"},it="motive",add="c8277dbd"},{q="Why does Gryth Thurden send an adventurer instead of handling it himself?",a="Gryth Thurden cannot abandon his post at the Great Forge, where he oversees the constant flow of riders and the care of Ironforge's prized gryphons. Because you personally carried Brock's missive into the city and unlocked the flight route back to Thelsamar, you are the ideal courier to test the newly established link and bring the supplies straight back into the miner's hands.",al={"why does gryth need me","why send an adventurer to thelsamar","why not send a courier"},it="why_me",add="be2b1abc"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Delivering the Honorary Picks gives Loch Modan’s new miners tools for their work and carries on the dwarven tradition of excavation and prospecting.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know how Wildhammer gryphons and Ironforge handlers link the dwarven holds by air."},kw={"brock stoneseeker","flight master","gryphon","gryth thurden","honorary picks","ironforge","return to brock","thelsamar"},rel={"npc:brock-stoneseeker","quest:6388","subzone:thelsamar","zone:ironforge","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Gryth Thurden",["end"]="Brock Stoneseeker",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6392},src={"Return to Brock"}}
E["quest:6625"] = {t="quest",n="Alliance Trauma",z="ironforge",s="Across the Alliance, accomplished medics are sent to Theramore Isle for service. There, you study under Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen, chief physician of the Alliance's elite medical corps.",h="Across the Alliance, accomplished medics are sent to Theramore Isle for service.",sec={{t="A Call to the Field",b="Your skill with needle, cloth, and triage has drawn Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen's notice. From Theramore Isle, he leads Alliance Trauma, caring for the wounded in Kalimdor's fiercest warzones and beyond.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Theramore",b="In Ironforge, Nissa Firestone treats VanHowzen's personal summons as a rare privilege. Theramore Isle faces regional threats, skirmishes, and harsh wilderness, so grievously wounded soldiers arrive in a steady stream.\n\nYou cross the sea to Dustwallow Marsh. There, VanHowzen tests how calmly you assess the wounded against his rigorous triage standards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Alliance Trauma?",a="Alliance Trauma is the Alliance's elite medical corps, devoted to battlefield medicine and emergency triage. Chief Physician Gustaf VanHowzen leads it, treating critical wounds ordinary field dressings cannot manage.",al={"alliance trauma lore","who are alliance trauma"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends you on this quest?",a="Alliance first aid instructors send promising practitioners after they master the standard training in their cities. Nissa Firestone in Ironforge is one such instructor.",al={"who gives alliance trauma","ironforge first aid quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where do you have to travel?",a="You travel to Theramore Isle, a human port fortress on Kalimdor's eastern coast in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"where is vanhowzen","alliance trauma destination"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen?",a="Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen leads Alliance Trauma as its chief physician. He works at the military clinic in Theramore and is among the Alliance's foremost authorities on emergency medicine and surgical triage.",al={"gustaf vanhowzen","chief physician vanhowzen"},it="target"},{q="What happens after reporting to Doctor VanHowzen?",a="At Theramore, VanHowzen gives candidates a hands-on triage evaluation. They must show they can save waves of dying soldiers before he admits them to the upper ranks of field medicine.",al={"what comes after alliance trauma","triage quest next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the clinic based in Theramore instead of Stormwind or Ironforge?",a="Theramore is an active frontier garrison amid hostile marshlands, dangerous beasts, and territorial skirmishes. Critically wounded troops arrive constantly, giving its clinic the steady pressure needed for advanced trauma training.",al={"why theramore clinic","why dustwallow for trauma"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Nissa Firestone send you to Theramore?",a="Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen, the chief physician of Alliance Trauma, issued a personal request for you to join his ranks in Theramore. Nissa Firestone holds the renowned surgeon in the highest esteem and views working under him as an unmatched honor. She passes along the summons because she wants to ensure you do not squander such a rare medical opportunity.",al={"why does nissa want this done","nissa firestone motive","why send to theramore"},it="motive",add="a452e047"},{q="Why does Doctor VanHowzen ask for you specifically?",a="Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen needs capable, experienced field medics who can handle severe casualties under pressure. Having proven your exceptional mastery in first aid, you have caught the attention of the Alliance's senior surgical corps, prompting VanHowzen to summon you personally to Theramore to assess your skills under battlefield conditions.",al={"why me alliance trauma","why does vanhowzen want me","why send player to theramore"},it="why_me",add="a6ba6381"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance Trauma gives frontline fighters across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms access to skilled medics. They can stabilize critical injuries under fire.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may catch the eye of instructors like Nissa Firestone in Ironforge. She seeks promising practitioners from the Great Forge for medical service in Theramore."},kw={"alliance trauma","dustwallow marsh","first aid","ironforge","nissa firestone","theramore","triage","vanhowzen"},rel={"npc:doctor-gustaf-vanhowzen","npc:nissa-firestone","zone:dustwallow","topic:alliance"},m={start="Nissa Firestone",["end"]="Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen",faction="Alliance",id=6625},src={"Alliance Trauma (quest)"}}
E["quest:686"] = {t="quest",n="A King's Tribute",z="ironforge",s="King Magni Bronzebeard answers Sara Balloo with a lasting tribute to her fallen husband, Sully. He sends you across Ironforge with a royal commission for Grand Mason Marblesten.",h="King Magni Bronzebeard answers Sara Balloo with a lasting tribute to her fallen husband, Sully.",sec={{t="A Sovereign's Burden",b="Sara Balloo's plea weighs on King Magni Bronzebeard. War's harsh needs can be hard for common folk to understand, yet every soldier beneath the Alliance banner weighs on his conscience. He cannot undo a death on the front lines. He can see that Sully Balloo's sacrifice is remembered.",sp=0},{t="The Mason's Chisel",b="King Magni chooses a stone memorial for Sully, not empty words. He entrusts you with his royal commission and sends you across Ironforge to Grand Mason Marblesten. The master stonemason receives the king's personal charge and prepares to carve the fallen defender's memory into stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Sully Balloo?",a="Sully Balloo was a dwarven soldier who died defending the Thandol Span for the Alliance. After learning of his death, his widow, Sara Balloo, petitioned King Magni Bronzebeard.",al={"who is sully","sully balloo lore","who died"},it="people"},{q="Why does King Magni commission a memorial?",a="King Magni bears the weight of every dwarven life lost in the Alliance's struggles. He cannot restore Sully to his widow, so he commissions a lasting monument to honor the soldier's courage.",al={"why build memorial","magni motive","kings tribute purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Grand Mason Marblesten?",a="Grand Mason Marblesten is Ironforge's master stoneworker. He is entrusted with major civic and royal building projects throughout the city, and King Magni relies on him to sculpt Sully Balloo's memorial.",al={"who is marblesten","grand mason role"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You travel within Ironforge, starting at the High Seat with King Magni Bronzebeard and then going to Grand Mason Marblesten elsewhere in the capital.",al={"where is this quest","quest location"},it="place"},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Before this, you deliver Sara Balloo's heartfelt letter directly to King Magni Bronzebeard.",al={"prerequisites","previous quest"},gp=true},{q="Is this memorial only for Sully Balloo?",a="The tribute bears Sully Balloo's name and is meant to console his widow, Sara. It also honors every dwarven fighter who dies serving the Alliance.",al={"who does it honor","is it just for sully"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does King Magni choose you as custodian for the tribute?",a="You were the one who carried Sara Balloo's heartfelt plea directly into the High Seat, bringing her personal tragedy before the throne. Because you chose to hear a grieving widow's sorrow and deliver her words to the king, Magni entrusts you to see the royal honor carried out, making you the custodian of his bidding rather than delegating it to palace bureaucrats.",al={"why me kings tribute","why does magni send you","why pick me"},it="why_me",add="66401eff"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see King Magni's devotion to his people. Even the lowliest dwarven foot soldier is remembered by the throne.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance fighter, you know the fallen at the Thandol Span gave their lives guarding crucial supply lines between Khaz Modan and the northern kingdoms."},kw={"ironforge","magni bronzebeard","marblesten","memorial","sara balloo","sully balloo","thandol span"},rel={"npc:magni-bronzebeard","npc:grand-mason-marblesten","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance"},m={start="King Magni Bronzebeard",["end"]="Grand Mason Marblesten",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=686},src={"A King's Tribute"}}
E["quest:700"] = {t="quest",n="A King's Tribute",z="ironforge",s="Magni Bronzebeard gives Sully Balloo a memorial in Ironforge. Granite from Lordaeron keeps the fallen dwarf in his people's memory.",h="Magni Bronzebeard gives Sully Balloo a memorial in Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Monument Carved in Grief",b="King Magni Bronzebeard commissioned a monument for Sully Balloo, a dwarf who died serving his people. Grand Mason Marblesten carved it from fine granite brought from Lordaeron's war-torn lands. The monument stands in Ironforge, honoring soldiers whose sacrifices help preserve the dwarven kingdom.",sp=0},{t="A Sovereign's Reflection",b="When told the monument is complete, Magni considers stone and mortality. Carved rock can never equal a brave dwarf's life, he knows, yet he hopes the memorial endures. Then generations walking Azeroth may remember the heroes who bled to secure their tomorrow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is being honored by this memorial?",a="The memorial honors Sully Balloo, a brave dwarven soldier who gave his life fighting for his people and the Alliance.",al={"who is this memorial for","sully balloo monument","who died"},it="purpose"},{q="Why was the stone gathered from Lordaeron?",a="Grand Mason Marblesten needed fine granite for a lasting royal tribute. Lordaeron is known for exceptional quarried stone, though the region lies in ruin after the Scourge.",al={"why lordaeron stone","lordaeron granite","marblesten stone"},it="origin"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You meet Grand Mason Marblesten, then bring word to King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge's High Seat.",al={"where to turn in","who completes quest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does King Magni commission this tribute personally?",a="Magni believes rulers must honor the foot soldiers who defend their realms. He wants the memorial to remind future generations of the price common soldiers paid for their safety.",al={"why does magni care","magni bronzebeard sully balloo"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after the memorial is finished?",a="Reporting to King Magni completes the memorial chain. The statue remains in Ironforge as a permanent landmark honoring Sully Balloo.",al={"what comes next","kings tribute follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the masonry significance of the statue?",a="Grand Mason Marblesten is among Ironforge's most accomplished dwarven artisans. He shaped imported Lordaeron granite into a fitting national work of art for the monarch.",al={"marblesten role","grand mason craft"}},{q="Why does Grand Mason Marblesten send you to the King?",a="You were the one who braved the dangerous journey to the ruins of Lordaeron to retrieve the fine granite for the sculpture. Having secured the stone and made the tribute possible, Grand Mason Marblesten entrusts you with delivering the proud news directly to King Magni Bronzebeard that Sully Balloo's memorial is complete.",al={"why send me to Magni","why tell king magni","why marblesten sends player"},it="why_me",add="964451bf"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you share a tradition of honoring fallen ancestral warriors in enduring stone.",["faction:Alliance"]="The monument reminds you of the heavy toll recent conflicts exacted across Khaz Modan and the northern kingdoms.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you hear Magni honor the selfless valor of frontline soldiers like Sully Balloo, who gave everything in battle."},kw={"a king's tribute","granite","ironforge","lordaeron","magni bronzebeard","marblesten","memorial","sully balloo"},rel={"npc:magni-bronzebeard","npc:grand-mason-marblesten","quest:686","topic:dwarf","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Grand Mason Marblesten",["end"]="King Magni Bronzebeard",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=700},src={"A King's Tribute (3)"}}
E["quest:7025"] = {t="quest",n="Treats for Greatfather Winter",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, the dwarf playing Greatfather Winter asks you for a holiday treat. Bring five freshly baked gingerbread cookies and ice cold milk, and he thanks you with a festive gift.",h="In Ironforge, the dwarf playing Greatfather Winter asks you for a holiday treat.",sec={{t="A Long Day in the Seat",b="Smokywood Pastures sponsors the Winter Veil festivities in Ironforge. By the holiday tree in the Commons, a performer sits dressed as Greatfather Winter. For hours, he hears holiday wishes from citizens and eager children. He wears the guise of an immortal figure from ancient titan lore and dwarven myth.",sp=0},{t="Baking Holiday Cheer",b="After hearing requests for gifts all day, the performer grows hungry. He asks for five freshly baked gingerbread cookies and ice cold milk. The simple meal gives the exhausted festival worker a moment of relief. Your kindness spreads goodwill through Ironforge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Greatfather Winter in Ironforge?",a="Greatfather Winter sits beside the large holiday tree and the Smokywood Pastures display in the Commons of Ironforge, amid festive decorations.",al={"where is greatfather winter","greatfather winter location ironforge","ironforge santa location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you make Gingerbread Cookies?",a="Smokywood Pastures vendors near Greatfather Winter sell the recipe. You need Cooking skill, holiday spices from the festival merchant, and small eggs gathered from wild birds to bake the cookies.",al={"where to get gingerbread cookies","gingerbread recipe","how to bake cookies"},gp=true},{q="Where do I get Ice Cold Milk?",a="Innkeepers, food vendors, and drink sellers in major Alliance cities sell Ice Cold Milk. You can find it in the taverns across Ironforge.",al={"ice cold milk vendor","where to buy milk","milk ironforge"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is this Greatfather Winter the real mythic figure?",a="No. During Winter Veil, Smokywood Pastures hires a dwarf to portray the legendary figure associated with the titans.",al={"is greatfather winter real","who is the guy in ironforge","is he really greatfather winter"},it="identity"},{q="What does Greatfather Winter send you after finishing the quest?",a="After receiving the cookies and milk, Greatfather Winter thanks you with a Smokywood Pastures Gift Pack.",al={"treats for greatfather winter reward","mail from greatfather winter","smokywood pastures sampler"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="Can Horde players complete this specific quest?",a="This Ironforge offering is for Alliance travelers. Horde members have an equivalent offering that sends them to Greatfather Winter in Orgrimmar.",al={"can horde do this quest","horde treats for greatfather winter"},gp=true},{q="Why does Greatfather Winter want this done?",a="Greatfather Winter has been sitting in Ironforge listening to holiday wishes and greeting visitors all day without a break. While the Feast of Winter Veil brings joy to everyone else, all the talk of festival treats has left him exhausted and hungry, so he asks you to fetch him a much-needed snack.",al={"greatfather winter cookies motive","why does greatfather winter want cookies","why treats for greatfather winter"},it="motive",add="4b1f8d0d"},{q="What is the Ice Cold Milk for?",a="The Ice Cold Milk is simply a refreshing drink to wash down the batch of warm gingerbread cookies. Spending all day greeting travelers and shouting festive well-wishes is thirsty work, and nothing complements sweet festival biscuits better than an ice-cold beverage.",al={"why ice cold milk","milk for greatfather winter","ice cold milk purpose"},it="item",add="a70b2277"},{q="What are the Gingerbread Cookies for?",a="The Gingerbread Cookies serve as a personal holiday treat for Greatfather Winter himself. After handing out treats and hearing requests from citizen after citizen, he craves a traditional Winter Veil confection made with holiday spices to restore his energy.",al={"gingerbread cookies treats for greatfather","why gingerbread cookies","cookies for greatfather winter"},it="item",add="cc125737"},{q="Why does Greatfather Winter need you rather than getting treats himself?",a="Greatfather Winter cannot abandon his post amidst the festival festivities. He is stationed by the tree in Ironforge to greet the crowds and spread cheer for Smokywood Pastures, meaning he is stuck in place and relies on generous passersby like you to run errands for food.",al={"why does greatfather winter need me","why can't greatfather winter get his own cookies","why does greatfather winter ask an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="6bf2696f"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you bake gingerbread cookies with small eggs and holiday spices.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Greatfather Winter as an ancient legend tied to the titans and winter’s bounty. In the Commons, the figure enjoys cookies, bringing the myth down to earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find Winter Veil festivities in Ironforge. Visitors from across the Eastern Kingdoms gather by the holiday tree in the Commons."},kw={"feast of winter veil","gingerbread cookie","greatfather winter","ice cold milk","ironforge","smokywood pastures","treats for greatfather winter"},rel={"npc:greatfather-winter","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Greatfather Winter",faction="Alliance",id=7025,ri={"Gingerbread Cookie","Ice Cold Milk"}},src={"Treats for Greatfather Winter"}}
E["quest:8353"] = {t="quest",n="Chicken Clucking for a Mint",z="ironforge",s="At Hallow's End, Innkeeper Firebrew asks Ironforge visitors to cluck for a mint for Jesper, a young orphan in Stormwind. Alliance champions gather sweets from their capitals to bring him cheer.",h="At Hallow's End, Innkeeper Firebrew asks Ironforge visitors to cluck for a mint for Jesper, a young orphan in...",sec={{t="A Hallow's End Tradition",b="Jesper is sick, orphaned in Stormwind, and longs for Hallow's End sweets. Alliance champions gather treats for him from innkeepers in their capitals. So seasoned adventurers have reason to go door to door during the harvest-to-winter celebration.",sp=0},{t="Innkeeper Firebrew's Price",b="Innkeeper Firebrew keeps the Ironforge Mints at the Stonefire Tavern in Ironforge's Commons. A polite request won't do. Visitors flap their arms and cluck like chickens before he parts with one. The performance gives the tavern's patrons a laugh, and the mint helps bring holiday cheer to Jesper.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Innkeeper Firebrew want me to cluck like a chicken?",a="Innkeeper Firebrew asks you to cluck because Hallow's End calls for playful theater. Seasoned adventurers are too old to trick-or-treat, so he trades an Ironforge Mint for a comical performance and a laugh from the tavern patrons.",al={"why chicken cluck","firebrew chicken reason","why do i have to cluck"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Jesper and why am I getting mints for him?",a="Jesper is a young, sick orphan in Stormwind who longs for Hallow's End sweets. Alliance champions collect four special candies from the major Alliance cities, including the Ironforge Mint from Dun Morogh, to bring him holiday cheer.",al={"who is jesper","why get mints","jesper orphan"}},{q="Where does this quest fit into the Hallow's End holiday?",a="The Ironforge Mint is one of four regional candies gathered for Jesper during Hallow's End. Innkeepers in Stormwind and Darnassus, along with Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge, also ask for a specific theatrical gesture before giving up their city's candy.",al={"hallows end chain","jesper candy questline","quest order"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Firebrew?",a="Innkeeper Firebrew can be found at the Stonefire Tavern in Ironforge's Commons, where he serves drinks and boards travelers.",al={"where is firebrew","firebrew location","ironforge innkeeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do I receive for clucking?",a="Innkeeper Firebrew gives you an Ironforge Mint, a holiday candy to take back to Stormwind for Jesper's Hallow's End assortment.",al={"quest reward","what is the mint","ironforge mint"},gp=true},{q="Can Horde players complete this task?",a="No, only Alliance champions can take part. Horde adventurers gather treats for the orphan Spoops from innkeepers in Orgrimmar, the Undercity, and Thunder Bluff.",al={"is this alliance only","horde chicken quest","can horde do this"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you carry Ironforge's hospitality to Stormwind to cheer an orphaned child.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Ironforge's festival traditions leave room for a joke. Firebrew's demand shows that no patron takes themselves too seriously."},kw={"chicken","cluck","firebrew","hallow's end","innkeeper","ironforge mint","jesper","treats"},rel={"quest:8311","npc:innkeeper-firebrew","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Innkeeper Firebrew",faction="Alliance",id=8353},src={"Chicken Clucking for a Mint (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:8355"] = {t="quest",n="Incoming Gumdrop",z="ironforge",s="Talvash del Kissel keeps a Gnomeregan Gumdrop in Ironforge for a sick child in Stormwind. To earn it, you must give him a convincing train impression.",h="Talvash del Kissel keeps a Gnomeregan Gumdrop in Ironforge for a sick child in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Whimsical Toll",b="At Hallow’s End, trick-or-treaters visit the Alliance strongholds for treats. In Ironforge’s Mystic Ward, Talvash del Kissel keeps the Gnomeregan Gumdrop. He feels for the young orphan who hopes to receive it. Yet Talvash asks you to bring some mischief to the holiday with a convincing train impression.",sp=0},{t="Holiday Charity",b="Jesper is an ailing orphan in Stormwind City, hoping for four treats from across the Alliance. He wants nougat from Stormwind, a mint from Ironforge, marzipan from Darnassus, and a gumdrop from Gnomeregan. Your locomotive impression entertains Talvash and earns you the gumdrop. It brings Jesper closer to his holiday wish.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What do I need to do to complete Incoming Gumdrop?",a="Give Talvash del Kissel a convincing train impression. Once he hears the noise, he hands you the Gnomeregan Gumdrop.",al={"how to do incoming gumdrop","incoming gumdrop objective","talvash gumdrop trick"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Talvash del Kissel?",a="Talvash del Kissel is a gnome jeweler from Gnomeregan who lives in Ironforge’s Mystic Ward. During Hallow’s End, he gives Gnomeregan’s signature gumdrops to the Alliance.",al={"who is talvash","talvash del kissel lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Gnomeregan Gumdrop used for?",a="The Gnomeregan Gumdrop is one of four Hallow’s End treats gathered for Jesper, an orphan boy resting in Stormwind City’s orphanage.",al={"gnomeregan gumdrop purpose","what is the gumdrop for"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where can Talvash del Kissel be found?",a="Talvash del Kissel can be found in Ironforge’s Mystic Ward.",al={"where is talvash","talvash location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Talvash make you imitate a train?",a="Hallow’s End brings trick-or-treating, and Talvash asks for a harmless trick before handing over his treat. He wants a locomotive impression.",al={"why train noise","why do train for talvash"},it="motive"},{q="Is this quest available year-round?",a="No. It is available only during Hallow’s End, the annual autumn festival.",al={"can i do incoming gumdrop anytime","is this seasonal"},gp=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome in Tinker Town, offering a Gnomeregan Gumdrop during Hallow’s End can bring a cheerful reminder of home and mechanical ingenuity amid your people’s displacement.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you travel through the kingdoms for a festival gumdrop, helping an ailing child in Stormwind share in the holiday."},kw={"gnomeregan gumdrop","hallow's end","incoming gumdrop","ironforge","jesper","talvash del kissel","tinker town","train emote"},rel={"npc:talvash-del-kissel","quest:8311","zone:gnomeregan"},m={start="Talvash del Kissel",faction="Alliance",id=8355},src={"Incoming Gumdrop (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:8827"] = {t="quest",n="Winter's Presents",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, revelers gather for the Feast of Winter Veil. They direct travelers to Greatfather Winter beside the Smokywood Pastures stalls, where gifts wait beneath the holiday tree.",h="In Ironforge, revelers gather for the Feast of Winter Veil.",sec={{t="A Season of Cheer",b="Winter settles over Khaz Modan, and Ironforge fills with cheer for the Feast of Winter Veil. Revelers and holiday enthusiasts point passersby toward the decorated tree near the Smokywood Pastures vendors.",sp=0},{t="Smokywood Pastures and Greatfather Winter",b="Smokywood Pastures, a goblin enterprise, shares the season with Greatfather Winter. He greets visitors as goblin merchants remind gift recipients that festive treats and seasonal wares make gifts for friends and family.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to speak with Greatfather Winter?",a="A Holiday Enthusiast or a Wonderform Operator at an Ironforge PX-238 Winter Wondervolt machine invites you to visit Greatfather Winter at the decorated tree.",al={"quest giver","who starts winter's presents","who gives the quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Greatfather Winter in Ironforge?",a="In Ironforge, Greatfather Winter sits beside the festive tree and Smokywood Pastures vendor stalls. He welcomes visitors of every Alliance race.",al={"where is greatfather winter","greatfather winter location ironforge","find greatfather winter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the PX-238 Winter Wondervolt mentioned by the operator?",a="Goblin operators run the PX-238 Winter Wondervolt, a holiday invention that briefly disguises festival-goers as merry little holiday helpers.",al={"px-238","winter wondervolt","wondervolt machine"}},{q="Why is Smokywood Pastures involved in Winter Veil?",a="Smokywood Pastures is a goblin merchant organization that sponsors seasonal treats, holiday novelties, and feasts across Azeroth. It joins festive spirit with seasonal commerce.",al={"smokywood pastures role","why goblins winter veil","goblin holiday"},it="history"},{q="Can Horde players do this quest?",a="No. This invitation is for the Alliance in Ironforge. The Horde celebrates Winter Veil with Greatfather Winter in Orgrimmar.",al={"is this alliance only","horde winter presents","can horde turn this in"},gp=true},{q="What happens after speaking to Greatfather Winter?",a="Greatfather Winter welcomes you and says he has not forgotten you. He encourages you to look at the colorful packages beneath the holiday tree.",al={"what comes next","opening presents","after quest turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do the Wonderform Operator and Holiday Enthusiast send you to Greatfather Winter?",a="They simply want you to share in the cheer of the Feast of Winter Veil. Greatfather Winter has arrived in Ironforge and laid out gifts under the tree with the backing of Smokywood Pastures. While the Wonderform Operator is bound by duty to supervise the PX-238 Winter Wondervolt and cannot leave their post, they make sure passersby do not miss out on the holiday celebration and the presents waiting for them.",al={"why send me to greatfather winter","why winter's presents quest","holiday enthusiast motive"},it="motive",add="c93f10ff"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Ironforge gathers Alliance races for the winter season. Elves, humans, and gnomes come together to share festive cheer.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you welcome travelers to the Feast of Winter Veil in the Great Forge. Lively song, warm hearth fires, and cold ale fill your mountain home.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can marvel at the holiday contraptions brought in for the season. PX-238 Winter Wondervolts are operated across town."},kw={"feast of winter veil","greatfather winter","holiday enthusiast","ironforge","smokywood pastures","winter veil","winter's presents","wonderform operator"},rel={"npc:greatfather-winter","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Wonderform Operator / Holiday Enthusiast",["end"]="Greatfather Winter",faction="Alliance",id=8827},src={"Winter's Presents (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:8846"] = {t="quest",n="Five Signets for War Supplies",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, Field Marshal Snowfall trades commendation signets for supplies bound for the Grand Alliance’s war effort. You can exchange them for field rations, bandages, and combat gear to keep those serving on the home front equipped for the conflicts ahead.",h="In Ironforge, Field Marshal Snowfall trades commendation signets for supplies bound for the Grand Alliance’s...",sec={{t="Supplying the Front",b="Couriers and heroes bring Snowfall commendation signets earned through civic service. He trades them for survival rations and tactical gear bound for the fronts. Armies there need steady supplies as much as courage.",sp=0},{t="A Pragmatic Trade",b="Royal heralds offer public honor and civic standing for commendation signets. Snowfall offers another choice: five signets buy field gear, without pomp, glory, or official recognition. These goods help soldiers and volunteers stay alive as they march into hostile lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Field Marshal Snowfall?",a="Field Marshal Snowfall is a senior Alliance military officer stationed in Ironforge. He is one of the Alliance’s primary quartermasters, gathering materials and distributing supplies to soldiers and adventurers aiding the war effort.",al={"snowfall ironforge","field marshal snowfall","who is snowfall"},it="identity"},{q="What are Alliance Commendation Signets?",a="Alliance Commendation Signets are tokens awarded to citizens and adventurers who donate trade goods, bandages, herbs, and ores to support the Alliance’s mobilization.",al={"commendation signets","alliance signets","what are signets"},it="item"},{q="Why trade signets for supplies rather than prestige?",a="Trading signets for supplies gives you immediate, practical resources instead of civic reputation. For frontline fighters who need consumables, rations, and bandages, practical gear can matter more than ceremonial standing.",al={"why do this quest","signets for supplies worth it","snowfall supplies trade"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this exchange take place?",a="The exchange takes place in Ironforge. Field Marshal Snowfall stands near the war staging grounds and supply depots, coordinating shipments across Khaz Modan and beyond.",al={"where is snowfall","quest location","snowfall ironforge location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can I repeat this exchange?",a="Yes. Field Marshal Snowfall authorizes more supply bundles whenever you provide five commendation signets.",al={"is this repeatable","can i do this again","turn in more signets"},gp=true},{q="Does this turn-in grant reputation?",a="No. Field Marshal Snowfall warns that trading signets directly for personal supplies grants no civic recognition or prestige with the Alliance factions. Their value comes back as physical goods.",al={"does this give rep","ironforge rep signets","recognition for signets"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you help keep troops supplied with bandages and rations for major campaigns across Azeroth.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can take pride in seeing Ironforge’s halls arm all allied races."},kw={"commendation","ironforge","materiel","rations","signets","snowfall","war supplies"},rel={"npc:field-marshal-snowfall","topic:alliance"},m={start="Field Marshal Snowfall",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=8846,ri={"Alliance Commendation Signet"}},src={"Five Signets for War Supplies (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:8866"] = {t="quest",n="Bronzebeard the Elder",z="ironforge",s="During the Lunar Festival, travelers honor Bronzebeard the Elder beneath Ironforge. His greeting offers wisdom and a token of esteem. Across Khaz Modan, people revere their forebears and their long-lived heritage.",h="During the Lunar Festival, travelers honor Bronzebeard the Elder beneath Ironforge.",sec={{t="Homage to the Mountain Clan",b="During the Lunar Festival, spirits and venerable elders appear across Azeroth to share wisdom with travelers who honor the past. In Ironforge, Elder Bronzebeard carries the Bronzebeard clan’s stalwart resilience. He is quietly pleased when travelers come to pay their respects and the people honor the lineage of the old races.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Ancestral Esteem",b="No great trial or perilous journey is needed. Travelers pause to greet Elder Bronzebeard and offer their good wishes. He returns the greeting with a Coin of Ancestry, a festival token recalling the living bond between the present and the generations who forged Khaz Modan from stone and fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Bronzebeard?",a="Elder Bronzebeard is an ancestral dwarf honored during the Lunar Festival. In Ironforge’s subterranean stronghold, he greets visitors and celebrates their heritage.",al={"elder bronzebeard","who is the elder","ironforge elder"}},{q="What does honoring Elder Bronzebeard signify?",a="Greeting Elder Bronzebeard honors the ancestors during the Lunar Festival. He commends travelers who remember the roots and ancient sacrifices of Azeroth’s early races.",al={"why honor bronzebeard","bronzebeard elder purpose"}},{q="Where in Ironforge is Elder Bronzebeard found?",a="Elder Bronzebeard is found within Ironforge’s subterranean stronghold. Adventurers exploring the mountain city can reach him there.",al={"elder bronzebeard location","where is bronzebeard the elder","ironforge elder spot"}},{q="Can Horde players speak with Elder Bronzebeard?",a="Elder Bronzebeard acknowledges anyone who greets him. Horde travelers must brave Ironforge’s fortified depths and evade the dwarven guards to reach him.",al={"can horde do this quest","horde elder bronzebeard"}},{q="What reward does the elder bestow?",a="Elder Bronzebeard offers an ancestral blessing and a festival coin. Both are tokens of goodwill and respect for the ancient generations.",al={"elder bronzebeard reward","what token does he give"}},{q="Does this quest involve any combat?",a="No combat is needed to greet Elder Bronzebeard. The journey through hostile territory may still bring danger.",al={"do i have to fight","bronzebeard the elder fight"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, paying homage to Elder Bronzebeard brings you into communion with the noble ancestors who built your mountain kingdom from stone and iron.",["faction:Alliance"]="Elder Bronzebeard lives peacefully in Ironforge and welcomes Alliance members who come to honor ancient traditions beneath the mountain.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, reaching Elder Bronzebeard means entering Ironforge’s fortified core. Stealth or daring can carry you there to offer a greeting."},kw={"ancestors","bronzebeard","coin of ancestry","elder","ironforge","lunar festival"},rel={"npc:elder-bronzebeard"},m={start="Elder Bronzebeard",id=8866},src={"Bronzebeard the Elder"}}
E["quest:9261"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate the Scourge of Ironforge",z="ironforge",s="The Scourge presses against Ironforge’s gates, and Lieutenant Nevell calls for defenders. Undead troops gather beneath a hovering necropolis while glowing runic circles mark their camps.",h="The Scourge presses against Ironforge’s gates, and Lieutenant Nevell calls for defenders.",sec={{t="Death at the Mountain Gates",b="Lieutenant Nevell and the Argent Dawn watch the undead at Ironforge’s mountain entrance. Necropolises hover above Dun Morogh’s frigid heights, far from Lordaeron and the plagued lands of the north. They mean to stop the Scourge before it reaches the Bronzebeard fortress.",sp=0},{t="Unholy Inscriptions",b="Undead camps lie beneath the necropolis. Glowing runic circles and pulsing necrotic stones mark the ground, and scouts near the circles hear dark voices in the surrounding magic. Lieutenant Nevell believes the circles carry messages, though he does not know who the Scourge is contacting.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Nevell?",a="Lieutenant Nevell is an Argent Dawn officer stationed at Ironforge to coordinate its defense against the Scourge. He asks defenders to collect necrotic stones and learn the purpose of the unholy sigils around the invaders’ camps.",al={"nevell","lieutenant nevell","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Scourge attacking Ironforge?",a="Scourge forces camp beneath a necropolis outside Ironforge. Lieutenant Nevell asks defenders to thin their ranks and investigate the strange runic circles nearby.",al={"scourge outside ironforge","why undead in dun morogh","ironforge invasion"},it="threat"},{q="What are Dim Necrotic Stones?",a="Dim Necrotic Stones are taken from Scourge invaders and brought to the Argent Dawn as proof that undead have been slain.",al={"necrotic stones","dim necrotic stone","scourge stones"},it="item"},{q="What is the purpose of the glowing runic circles?",a="The glowing runic circles appear near Scourge forces. Lieutenant Nevell asks you to investigate their purpose.",al={"runic circles","glowing circles","what are the runes"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Lieutenant Nevell want this investigated?",a="With the Scourge marching upon Ironforge's doorstep and a Necropolis looming overhead, Lieutenant Nevell and the Argent Dawn refuse to remain idle. Strange runic circles glowing with unholy magic have appeared near the undead encampments outside the gates. Nevell knows these rituals bear grim significance, and he needs you to uncover what sinister forces the invaders are channeling before the city faces an even greater catastrophe.",al={"nevell motive","why investigate scourge ironforge","why does nevell want this done"},it="motive",add="4916b51d"},{q="Who are you sent to fight outside Ironforge?",a="You are sent against the vanguard of the Scourge encamped right outside the gates of Ironforge. Dispatched under the command of the Lich King and bolstered by a hovering Necropolis, these undead horrors seek to terrorize Dun Morogh and lay siege to the dwarven kingdom.",al={"who to fight","scourge targets ironforge","who am i fighting"},it="target",add="f222933f"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the rot spreading across Dun Morogh’s clean snows is an outrage. The mountain entrance is the threshold of your home.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, you know Ironforge is a vital pillar of trade and war. An undead foothold at its gates threatens supply routes across the Eastern Kingdoms.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you oppose the Scourge, enemies of the Holy Light. You are called to investigate the Lich King’s runic malice and purge his mindless thralls.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you know the whispers in the runic circles could threaten ordinary soldiers’ sanity. Resisting them takes spiritual strength."},kw={"argent dawn","dim necrotic stone","dun morogh","investigate the scourge of ironforge","ironforge","lich king","lieutenant nevell","necropolis","runic circle","scourge"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-nevell","zone:ironforge","topic:scourge","topic:argent-dawn","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Lieutenant Nevell",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=9261},src={"Investigate the Scourge of Ironforge"}}
E["subzone:commons"] = {t="subzone",n="Commons",z="ironforge",s="Travelers and traders fill the Commons just inside Ironforge's gates. From here, the mountain city's great caverns open before them, and merchants, travelers, and bankers arrive from across the Alliance.",h="Travelers and traders fill the Commons just inside Ironforge's gates.",sec={{t="The Commercial Hub of the Mountain",b="The Commons greets you just northeast of the Gates of Ironforge. Its market street is cut from mountain stone, with the Alliance Auction House, Stonefire Tavern, and the central bank in the Vault of Ironforge. Broad roads lead to the Great Forge, the Mystic Ward, and the Military Ward. Nearly everyone crossing the city passes its shops.",sp=0},{t="A Crossroads for the Alliance",b="Trade reaches the Commons from across the Eastern Kingdoms. Ironforge's central position and the underground Deeprun Tram to Stormwind bring travelers and merchants through its streets. Adventurers trade goods from across Azeroth, buy weapons at Steelfury's Weapon Emporium, or purchase reagents from Barim. Some gather beneath the inn's warm lanterns before setting out into the snows of Khaz Modan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes the Commons so crowded compared to other districts?",a="The Commons is crowded because the Alliance Auction House, the Vault of Ironforge, and Stonefire Tavern are here. Just inside the main gates, it is an easy place to meet and trade.",al={"why is commons busy","why so many players here","ironforge trade hub"},it="fame"},{q="Where does the Commons lead?",a="The Commons leads to nearly every major district in Ironforge. Southwest lies the city gates, northeast the Great Forge, east the Military Ward, and north the Mystic Ward.",al={"commons exits","how to leave commons","commons directions"},gp=true},{q="What key shops and services are found here?",a="The Commons has the Auction House and bank, along with the Ironforge Visitor's Center, Steelfury's Weapon Emporium, the Ironforge Armory, Barim's Reagents, and Fizzlespinner's General Goods.",al={"commons vendors","services in commons","ironforge commons amenities"},it="purpose"},{q="Is the bank located here?",a="Yes. The Vault of Ironforge, the city's main bank, stands across from the Auction House in the Commons.",al={"where is ironforge bank","ironforge vault","bank location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Commons?",a="The Commons serves as the primary commercial thoroughfare of Ironforge. Situated just past the city gates and connecting to nearly every other district, it functions as the vibrant economic heart of the dwarven capital. Here, travelers and citizens gather to trade goods at the Auction House, access the city vaults, stay at the Stonefire Tavern, or browse the wares of various local merchants.",al={"what is the commons","ironforge commons","about the commons"},it="place",add="1b528195"},{q="Is the Commons dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest. The Commons is one of the most secure and heavily populated districts in all of Khaz Modan. Protected by the mountain's impenetrable stone walls and patrolled constantly by vigilant Ironforge guards, visitors have nothing to fear from wild beasts or enemy incursions while conducting their business here.",al={"is commons dangerous","danger in the commons","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="e4c18740"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the Commons is a busy place to trade. Heroes from Teldrassil, Stormwind, and Gnomeregan come to auction valuable spoils and gather supplies.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard dwarf, you can see dwarven hospitality, industry, and commerce thriving deep within a frozen mountain."},kw={"auction house","bank","commons","ironforge","market","stonefire tavern","vault of ironforge"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:vault-of-ironforge","subzone:stonefire-tavern","subzone:gates-of-ironforge","subzone:great-forge","subzone:military-ward","subzone:mystic-ward","topic:alliance"},src={"Commons"}}
E["subzone:deeprun-tram"] = {t="subzone",n="Deeprun Tram",z="ironforge",s="Beneath the mountains, the Deeprun Tram carries travelers between Ironforge and Stormwind City. King Magni Bronzebeard commissioned it after the Second War, and its twin tracks carry citizens, soldiers, and goods between the Alliance capitals.",h="Beneath the mountains, the Deeprun Tram carries travelers between Ironforge and Stormwind City.",sec={{t="A Marvel of Subterranean Engineering",b="After the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard sought a faster way to send dwarven aid and supplies to Stormwind. Mountain passes made the journey slow, so he asked High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque to design an underground railway.\n\nGnomish engineers cut a route beneath a mountain and through a vast subterranean lake. Rats plagued the work, but the tram was finished. It carries thousands between Ironforge and Stormwind without charge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was the Deeprun Tram built?",a="After the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard needed a faster route for supplies and dwarven troops aiding Stormwind's rebuilding and defense. He commissioned High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque to design and build the underground railway linking the two capitals.",al={"why build the tram","tram purpose","who built deeprun tram"},it="purpose"},{q="How does the tram travel underwater?",a="While digging between Dun Morogh and Stormwind, gnomish engineers breached a vast subterranean lake. They built a sealed, reinforced glass tunnel through the water, where passengers can watch threshadons and sharks swim beside the track.",al={"tram water window","underwater tram","deeprun tram lake"}},{q="Why are there so many rats along the tracks?",a="The dark, damp shafts along the tracks give vermin room to breed. Gnomish station masters struggle to keep rats from chewing cables and overrunning platforms, and travelers and rat catchers like Monty sometimes help thin their numbers.",al={"deeprun rats","why rats in tram","rat problem"},it="threat"},{q="Is the tram free to ride?",a="Yes. Ironforge and Stormwind sponsor the tram as a civic and military service. It runs continuously without fare for citizens and Alliance allies.",al={"tram cost","tram ticket price","how much to ride tram"},gp=true},{q="What is the Deeprun Tram?",a="The Deeprun Tram is an underground and underwater railway system designed by gnomes that connects the Alliance capitals of Ironforge and Stormwind City. Consisting of double tracks and two sets of three wagons, it provides rapid, free transit between the dwarven mountain stronghold and the human kingdom.",al={"what is deeprun tram","deeprun tram info","about deeprun tram"},it="place",add="a94670c5"},{q="What happened at the Deeprun Tram?",a="Following the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard wanted a faster way to transport dwarven supplies and troops to help rebuild the battered kingdom of Stormwind. He commissioned High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque to design the subterranean line. Despite facing an unexpected subterranean lake and an ongoing rat invasion during construction, the railway was completed and became an indispensable lifeline for the Alliance.",al={"deeprun tram history","history of deeprun tram","how was deeprun tram built"},it="history",add="a0c9cf68"},{q="Who maintains and runs the Deeprun Tram?",a="Gnomish engineers work on the Deeprun Tram daily to ensure its mechanical wagons run smoothly and safely between the capitals. Alongside the engineering crews, tram stations and tunnels are frequented by local vendors, rail workers, and pest catchers like Monty, who tirelessly attempts to rein in the persistent rat population along the tracks.",al={"who runs deeprun tram","deeprun tram staff","who works in deeprun tram"},it="residents",add="c0b14a4e"},{q="Is the Deeprun Tram dangerous?",a="The tram ride itself is remarkably smooth and secure, engineered to safely ferry travelers beneath mountains and subterranean waters. Walking the tracks on foot, however, exposes you to speeding wagons and a notorious infestation of deeprun rats. Outside the reinforced glass tubes, aquatic predators like threshadons and sharks lurk in the dark lake depths, safely separated from passengers.",al={"deeprun tram danger","is the tram safe","hazards in deeprun tram"},it="danger",add="2e1a8782"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The railway is a gnomish engineering achievement, with advanced track propulsion, reinforced glasswork made to withstand the depths of a subterranean lake, and intricate electrical switching stations.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the tram links two of its most fortified capitals. It lets troops move quickly between them and supports their mutual defense."},kw={"deeprun tram","dwarven district","gelbin mekkatorque","magni bronzebeard","subterranean lake","subway","tinkertown","tram"},rel={"zone:ironforge","zone:stormwind","npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","npc:magni-bronzebeard","topic:alliance","topic:second-war","topic:gnome"},src={"Deeprun Tram"}}
E["subzone:forlorn-cavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Forlorn Cavern",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's northern depths, the Forlorn Cavern shelters those who keep to the shadows. Thieves, cutpurses, and practitioners of the dark arts conduct business there, far from the Great Forge and the dwarven guards.",h="In Ironforge's northern depths, the Forlorn Cavern shelters those who keep to the shadows.",sec={{t="Ironforge's Shaded Corner",b="Cold and damp, the Forlorn Cavern lies beneath Ironforge's clang of anvils and the Great Forge's heat. Its winding paths follow the northern edge of the underground lake, hidden between the Mystic Ward and the Hall of Explorers. Rogues and warlocks train there, and vendors serve them. Weapon merchants and fishermen work beside the lake as well.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Forlorn Cavern located in Ironforge?",a="The cavern lies in northern Ironforge, along the underground lake. Enter from the Mystic Ward to the east, or follow the tunnel west from the Hall of Explorers.",al={"forlorn cavern location","how to get to forlorn cavern","where is forlorn cavern"},gp=true},{q="Why do rogues and warlocks gather here?",a="The cavern's natural darkness and seclusion make it a discreet meeting place. Rogue and warlock trainers and merchants who serve both groups can be found there.",al={"why warlocks here","why rogues in forlorn cavern","shady district ironforge"},it="purpose"},{q="What shops and services can be found in the Forlorn Cavern?",a="The cavern has rogue and warlock trainers, Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms for practitioners of dark magic, the Stoneblade weapon shop, and The Traveling Fisherman, an angling supply post.",al={"forlorn cavern vendors","shops in forlorn cavern"},gp=true},{q="What is the Forlorn Cavern?",a="The Forlorn Cavern is a dark, winding district wrapped around an underground lake deep within Ironforge. Tucked away between the Mystic Ward and the Hall of Explorers, its secluded shadows provide a quiet refuge for Ironforge's less savory residents, including local rogues, covert warlocks, and niche merchants who prefer to operate away from prying dwarven eyes.",al={"what is forlorn cavern","forlorn cavern overview","about forlorn cavern"},it="place",add="307bd9d1"},{q="Is the Forlorn Cavern dangerous?",a="While it is guarded as part of Ironforge, you should still tread carefully. The cavern's dim corners shelter shady characters, thieves, cutpurses, and practitioners of dark fel magic. As long as you keep your wits about you and respect the delicate business being conducted, the district remains peaceful enough for travelers to pass through unharmed.",al={"is forlorn cavern safe","danger in forlorn cavern","threats in forlorn cavern"},it="danger",add="15f7ff40"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can find trainers and supplies in this Alliance hub in Khaz Modan. Poisons and specialized blades are sold along its damp stone walkways.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can train and find supplies at Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms in this secluded part of Ironforge."},kw={"bonegrip","forlorn cavern","hall of explorers","ironforge lake","mystic ward","rogue trainers","stoneblade","warlock trainers"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:mystic-ward","subzone:hall-of-explorers"},src={"Forlorn Cavern"}}
E["subzone:gates-of-ironforge"] = {t="subzone",n="Gates of Ironforge",z="ironforge",s="From Dun Morogh, travelers climb to the Gates of Ironforge, where a stone king guards the way into the dwarven capital. The gates open in the mountain face, with High King Modimus Anvilmar's statue just inside.",h="From Dun Morogh, travelers climb to the Gates of Ironforge, where a stone king guards the way into the...",sec={{t="The Threshold of the Mountain",b="From central Dun Morogh, you climb a winding, fortified ramp through the snowy lowlands to the Gates of Ironforge. Beyond the great portal stands a stone likeness of High King Modimus Anvilmar. He united the dwarven clans before the War of the Three Hammers. The passage opens into the Commons, where Ironforge's trade and banking are centered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the Gates of Ironforge lead?",a="The Gates of Ironforge lead from Dun Morogh into Ironforge. You emerge in the southwestern Commons, the city's center of trade and banking.",al={"ironforge entrance","where do the gates go","gates of ironforge location"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is the statue inside the gates depicting?",a="The statue just inside the entrance depicts High King Modimus Anvilmar. He ruled all dwarven clans before political rifts divided them into the Bronzebeard, Wildhammer, and Dark Iron factions.",al={"ironforge gate statue","giant dwarf statue","who is the statue at the gate"},it="identity"},{q="How do you reach the gates from Dun Morogh?",a="From central Dun Morogh, head north and climb the broad, fortified stone ramp cut into the mountainside. It leads straight to the fortress's outer threshold.",al={"how to get into ironforge","path to ironforge gates","ironforge ramp"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What are the Gates of Ironforge?",a="The Gates of Ironforge, also known as the Ironforge Main Gate, form the monumental entrance carved directly into the mountain face, connecting the snowy wilderness of Dun Morogh with the dwarven capital city inside. Dominating the landscape, these massive stone portals welcome travelers arriving from the great ramp to the south, leading them straight past an imposing statue of High King Modimus Anvilmar and into the bustling Commons.",al={"what are the gates of ironforge","ironforge main gate","gates of ironforge overview"},it="place",add="d3165cf1"},{q="Are the Gates of Ironforge dangerous?",a="No, the Gates of Ironforge are completely safe for members of the Alliance and peaceful visitors. Guarded vigilantly by the stalwart mountain kings and Ironforge guards, this grand threshold is heavily fortified against any hostile incursions, standing as an impenetrable defense for the underground kingdom against the troggs, frost trolls, and wild beasts roaming the crags of Dun Morogh.",al={"is gates of ironforge safe","ironforge gate danger","are the gates safe"},it="danger",add="d5c3b229"},{q="Why are they called the Gates of Ironforge?",a="They are named quite literally for their function: they serve as the grand, fortified main gateway into Ironforge, the ancient mountain home of the Bronzebeard dwarves. Through these colossal arches, visitors pass from the harsh elements of central Dun Morogh into the subterranean fires and stone halls of the kingdom itself.",al={"why called gates of ironforge","gates of ironforge name meaning","ironforge main gate name"},it="name",add="7ab63378"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Beneath High King Modimus Anvilmar's likeness, remember the ancient era when all dwarven clans lived beneath one mountain as a single kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="You enter the Gates of Ironforge, one of the Alliance's most fortified strongholds. From Dun Morogh's frigid valleys, it is nearly impossible to besiege."},kw={"commons","dun morogh","gates of ironforge","ironforge entrance","ironforge main gate","modimus anvilmar"},rel={"zone:ironforge","zone:dunmorogh","subzone:commons","subzone:anvilmar"},src={"Gates of Ironforge"}}
E["subzone:great-forge"] = {t="subzone",n="Great Forge",z="ironforge",s="At Ironforge’s center, the Great Forge keeps its fires burning and smiths at work. Its Great Anvil draws people from across the mountain city.",h="At Ironforge’s center, the Great Forge keeps its fires burning and smiths at work.",sec={{t="Heart of the Mountain",b="The Great Forge was the first structure the early dwarves built beneath Ironforge Mountain. The capital grew outward in rings around it. Molten stone and slag run from giant foundries through glowing channels, lighting the cavern with an amber haze.\n\nAt the center, Master of the Forge Myolor Sunderfury oversees the massive Great Anvil. Masters of metalwork gather around its rim to hammer armor, tools, and weapons day and night.",sp=0},{t="Hub of the Alliance",b="Smithing is only part of the Great Forge’s work. Guild offices, supply shops, and the city’s main gryphon roost ring the chamber. Gryth Thurden tends the roost, where travelers from across the Alliance mingle amid the hammer blows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the city named after this forge?",a="The Great Forge was the first part of the settlement the dwarves carved beneath the mountain. As the halls spread outward from its central chamber, they named the city Ironforge for the great furnace at its heart.",al={"why ironforge named ironforge","city namesake","ironforge origin"},it="name"},{q="What notable items have been created here?",a="Dwarven smiths have made generations of weapons and armor on the Great Anvil, including historic masterpieces. The forge’s fires have never been allowed to go cold.",al={"what was made at the great anvil","great forge famous weapons"},it="history"},{q="Who oversees the forge?",a="Myolor Sunderfury directs the Great Forge’s daily work and upkeep as Keeper of the Great Forge.",al={"keeper of the great forge","who runs the forge"},it="residents"},{q="Why is it always so crowded here?",a="The Great Forge lies at Ironforge’s center and connects to the outer ring and nearby districts. Its crafting trainers, shops, and central gryphon roost draw citizens, couriers, and travelers through the chamber.",al={"why so many people at the forge","why is the forge busy"}},{q="What is the Great Forge?",a="The Great Forge is the fiery heart and namesake of Ironforge. Situated at the very center of the subterranean mountain city, it is a bustling, soot-filled hub centered around the legendary Great Anvil. Ringed by roaring foundries, busy shops, trade trainers, and the city's gryphon roost, the forge never shuts down, serving as both an economic powerhouse and the lively crossroads of dwarven life.",al={"what is great forge","great forge ironforge","about the great forge"},it="place",add="eab323ad"},{q="Is the Great Forge dangerous?",a="Within the secure underground borders of Ironforge, you are safe from wild beasts and hostile armies, guarded by stalwart dwarven sentries. However, the forge itself is an active industrial marvel filled with open troughs of molten slag, blistering heat, and heavy machinery. A careless misstep over the railing or into the blazing pits will quickly prove fatal to anyone unprepared.",al={"is great forge dangerous","great forge hazards","can you fall in great forge"},it="danger",add="dc416ec6"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The Great Anvil is the Alliance’s foremost smithing site, with high-ranking trainers at the heart of the city.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, the Great Forge is the foundation of civilization beneath the mountain. Its fires keep centuries of smithing tradition alive."},kw={"foundry","great anvil","great forge","gryth thurden","ironforge","magni bronzebeard","myolor sunderfury"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:high-seat","npc:magni-bronzebeard","quest:6388","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","zone:stormwind"},src={"Great Forge"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-arms"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Arms",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge’s Military Ward, the Hall of Arms readies the city’s forces for battle. Command staff oversee the troops while warriors and hunters train, and machines are prepared for war.",h="In Ironforge’s Military Ward, the Hall of Arms readies the city’s forces for battle.",sec={{t="Heart of the Mountain's Arsenal",b="The Hall of Arms commands Ironforge’s armed forces from the Military Ward’s southeastern corner. Veteran instructors train warriors and hunters there, while the facility stores and stages machines of war. Steam tanks are assembled and maintained for Alliance battlefields. Gyrocopters and flying machines ride industrial conveyor belts through shafts in the cavern ceiling, then launch toward the Ironforge Airfield above.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Hall of Arms?",a="The Hall of Arms commands Ironforge’s military forces. It trains warriors and hunters and stores, maintains, and deploys war machines such as steam tanks and gyrocopters.",al={"what is hall of arms","hall of arms role","why hall of arms exists"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do the flying machines launched from the ceiling go?",a="Conveyor systems carry flying machines through shafts in the ceiling to the Ironforge Airfield on the mountain slopes above. This chimney is one of the only direct exits from the mountain besides the main gates.",al={"ceiling shaft ironforge","flying machine tunnel","where do copters go"}},{q="Who can I find training inside the Hall?",a="Warrior and hunter instructors train inside the Hall of Arms. Alliance battlemasters also organize troop movements and enlistments for battlefronts across the continent.",al={"trainers in hall of arms","who teaches here"},it="residents"},{q="Where is the Hall of Arms located?",a="The Hall of Arms stands at the back of Ironforge’s Military Ward, in the city’s southeastern quadrant.",al={"hall of arms location","how to get to hall of arms"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Hall of Arms?",a="The Hall of Arms serves as the command center and primary headquarters of Ironforge's military power. Located within the mountain city's Military Ward, it functions as a vital arsenal, training barracks, and mechanical depot where dwarven siege engines and flying machines are built, maintained, and readied for war across the Alliance.",al={"what is hall of arms","hall of arms info","about hall of arms"},it="place",add="b2a6f890"},{q="Is the Hall of Arms dangerous?",a="Not for citizens and allies of Ironforge. While it bristles with dwarven weaponry, siege machinery, and heavily armed troops, it is one of the most secure bastions in the kingdom. Only those foolish enough to threaten the city or cross the Alliance need fear the firepower assembled inside.",al={"is hall of arms safe","hall of arms danger","danger hall of arms"},it="danger",add="db189d23"},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Arms?",a="The complex earns its name by serving as the kingdom's central arsenal and martial heart. It is the repository where Ironforge gathers its arms—from personal weapons and armor used to drill warriors and hunters to heavy mechanized war machines like steam tanks and gyrocopters.",al={"why named hall of arms","hall of arms name origin","hall of arms meaning"},it="name",add="15a89202"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Khaz Modan’s union of martial discipline and mechanical ingenuity in the Hall of Arms. Tanks and aerial squadrons protect the mountain kingdom.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can find dwarven armsmen and veterans at the Hall of Arms for instruction and battlemaster leadership."},kw={"battlemasters","dwarven army","flying machines","hall of arms","ironforge","military ward","steam tanks"},rel={"subzone:military-ward","zone:ironforge","subzone:ironforge-airfield","topic:alliance","subzone:command-center"},src={"Hall of Arms"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-explorers"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Explorers",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, the Hall of Explorers draws the dwarves who seek their people's origins. The Explorers' League studies Azeroth's past here.",h="In Ironforge, the Hall of Explorers draws the dwarves who seek their people's origins.",sec={{t="Headquarters of the League",b="In northeastern Ironforge, the Hall of Explorers fills a cavern with scholars and field agents. High Explorer Muninn Magellas directs their work as they arrange digs in distant lands. Those expeditions bring back relics, ancient titan machinery, and prehistoric bones. At the hall's center, the Library keeps historical lore. Visitors may see its displays, while other records remain restricted.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hall of Explorers used for?",a="The Hall of Explorers is the Explorers' League headquarters and museum. Scholars study reports, catalog excavation relics, and arrange digs to learn about the dwarves' origins and ancient Azeroth.",al={"hall of explorers purpose","what happens here","explorers league base"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the operations here?",a="High Explorer Muninn Magellas directs the hall's expeditions, museum, and research archives.",al={"who runs hall of explorers","explorers league leader","high explorer"},it="in_charge"},{q="How does this place connect to the rest of Ironforge?",a="The Hall of Explorers lies in northeastern Ironforge. Archways connect it to the Great Forge to the southwest, the Forlorn Cavern to the west, and Tinker Town to the south.",al={"how to get here","hall of explorers exits","where is hall of explorers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Hall of Explorers?",a="The Hall of Explorers, sometimes called the Assembly of Explorers, is a prominent northeastern district within Ironforge. It serves as the world headquarters of the dwarven Explorers' League. Beyond housing offices and research archives, it acts as a grand museum and library displaying ancient relics, massive skeletons, and historical tomes recovered from excavations across Azeroth.",al={"what is hall of explorers","hall of explorers ironforge","assembly of explorers"},it="place",add="f8b05ac5"},{q="Is the Hall of Explorers dangerous?",a="Not at all. The hall rests safely within the heavily fortified heart of Ironforge. While the expeditions sent out into the wilds face perilous ruins, hostile beasts, and ancient curses, the district itself is a quiet, scholarly sanctuary filled with archivists, archaeologists, and Alliance dignitaries studying their finds.",al={"is hall of explorers dangerous","danger hall of explorers","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="4a4e8160"},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Explorers?",a="The district takes its name directly from its founding tenants and leaders, the dwarven Explorers' League. Established to unearth the origins of the dwarven race and piece together titan history, the League turned this wing of the mountain city into the central staging ground and archive for its intrepid explorers.",al={"why hall of explorers","why is it named hall of explorers","hall of explorers name origin"},it="name",add="eaed4071"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarven adventurer, you can explore relics gathered here as the League seeks your people's ancient origins and their connection to the Titans."},kw={"archaeology","explorers' league","hall of explorers","ironforge library","magellas","museum"},rel={"topic:explorers-league","subzone:library-ironforge","zone:ironforge","subzone:great-forge","subzone:tinker-town","subzone:forlorn-cavern","quest:301","quest:2300"},src={"Hall of Explorers"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-mysteries"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Mysteries",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge’s Mystic Ward, the Hall of Mysteries gathers dwarven and gnomish practitioners for faith and arcane study. They read ancient texts, learn the Holy Light, and weave enchantments within its blue-lit halls.",h="In Ironforge’s Mystic Ward, the Hall of Mysteries gathers dwarven and gnomish practitioners for faith and...",sec={{t="A Temple of Magic and Faith",b="Blue and purple light marks the Hall of Mysteries among Ironforge’s stone, iron, and heavy plate. Five soaring pillars shelter scholars in flowing robes. Here, the dwarven priesthood and the Order of the Silver Hand hold their headquarters within Khaz Modan. They join arcane study with devotion to the Holy Light.\n\nYoung clerics and knights study texts such as the Tome of Divinity here. They receive guidance before traveling onward to Stormwind’s Cathedral of Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Hall of Mysteries?",a="The Hall of Mysteries brings divine devotion and arcane learning together in Ironforge. Dwarven and gnomish priests, paladins, and mages gather there to study scripture, practice their crafts, and train newcomers.",al={"what is this place","hall of mysteries purpose","why visit hall of mysteries"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the clergy here?",a="High Priest Rohan oversees the priesthood in the hall and guides dwarven practitioners of the Light. Paladin mentors such as Valgar Highforge direct the city’s knights of the Silver Hand.",al={"who runs hall of mysteries","priest leader ironforge","who is high priest rohan"},it="in_charge"},{q="How does it compare to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind?",a="Stormwind’s Cathedral of Light is devoted to holy faith and ceremonial worship. The Hall of Mysteries joins holy study with arcane scholarship, and its atmosphere is scholarly and quiet.",al={"cathedral of light vs hall of mysteries","is it like stormwind cathedral"},it="place"},{q="Can paladins complete their training trials here?",a="Yes. Dwarven paladins study the Tome of Divinity at the hall under the Silver Hand’s mentorship. Their instruction and sacred trials test compassion, devotion, and courage.",al={"paladin quests ironforge","tome of divinity ironforge","dwarf paladin quests"},gp=true},{q="What is the Hall of Mysteries?",a="The Hall of Mysteries is a grand temple and sanctuary located within Ironforge's Mystic Ward. Dominated by a soft blue-purple glow and towering geometric pillars, it serves as the capital's central hub for both divine devotion and the arcane arts. Within its chambers, dwarven and gnomish scholars, priests, paladins, and mages gather to study, practice their arts, and instruct new apprentices.",al={"what is hall of mysteries","hall of mysteries ironforge","mystic ward temple"},it="place",add="1847c72f"},{q="Who resides in the Hall of Mysteries?",a="The hall is populated primarily by dwarven and gnomish scholars clad in flowing robes, contrasting with the heavy plate seen elsewhere in Ironforge. Its resident clergy and mentors include High Priest Rohan of the Church of the Light and Valgar Highforge of the Order of the Silver Hand, alongside esteemed mage instructors who guide students in arcane lore.",al={"who lives in hall of mysteries","hall of mysteries inhabitants","who is in hall of mysteries"},it="residents",add="e1807a94"},{q="Is the Hall of Mysteries dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest. The Hall of Mysteries is a thoroughly secure sanctuary deep in the heart of Ironforge. Guarded by the kingdom's finest paladins, priests, and mages, it is a safe refuge for Alliance citizens seeking healing, spiritual contemplation, or academic study.",al={"is hall of mysteries safe","danger hall of mysteries","enemies in hall of mysteries"},it="danger",add="68d8f867"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For dwarven champions of the Silver Hand, the hall is where masters assign trials of virtue and grant access to the sacred Tome of Divinity.",["class:Priest"]="High Priest Rohan guides acolytes of the Light through spiritual lessons here. Promising priests then travel south to confer with Stormwind’s leadership."},kw={"hall of mysteries","ironforge","mage","mystic ward","paladin","priest","rohan","silver hand","tome of divinity"},rel={"subzone:mystic-ward","zone:ironforge","npc:high-priest-rohan","subzone:cathedral-of-light","quest:1641","topic:light","zone:stormwind","topic:dwarf"},src={"Hall of Mysteries"}}
E["subzone:high-seat"] = {t="subzone",n="High Seat",z="ironforge",s="King Magni Bronzebeard holds court in High Seat, between the Commons and the Great Forge. His advisors and historians gather there, and a sealed passage leads down to Old Ironforge.",h="King Magni Bronzebeard holds court in High Seat, between the Commons and the Great Forge.",sec={{t="Heart of Dwarven Rule",b="King Magni Bronzebeard hears petitioners and meets with his advisors in High Seat. Royal Historian Archesonus and Senator Barin Redstone stand at his side. From here, Magni directs the defense of the Alliance's northern bastions. High Seat is the seat of power for Khaz Modan, and he leads the kingdom through troubling times across Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Gateway to Old Ironforge",b="A heavy doorway at the back of the throne room leads down into Old Ironforge. The lower ruins are ancestral halls the dwarves carved before the city was reconfigured around the Great Forge. The passage is sealed and guarded, keeping general traffic from the ancient halls beneath the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules from the High Seat?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard rules Ironforge from the throne in High Seat. He hears his subjects and directs the affairs of the Bronzebeard clan. He also coordinates military and diplomatic matters with the Grand Alliance.",al={"who is on the throne","ironforge king","magni throne room"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is the High Seat located in Ironforge?",a="High Seat lies between the Commons and the Great Forge, connected directly to Ironforge's outer ring. Citizens and envoys can reach the chamber from there.",al={"where is high seat","find high seat","throne room location"},gp=true},{q="What is the sealed corridor at the back of the throne room?",a="The large archway at the rear of High Seat leads into Old Ironforge, the ancestral ruins beneath the modern mountain city. Access to the lower passages is restricted.",al={"door behind magni","old ironforge door","high seat basement"}},{q="Who else can be found advising the King here?",a="Royal Historian Archesonus and Senator Barin Redstone advise King Magni in High Seat.",al={"high seat npcs","magni advisors"},it="residents"},{q="What is the High Seat?",a="The High Seat, also known as the High Throne, is the great throne room of the kingdom of Ironforge. Situated at the very heart of the mountain city just off the Great Forge, this grand stone hall is where the dwarven monarch holds court, receives emissaries, and hears petitions from subjects across Khaz Modan.",al={"what is high seat","ironforge throne room","high seat ironforge"},it="place",add="dcfee083"},{q="Is the High Seat dangerous?",a="Not if you are a friend to the Alliance. It is the heart of dwarven governance, heavily guarded by the King's personal protectors and veteran dwarven guards. Unless an invading Horde army manages to breach Ironforge's deep mountain defenses, visitors under the King's peace have nothing to fear within these halls.",al={"is high seat safe","high seat danger","threats in the high seat"},it="danger",add="e56e0189"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you look to High Seat, where King Magni Bronzebeard leads the people of Khaz Modan and carries on their rule.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to High Seat for dwarven counsel. Envoys, advisors, and royal decrees gather there."},kw={"archesonus","barin redstone","bronzebeard","high seat","ironforge","magni","throne"},rel={"npc:magni-bronzebeard","zone:ironforge","subzone:old-ironforge","npc:royal-historian-archesonus","subzone:great-forge","subzone:commons"},src={"High Seat"}}
E["subzone:library-ironforge"] = {t="subzone",n="Library (Ironforge)",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, the Explorers' League keeps its histories and recovered relics in the Library. The eastern wing of the Hall of Explorers holds books and artifacts gathered across Azeroth.",h="In Ironforge, the Explorers' League keeps its histories and recovered relics in the Library.",sec={{t="Heart of the Explorers' League",b="In the Hall of Explorers, dwarven scholars study relics and field reports in a great chamber. The Explorers' League keeps the Library, where shelves hold chronicles of the War of the Three Hammers, the ancient Troll Wars, and the origins of the dwarven race. Librarian Mae Paledust helps visitors find rare books and records.",sp=0},{t="The Museum Displays",b="Curator Thorius oversees displays of finds from deep excavations, abandoned ruins, and distant shorelines. League members study, preserve, and display these objects. The collection ranges from crude murloc idols and carved knives to relics recovered frozen in northern ice. Curators record each find as they piece together the history of the Titans and early Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Library in Ironforge?",a="The Library is the Explorers' League's main archive and museum. League members bring recovered artifacts, tomes, and field notes there to be cataloged, deciphered, and preserved for the dwarven people and the Alliance.",al={"ironforge library purpose","what is this place","hall of explorers library"},it="purpose"},{q="Who manages the collections here?",a="Librarian Mae Paledust helps visitors with written collections and archival searches. Curator Thorius oversees the museum wing and its physical historical artifacts.",al={"who runs the library","ironforge librarian","museum curator"},it="residents"},{q="What kind of books can be read here?",a="The Library holds histories of ancient and modern events, including the Old Gods, the Dragonflights, the Troll Wars, the War of the Three Hammers, the Rise of the Horde, and the formation of the Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"ironforge books","readable tomes","what lore is here"},it="item"},{q="Where in Ironforge is the Library located?",a="The Library occupies the eastern wing of the Hall of Explorers, in Ironforge's northeastern quadrant.",al={"ironforge library location","how to find the library"},gp=true},{q="What is the Library of Ironforge?",a="The Library is an expansive repository of knowledge, history, and ancient artifacts housed within the eastern wing of the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. Arguably the largest singular structure in the mountain city, it functions as both an immense archive of historical tomes and an active museum. It serves as the primary base of operations for the dwarven scholars and field agents of the Explorers' League.",al={"what is the library","library ironforge info","ironforge library"},it="place",add="0caa8ddd"},{q="Is the Ironforge Library dangerous?",a="The Library rests safely within Ironforge, bustling with scholars, archivists, and members of the Explorers' League studying recovered relics and historical records.",al={"is library dangerous","library danger ironforge","threats in the library"},it="danger",add="8f38528b"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can find accounts here of the Awakening and the War of the Three Hammers. These records are kept in the hall King Magni Bronzebeard devoted to uncovering your Titan origins.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can consult records from the Alliance of Lordaeron and eyewitness reports from the Second and Third Wars in the Library's strategic archive."},kw={"books","curator thorius","explorers league","hall of explorers","ironforge","library","mae paledust","museum"},rel={"subzone:hall-of-explorers","zone:ironforge","topic:explorers-league","topic:alliance","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","subzone:grim-batol","topic:old-god","topic:troll"},src={"Library (Ironforge)"}}
E["subzone:military-ward"] = {t="subzone",n="Military Ward",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge, red banners gather the city's defenders in the Military Ward. Its halls, barracks, weapons masters, siege engines, and flying machines ready the mountain city's military.",h="In Ironforge, red banners gather the city's defenders in the Military Ward.",sec={{t="The Anvil of Dwarven Might",b="Along the northern edge of Ironforge, the Military Ward gathers the city's defenses. At its heart, the Hall of Arms holds warrior and hunter trainers and battlemasters. Nearby hangars house dwarven flying machines and steam tanks.\n\nDrill squares and training dummies fill the ward, with supply shops close at hand. Craghelm's Plate and Chain, Goldfury's Hunting Supplies, and Timberline Arms serve those who train and defend the city. Mountaineers and city defenders gather here before setting out.",sp=0},{t="A Garrison under Banners of War",b="Red banners cover the Military Ward, unlike the Commons' pale blue and the Great Forge's fiery orange. Soldiers drill and inspect their weapons, then gather with off-duty guards for ale at Bruuk's Corner.\n\nWeapon Master Buliwyf Stonehand teaches recruits the ancient martial traditions of the dwarves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Military Ward?",a="Ironforge's dwarven army gathers in the Military Ward, alongside warrior and hunter trainers, weapons merchants, and siege machinery.",al={"military ward ironforge","ironforge barracks","ironforge warrior district"},it="place"},{q="Where can I train in weapons in Ironforge?",a="Weapon Master Buliwyf Stonehand teaches weapons at Timberline Arms in the Military Ward. There, Alliance fighters train with various armaments.",al={"ironforge weapon master","where is buliwyf stonehand","learn weapons ironforge"},gp=true},{q="What is kept inside the Hall of Arms?",a="The Hall of Arms holds combat instructors and battlemasters. Large bays there house steam tanks and dwarven flying machines.",al={"hall of arms ironforge","what is in hall of arms","ironforge siege engines"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the banners red in this district?",a="Red banners mark the Military Ward as Ironforge's martial district. The city's districts use distinct heraldic colors for navigation and tradition.",al={"military ward colors","red banners ironforge"}},{q="Is the Military Ward dangerous?",a="Not to you or any ally of the Alliance. The Military Ward is one of the most heavily fortified and secure areas in the entire mountain kingdom. It serves as the primary garrison and staging ground for Ironforge's armed forces, packed with seasoned warriors, battlemasters, and active steam tanks. Unless an enemy force breaches the mountain gates, it remains entirely under dwarven martial control.",al={"is military ward safe","military ward danger","danger in military ward"},it="danger",add="f3d6c901"},{q="Why is it called the Military Ward?",a="The district earns its name directly from its role as the command center and headquarters of Ironforge's standing military. Everything here is dedicated to the art of war, from the Hall of Arms and weapon shops to supply outposts and vehicle bays housing siege engines and gyrocopters.",al={"why military ward","how did military ward get its name","military ward name origin"},it="name",add="ba2db6a3"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can train in the Military Ward with warrior trainers and practice on its training dummies. Weapon masters can broaden your battlefield arsenal.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can find beast masters and supplies in the Hall of Arms. Goldfury's Hunting Supplies has munitions and gear for rangers and mountaineers."},kw={"buliwyf stonehand","flying machines","hall of arms","ironforge","military ward","steam tanks","timberline arms"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:great-forge","subzone:commons"},src={"Military Ward"}}
E["subzone:mystic-ward"] = {t="subzone",n="Mystic Ward",z="ironforge",s="Faith and arcane study share Ironforge's Mystic Ward, a quieter quarter of the city. Pale blue banners mark its halls, and priests, paladins, and mages gather beneath stone arches in the Hall of Mysteries.",h="Faith and arcane study share Ironforge's Mystic Ward, a quieter quarter of the city.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary of Faith and Sorcery",b="The Mystic Ward is where Ironforge turns to faith and learning. Pale blue banners mark the quarter between the Commons, the Forlorn Cavern, and the Great Forge. Shops such as The Fighting Wizard and Maeva's Mystical Apparel supply scholars and spellweavers with regalia, scrolls, and alchemical reagents. At the Hall of Mysteries, followers of the Holy Light and arcane practitioners find guidance in wielding unseen powers to defend the Alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Mystic Ward used for?",a="The Mystic Ward brings arcane study and spiritual worship together in Ironforge. Its shops supply spellcasters, while the Hall of Mysteries guides paladins, priests, and mages.",al={"purpose of mystic ward","what happens here","mystic ward role"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the main building in the Mystic Ward?",a="The Hall of Mysteries is the Mystic Ward's main building. Its vaulted chamber houses trainers of holy and arcane spellcasters, with a prominent ornamental pool.",al={"hall of mysteries","big temple","mystic ward building"}},{q="Why are the banners in this ward pale blue?",a="The Mystic Ward's pale blue banners mark its focus on contemplation, wisdom, and magical study. Ironforge's other districts use different heraldry: martial red in the Military Ward and fiery orange at the Great Forge.",al={"blue banners ironforge","why blue flags"}},{q="Where does the Mystic Ward lead?",a="The Mystic Ward lies in Ironforge's northwest. Passages lead south to the Commons, southeast to the Great Forge, and east into the Forlorn Cavern.",al={"mystic ward connections","how to get to mystic ward"},gp=true},{q="What is the Mystic Ward?",a="The Mystic Ward is the northwestern district of Ironforge, dedicated to the study and practice of arcane and holy arts. Far quieter than the bustling Great Forge, it houses magical merchants, reagent shops, and the grand Hall of Mysteries, where practitioners of magic gather to study and train beneath pale blue banners.",al={"mystic ward ironforge","what is mystic ward"},it="place",add="943c276c"},{q="Who lives in or runs the Mystic Ward?",a="The ward serves as a haven for scholars, mages, paladins, and priests within the dwarven capital. Rather than a single governor, it is populated by prominent magic instructors and spiritual leaders based out of the Hall of Mysteries, alongside local arcane purveyors and reagent shopkeepers.",al={"who runs mystic ward","mystic ward leaders","who is in mystic ward"},it="residents",add="fa80dc8d"},{q="Is the Mystic Ward dangerous?",a="Not to visitors and allies of Ironforge. The Mystic Ward is a peaceful, secure quarter of the Alliance capital. While potent magical and divine powers are channeled within its halls, they are kept under tight control by disciplined teachers and scholars.",al={"is mystic ward safe","is mystic ward hostile"},it="danger",add="95712a2a"},{q="Why is it called the Mystic Ward?",a="The district takes its name from its focus on the mystical arts. Unlike the industrial Great Forge or martial Military Ward, this enclave is entirely devoted to the kingdom's arcane and divine pursuits, reagent trade, and magical instruction.",al={"mystic ward name origin","why called mystic ward"},it="name",add="5e418007"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As an Alliance spellweaver, you can find arcane supplies, spell tomes, and advanced study in the Mystic Ward, Khaz Modan's foremost center outside Stormwind's academies.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can find a peaceful haven in the Mystic Ward and its Hall of Mysteries. Dwarven and visiting followers of the Holy Light gather there for prayer, guidance, and communion."},kw={"hall of mysteries","ironforge","longberrys reagents","maevas mystical apparel","mage trainer","mystic ward","priest trainer","the fighting wizard"},rel={"subzone:hall-of-mysteries","zone:ironforge","subzone:commons","subzone:great-forge","subzone:forlorn-cavern","subzone:military-ward"},src={"Mystic Ward"}}
E["subzone:old-ironforge"] = {t="subzone",n="Old Ironforge",z="ironforge",s="Beneath the High Seat, Old Ironforge remains sealed behind guarded gates. Known as the Assembly of Thanes, this ancient chamber lies deep below the royal throne room.",h="Beneath the High Seat, Old Ironforge remains sealed behind guarded gates.",sec={{t="The Assembly of Thanes",b="Old Ironforge lies beneath King Magni Bronzebeard's throne in the High Seat. Its cavernous halls sit deep in the mountain, where winding stone bridges cross pools of lava. Long before the Great Forge and the Commons filled with dwarven commerce, early thanes gathered here to govern the mountain kingdom.",sp=0},{t="A Sealed Chamber",b="The entrance from the throne room remains barred. Ironforge's royal guard watches the thresholds leading down into the old vaults.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Old Ironforge?",a="Old Ironforge, also called the Assembly of Thanes, is an ancient district beneath Ironforge. Its cavernous halls and lava conduits lie below the modern city.",al={"assembly of thanes","what is old ironforge","subterranean ironforge"},it="place"},{q="Can players enter Old Ironforge?",a="The gates in the High Seat are sealed and guarded by the dwarven royal guard, so ordinary citizens cannot enter through the throne room. Dark Iron maps show tunnels converging at a point beneath Ironforge itself.",al={"how to get into old ironforge","is old ironforge open","old ironforge door locked"},gp=true},{q="Where is the entrance located?",a="The entrance lies inside the High Seat, the royal audience chamber where King Magni Bronzebeard sits in Ironforge.",al={"where is old ironforge entrance","old ironforge location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Old Ironforge significant to dwarven history?",a="The Assembly of Thanes was an ancient meeting ground for dwarven leaders and mountain kings, before the upper rings of the modern mountain capital were fully established.",al={"history of old ironforge","why is it called assembly of thanes"},it="history"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Old Ironforge and the Assembly of Thanes preserve a sacred link to their ancestral roots, in the deepest stone foundations of their mountain realm.",["class:Rogue"]="King Magni's guards watch the sealed gates of the High Seat. Anyone caught meddling with the old halls below would face stern dwarven justice."},kw={"aegrim's study","assembly of thanes","high seat","ironforge","magni bronzebeard","old ironforge"},rel={"subzone:high-seat","zone:ironforge","npc:magni-bronzebeard"},src={"Old Ironforge"}}
E["subzone:stonefire-tavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonefire Tavern",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge’s Commons, travelers find the Stonefire Tavern just north of the city gates. Its hearth, dwarven ale, and rooms offer rest to those arriving from across Khaz Modan.",h="In Ironforge’s Commons, travelers find the Stonefire Tavern just north of the city gates.",sec={{t="Heart of the Commons",b="In Ironforge’s Commons, just north of the fortress gates, Innkeeper Firebrew runs Stonefire Tavern with his daughter Gwenna. Weary wayfarers can find meals, local brews, and lodging beneath the mountain.\n\nTravelers come from across the Alliance to rest from Dun Morogh’s mountain snows, trade tales, or gather supplies before exploring the city. The hearth draws them together at the heart of the Commons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Stonefire Tavern located?",a="Stonefire Tavern sits in Ironforge’s Commons, a short walk north of the main city gates.",al={"stonefire tavern location","ironforge inn location","where is stonefire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who operates the Stonefire Tavern?",a="Innkeeper Firebrew runs Stonefire Tavern with help from his daughter, Gwenna Firebrew.",al={"who runs stonefire tavern","stonefire innkeeper","firebrew inn"},it="residents"},{q="Can travelers bind their hearthstones here?",a="Yes. Innkeeper Firebrew lets Alliance travelers make Stonefire Tavern their home base in Ironforge.",al={"set hearth ironforge","ironforge home inn","hearthstone stonefire"},gp=true},{q="What amenities are nearby?",a="A city mailbox stands just outside the entrance. Banks, merchants, and trade supplies are close by in the Commons.",al={"stonefire services","mailbox near stonefire"},gp=true},{q="What is the Stonefire Tavern?",a="The Stonefire Tavern serves as one of the primary gathering places and inns within Ironforge. Situated in the bustling Commons district just north of the city gates, it provides a warm hearth, strong dwarven brew, and a welcoming place to rest for weary travelers, soldiers, and visitors arriving in the mountain capital.",al={"what is stonefire tavern","stonefire tavern ironforge","ironforge stonefire inn"},it="place",add="a8df8501"},{q="Is the Stonefire Tavern dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest. The Stonefire Tavern is a secure, friendly refuge nestled deep inside the fortified heart of Ironforge. Guarded by the dwarven patrol and surrounded by fellow Alliance patrons, the only real hazard you might face here is drinking a mug too many of the Firebrews' potent ale.",al={"is stonefire tavern safe","stonefire tavern danger","threats stonefire tavern"},it="danger",add="3314a531"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf returning from across Khaz Modan, you can stop at Stonefire Tavern for a cold pint of Firebrew ale and local gossip.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you’ll find Stonefire Tavern near Ironforge’s front gates, a gathering place when visiting the dwarven capital."},kw={"commons","dwarven inn","gwenna firebrew","innkeeper firebrew","ironforge","khaz modan","stonefire tavern"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-firebrew","subzone:commons","zone:ironforge"},src={"Stonefire Tavern"}}
E["subzone:thistlefuzz-arcanery"] = {t="subzone",n="Thistlefuzz Arcanery",z="ironforge",s="East of the Great Forge, Thistlefuzz Arcanery draws enchanters and scholars to a prominent gnome-run workshop and academy. Its chambers hum with arcane energy beside the fires of dwarven industry, offering a haven to those who weave magic into metal and parchment.",h="East of the Great Forge, Thistlefuzz Arcanery draws enchanters and scholars to a prominent gnome-run workshop...",sec={{t="Arcane Craft in the Mountain",b="East of the Great Forge, Thistlefuzz Arcanery offers a quieter craft beside the clanging anvils of dwarven smiths. Across its two levels, scholars, practitioners, and apprentices gather to study enchanting and the arcane arts. Dwarves reshape steel with muscle and fire, while the gnomes bind raw arcane energy into weapons, armor, and curious tools. For spellcasters making their way through the mountain stronghold, the Arcanery remains an essential sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Thistlefuzz Arcanery located?",a="Thistlefuzz Arcanery sits east of the Great Forge in central Ironforge. Arcane apparatus and enchanting supplies displayed around its doors mark the way.",al={"arcanery location","where is thistlefuzz","ironforge enchanting shop"},gp=true},{q="What services are offered inside the Arcanery?",a="Inside the Arcanery, enchanting trainers teach apprentices, spellcraft suppliers trade rare reagents, and scholars conduct experiments away from the smithies' physical soot.",al={"what is in thistlefuzz arcanery","trainers in thistlefuzz"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is an arcane workshop situated so close to the Great Forge?",a="The Arcanery's position beside the Great Forge is practical. Newly forged blades, armor plates, and mechanical components can be carried east at once, where they receive protective enchantments and elemental power.",al={"why is it near the forge","arcanery great forge connection"}},{q="What is Thistlefuzz Arcanery?",a="Thistlefuzz Arcanery is an arcane workshop and shop nestled just east of the Great Forge in the heart of Ironforge. While the surrounding city rings with the clash of anvils and molten iron, this quiet establishment caters to practitioners of the mystic arts, offering training and supplies for aspiring enchanters.",al={"thistlefuzz arcanery","what is thistlefuzz arcanery","ironforge arcanery"},it="place",add="b65c06f3"},{q="Is Thistlefuzz Arcanery dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest, provided you are welcome in Ironforge. The Arcanery is a peaceful commercial shop protected by the city guards and the Ironforge authorities. Unless you are hostile to the Alliance, you can browse its shelves and converse with its practitioners without fear of harm.",al={"is thistlefuzz dangerous","thistlefuzz arcanery danger"},it="danger",add="ddf479e1"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes residing in Ironforge, Thistlefuzz Arcanery is a comfortable reminder of their love for arcane theory, technical study, and delicate experimentation amid a city dominated by heavy dwarven iron.",["class:Mage"]="For visiting mages, the Arcanery offers familiar reagents, quiet corners for theory, and kindred spellcasters among the otherwise martial, weapon-focused halls of the dwarf capital."},kw={"arcane","enchanter","enchanting","gnome","great forge","ironforge","thistlefuzz arcanery"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:great-forge"},src={"Thistlefuzz Arcanery"}}
E["subzone:tinker-town"] = {t="subzone",n="Tinker Town",z="ironforge",s="Tinker Town is where gnomes make their home in exile beneath Ironforge. Since Gnomeregan fell, it has been the seat of High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque’s government and the Ironforge end of the Deeprun Tram.",h="Tinker Town is where gnomes make their home in exile beneath Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Home in Exile",b="Tinker Town shelters the gnomes who fled Gnomeregan. Troggs overran their high-tech city, so Ironforge’s dwarves opened their gates. They gave the refugees a cavern once used by dwarves, where the Deeprun Tram entrance already stood. High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his council lead the gnomes from here.\n\nAround a massive spherical contraption, the gnomes have rebuilt a semblance of their civilization. Gears whir, alchemy is tested, and gadgets take shape in the cramped district. Though guests in a stone city, the gnomes remain determined to reclaim their subterranean homeland.",sp=0},{t="Subway and Secrets",b="Tinker Town holds the Ironforge entrance to the Deeprun Tram. The engineering wonder carries travelers swiftly between the dwarven capital and Stormwind, joining the two cities.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are gnomes living in Ironforge instead of their own city?",a="Gnomeregan fell when primitive troggs invaded, and the gnomes evacuated. They fought the troggs alone rather than burdening the Alliance during the Third War. King Magni Bronzebeard offered Ironforge as a sanctuary, where High Tinker Mekkatorque established a temporary capital in exile.",al={"why are gnomes here","why do gnomes live in ironforge","gnome refugees ironforge"},it="history"},{q="What is the Deeprun Tram entrance doing here?",a="The Deeprun Tram connects Ironforge directly to Stormwind City. Gnomes and dwarves built it together, and its Ironforge terminus opens into Tinker Town. The tram links the two Alliance capitals with swift travel.",al={"where does the tram go","tram in tinkertown","tinkertown portal"}},{q="What is Tinker Town?",a="Tinker Town is the gnomish quarter of Ironforge, carved out around the grand entrance to the Deeprun Tram. After the fall of Gnomeregan, the Ironforge dwarves welcomed their displaced allies into the mountain, granting them this district to re-establish their community, workshops, and engineering laboratories.",al={"what is tinker town","tinker town info","gnome district ironforge"},it="place",add="d4e07867"},{q="Who rules Tinker Town?",a="Tinker Town serves as the seat of the gnomish government-in-exile, led by High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his council of senior advisers. Beneath his leadership, the district bustles with displaced gnomes, master engineers, alchemists, and inventors trying to forge a new future.",al={"who leads tinker town","tinker town leader","who is in charge of tinker town"},it="residents",add="37905e65"},{q="Is Tinker Town dangerous?",a="Tinker Town is entirely safe from external enemies, resting deep within the fortified heart of Ironforge. However, with volatile alchemical concoctions, whirring cogwheels, and experimental explosives packed into crowded workshops, minor mechanical mishaps and fiery accidents are never entirely out of the question.",al={"tinker town safe","is tinker town safe","tinker town threats"},it="danger",add="70a740c2"},{q="Why is it called Tinker Town?",a="The district takes its name from the gnomish passion for tinkering, invention, and mechanical tinkering, as well as the title of their elected leader, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque. It serves as a bustling center for tinkerers, engineers, and inventors working within the dwarven capital.",al={"why is it called tinker town","tinker town name origin","where did tinker town get its name"},it="name",add="3f3e824e"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Tinker Town is the heart of your people in exile. Amid clanking prototypes and fellow survivors, High Tinker Mekkatorque directs efforts to reclaim Gnomeregan.",["profession:Engineering"]="For an engineer, Tinker Town is an essential stop in Ironforge. Specialized trainers, gadget vendors, parts, and the Deeprun Tram are all here."},kw={"deeprun tram","engineering","gnomeregan","ironforge","mekkatorque","tinker town","tinkertown"},rel={"zone:ironforge","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:deeprun-tram","topic:gnome","topic:trogg"},src={"Tinker Town"}}
E["subzone:vault-of-ironforge"] = {t="subzone",n="Vault of Ironforge",z="ironforge",s="In Ironforge's Commons, citizens and Alliance travelers entrust their wealth to the Vault. Dinita and the Stonemantle family oversee its work.",h="In Ironforge's Commons, citizens and Alliance travelers entrust their wealth to the Vault.",sec={{t="Heart of Dwarven Commerce",b="Travelers, soldiers, and merchants bring coin, relics, and provisions to the Vault for safekeeping. City guards and tellers watch the deposits, keeping the wealth of citizens and Alliance visitors secure within the mountain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Vault of Ironforge used for?",a="The Vault keeps gold, gear, and prized possessions safe within the mountain. Citizens and Alliance travelers rely on it as Ironforge's central bank and treasure storehouse.",al={"vault purpose","ironforge bank","what is this place"},it="purpose"},{q="Who operates the bank?",a="Dinita and members of the Stonemantle family operate the bank. They manage deposits, transactions, and storage for visitors.",al={"bankers","who runs the vault","stonemantle family"},it="residents"},{q="Where is the Vault located?",a="The Vault is in Ironforge's Commons, directly across from the Auction House.",al={"vault location","where is ironforge bank","how to find vault"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Vault of Ironforge?",a="The Vault of Ironforge serves as the central bank and primary treasure repository for the dwarven capital. Situated directly across from the bustling Auction House in the Commons, it provides secure storage for travelers, merchants, and champions of the Alliance seeking a trustworthy haven for their hard-earned valuables.",al={"what is vault of ironforge","ironforge bank lore","vault of ironforge"},it="place",add="84f84a05"},{q="Is the Vault of Ironforge dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest for Alliance travelers. Located safely in the heart of the city's Commons district, the Vault is heavily guarded and protected by the full might of Ironforge's city watch. Unless hostile Horde forces manage an audacious raid into the mountain itself, it remains one of the safest establishments in the realm.",al={"is vault of ironforge safe","ironforge bank danger","vault safe"},it="danger",add="45fc2a88"},{q="Why is it called the Vault of Ironforge?",a="It takes its name from its function and fortress-like construction. Built as the grand treasury of the city, this cavernous hall is reinforced to safeguard wealth and relics beneath the mountain's solid stone, making it the definitive vault of the dwarven nation.",al={"why is it called the vault","vault of ironforge name origin","name vault of ironforge"},it="name",add="ef86fb6b"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can take pride in the Vault's reputation for safeguarding dwarven wealth within the mountain.",["faction:Alliance"]="Across from Ironforge's Auction House, the Vault helps Alliance adventurers keep their gold and supplies close at hand."},kw={"dinita","ironforge","ironforge bank","stonemantle","the commons","vault of ironforge"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:commons","topic:alliance"},src={"Vault of Ironforge"}}
E["zone:ironforge"] = {t="city",n="Ironforge",z="ironforge",s="Ironforge is carved into the heart of a mountain, in the snows of Dun Morogh. It is the ancient capital of the Bronzebeard dwarves, and one of the Alliance's strongest bulwarks. At its center burns the Great Forge. Here King Magni Bronzebeard rules, and now his halls also shelter the gnomes who lost Gnomeregan.",h="Ironforge is carved into the heart of a mountain, in the snows of Dun Morogh.",sec={{t="A City of Stone and Fire",b="Twenty-five centuries ago, the first dwarves awoke in Uldaman. Westward they journeyed, into the jagged peaks of Dun Morogh, and delved into the tallest mountain. There they raised a shrine to their maker, the titan Khaz'goroth, and beside it the Great Forge. And ever since, the city has grown outward in rings around that fiery hearth.\n\nNo city above the ground is like it. Ironforge lies wholly beneath stone, warmed by roaring hearths and by rivers of molten rock. Its fortified gates and deep halls have held through centuries of war.",sp=0},{t="The War of the Three Hammers",b="For generations, three dwarven clans shared the mountain. The Bronzebeards lived beside the Wildhammers and the Dark Irons. When High King Modimus Anvilmar died, a bitter civil war broke out for rule of Ironforge. The Bronzebeards won it, and drove their rivals out.\n\nThen Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan led the Dark Irons back for vengeance. His siege reached the very heart of Ironforge, before the Bronzebeards threw it back. In the south, by mischance, Thaurissan then summoned Ragnaros the Firelord. The Firelord's coming shattered the Redridge Mountains, and doomed Thaurissan's own host. Ever since, the Bronzebeards have held Ironforge unchallenged.",sp=0},{t="Honor to the Alliance",b="In the Second War, the Bleeding Hollow clan overran much of Khaz Modan. But Ironforge held firm behind its sealed gates, until the Alliance of Lordaeron broke the siege. For that debt of honor, King Magni Bronzebeard pledged Ironforge to the Alliance forever. He stood by it even when Gilneas and Quel'Thalas walked away.",sp=0},{t="A Haven for Exiles",b="In the Third War, Magni mourned his brother Muradin, lost in Northrend. When Gnomeregan fell, the king opened his gates to thousands of gnome refugees. Under High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, they carved out Tinker Town within the stone city. And the Deeprun Tram now runs beneath the earth, straight to Stormwind. So Ironforge has become a crossroads of dwarven steel and gnomish invention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules Ironforge?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard rules Ironforge and the kingdom of Khaz Modan from the High Seat. A skilled warrior and master blacksmith, he has governed his people through the Second and Third Wars and remains a deeply loyal pillar of the Alliance. Ironforge remains one of the Alliance's fiercest bulwarks.",al={"ironforge king","ruler of ironforge","who is the dwarf king"},it="leader"},{q="Why are there so many gnomes in Ironforge?",a="When the nearby gnomish capital of Gnomeregan fell to a sudden trogg invasion and a disastrous radiation accident, the surviving gnomes fled into Dun Morogh. King Magni welcomed them into Ironforge, granting them an entire quarter of the city now known as Tinker Town.",al={"gnomes in ironforge","why are gnomes here","tinker town gnomes"},it="people"},{q="What is the Great Forge?",a="The Great Forge is the fiery industrial heart of the city, fed by underground waterfalls of molten magma. It surrounds the Great Anvil, where dwarven weaponsmiths craft legendary arms and armor.",al={"great forge","ironforge anvil","center of ironforge"},it="place"},{q="How do you travel between Ironforge and Stormwind?",a="Ironforge is connected directly to Stormwind City by the Deeprun Tram, an extraordinary subterranean railway built by gnomish engineering that cuts straight through the mountain bedrock of the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"ironforge to stormwind","deeprun tram","train to stormwind"},gp=true},{q="Has Ironforge ever fallen to an enemy army?",a="Ironforge has never fallen to an outside invader. Kilrogg Deadeye's Bleeding Hollow clan laid siege to it for months during the Second War, and the Dark Irons fought into the city during the War of the Three Hammers, but the gates and defenders held.",al={"has ironforge been conquered","did ironforge fall","ironforge siege"},it="history"},{q="Where did the other dwarf clans go?",a="After the War of the Three Hammers, the defeated Wildhammer clan relocated north into the Wetlands and the Hinterlands, while the hostile Dark Iron clan settled within the Redridge and Blackrock regions under the thrall of the Firelord.",al={"where are wildhammers","where are dark irons","three hammer clans"},it="ties"},{q="What is Ironforge?",a="Ironforge is the ancestral capital city of the dwarves and one of the oldest settlements on Azeroth. Carved deep beneath the stone of Ironforge Mountain in snowy Dun Morogh, it stands as the heart of the dwarven Kingdom of Khaz Modan and a cornerstone of the Alliance. It is a fortified underground metropolis arranged in concentric rings of cavernous chambers, roaring forges, and lively stone halls bustling with craftsmen, explorers, and soldiers.",al={"ironforge city overview","what kind of place is ironforge","about ironforge"},it="place",add="0779b12a",nx={8,9}},{q="Who built Ironforge inside the mountain?",a="Thousands of years ago, early dwarven ancestors emerged from the titan ruins of Uldaman and journeyed west into Dun Morogh. Discovering the region's tallest mountain, they carved their home deep into its bedrock, constructing an altar to the titan Khaz'goroth and igniting the Great Forge around which the underground city grew.",al={"who built ironforge","how was ironforge created","who carved ironforge"},it="origin",add="9f789b9e"},{q="Why is there lava running through the middle of Ironforge?",a="The city was deliberately delved around natural subterranean torrents and waterfalls of molten rock. Dwarven metalworkers harnessed this boundless geothermal heat to power the Great Forge, fueling foundries, smelters, and smithies that allow Ironforge's armorers and weaponsmiths to craft world-renowned arms and armor without ever letting the fires die.",al={"why is there lava in ironforge","lava in the great forge","why magma in ironforge"},it="place",add="1ca57bea"},{q="What happened at Ironforge throughout its history?",a="Long after its founding, civil war broke out when High King Modimus Anvilmar died. The Bronzebeard clan drove out the rival Wildhammer and Dark Iron clans, subsequently defending the city from a brutal Dark Iron invasion. Centuries later during the Second War, the orcish Horde besieged Ironforge, but the mountain fortress held firm until the Alliance arrived to break the siege. Today, it remains an unbroken bastion.",al={"ironforge history","history of ironforge","what happened in ironforge history"},it="history",add="af5eaa17"},{q="Who lives in Ironforge?",a="Ironforge is home primarily to the Bronzebeard dwarves who govern Khaz Modan. However, the catastrophic fall of Gnomeregan brought a large population of gnomish refugees into the city, establishing their own district in Tinker Town under High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque. Human ambassadors, traveling merchants, and Alliance adventurers of all stripes regularly walk its stone thoroughfares.",al={"who lives in ironforge","ironforge population","races in ironforge"},it="residents",add="879099cb"},{q="Is Ironforge dangerous?",a="Within its massive sealed gates, Ironforge is considered one of the safest and most secure bastions in the world. Guards patrol every ring, and its mountain walls have repelled every besieging army. However, unwary visitors can fall into the blistering molten slag pits around the Great Forge, and shadowy conspirators are known to lurk in secluded corners.",al={"is ironforge safe","threats in ironforge","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="30458af2"},{q="Why is the city called Ironforge?",a="The city took its name from the Great Forge, the colossal heart of industry and craft that dwarven settlers built upon first delving into the mountain peak. Both the surrounding cavern city and the mountain itself were named in honor of that towering, eternal foundry.",al={"ironforge name origin","why called ironforge","where did ironforge get its name"},it="name",add="44f103f9"},{q="Who is in charge of Ironforge?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard, Thane of Ironforge and chieftain of the Bronzebeard clan, rules the kingdom from the High Seat. A veteran commander of the Second and Third Wars, Magni directs the dwarven nation and coordinates closely with Alliance leaders to secure Khaz Modan and the surrounding regions.",al={"ironforge leader","who leads ironforge","who is in charge"},it="in_charge",add="8722c25e",nx={15,16}},{q="Is King Magni a good king?",a="Magni is widely revered by his people as a steadfast, courageous, and capable monarch who protected his kingdom through the Horde's siege and the Scourge's onslaught. Though he personally wrestles with grief over his missing brother Muradin and tensions with his daughter Moira, he is a dedicated ruler fiercely committed to his folk and his allies.",al={"is magni bronzebeard a good king","how is king magni regarded","is magni well liked"},it="leader",add="f1f3f31b"},{q="Does King Magni answer to Stormwind?",a="No. Ironforge is a completely sovereign kingdom. King Magni treats Stormwind as an equal and valued partner within the Alliance, tied by ancient honor and mutual defense pacts. The dwarves helped rebuild Stormwind after the Second War, and the Deeprun Tram connects their capitals, but Magni answers only to his mountain throne.",al={"does magni answer to stormwind","is ironforge under stormwind","ironforge stormwind relationship"},it="ties",add="48b1fbac"},{q="Why is there a gnomish district inside Ironforge?",a="When the underground gnome capital of Gnomeregan fell to a sudden trogg invasion and toxic irradiation, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque led the surviving survivors to Ironforge. King Magni offered unconditional sanctuary to his longstanding neighbors, setting aside a district that became Tinker Town to shelter their court in exile.",al={"why do gnomes live in ironforge","why is tinker town here","gnomes in ironforge history"},it="history",add="df9a6ce3",nx={18,19}},{q="What happened to Gnomeregan?",a="Vicious subterranean primitives called troggs erupted into Gnomeregan from deep fissures. Desperate to purge the invaders, the gnomes vented radioactive waste into the lower levels. The radiation failed to wipe out the troggs and instead irradiated the city, sickening many citizens and forcing the survivors to flee.",al={"what happened at gnomeregan","fall of gnomeregan","why did gnomeregan fall"},it="history",add="f6bc736b"},{q="Are the gnomes planning to reclaim Gnomeregan?",a="Yes. Tinker Town serves as the staging ground for High Tinker Mekkatorque and his engineers as they scheme, invent, and build machines to reclaim their irradiated home. Gnomish commandos and Alliance volunteers routinely launch strikes into the city's corridors to clear troggs and eliminate traitorous threats.",al={"will gnomes take back gnomeregan","are gnomes retaking gnomeregan","gnomeregan retaking plans"},it="wants",add="cda22453"},{q="How did I end up in Ironforge?",a="If you are a dwarf or gnome, you likely marched up the great stone ramparts from Dun Morogh after proving yourself in Coldridge Valley and Kharanos, sent to present yourself to the city's leadership. If you hail from farther away, you likely arrived via the Deeprun Tram straight from the heart of Stormwind, or flew directly into the Great Forge on the back of a gryphon to trade, study, or answer King Magni's call to arms.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to ironforge","how did i reach ironforge"},it="arrival",add="c12e1e98"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Ironforge?",a="Ironforge serves as the beating heart of trade, training, and military planning for the Alliance in Khaz Modan. Here you can master your profession around the roaring fires of the Great Forge, seek advanced training in your class, or consult the Explorers' League in the Hall of Explorers. High Tinker Mekkatorque coordinates gnome resistance from Tinker Town, while King Magni Bronzebeard oversees the realm's defense against rising threats across the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"what should i do in ironforge","why am i here","what is my goal here"},it="purpose",add="fb631935"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Ironforge is the ancestral home of your kin. Its halls honor your people's resilience, their mastery of stone and the sacred lineage that traces back to the titans.",["race:Gnome"]="Since the disaster that consumed Gnomeregan, Tinker Town has served as your temporary home and command center as High Tinker Mekkatorque plots the liberation of your city.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The Great Forge is revered across Azeroth as the premier center of metalworking, housing the Great Anvil where master smiths and King Magni himself shape metal into legend.",["faction:Alliance"]="Linked to Stormwind by the Deeprun Tram, Ironforge is the Alliance's northern anchor and one of its most reliable military fortresses."},kw={"bronzebeard","deeprun tram","dun morogh","great forge","high seat","ironforge","khaz modan","magni bronzebeard","tinker town"},rel={"npc:magni-bronzebeard","subzone:great-forge","subzone:tinker-town","subzone:deeprun-tram","subzone:high-seat","zone:dunmorogh","npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","topic:bronzebeard-clan"},src={"Ironforge"}}
